      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The 128K starts here (and on a reset): interrupts off, a delay of $692B rounds, then\nRAM_TEST.","comment":"No interrupts during start-up"},
        "1": {"comment":"$692B rounds"},
        "4": {"synopsis":"The delay.","comment":"One round"},
        "5": {"comment":"BC down to 0?"},
        "9": {"comment":"To the RAM test"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: ROM 1's RST $10 (CALL_ROM1), which prints A through the current channel."},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: ROM 1's RST $18 (CALL_ROM1): the character at CH_ADD."},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: ROM 1's RST $20 (CALL_ROM1): the next character at CH_ADD."},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 1 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word:\n1. HL = that address; $5B5A = the place after the word, the return point.\n2. CALL_ROM1_GO stacks the RAM routine at $5B14 (ROM1_RETURN's copy) as the routine's\n   return, then the address, and jumps to $5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy), whose RET enters ROM 1\n   there with HL as it was.\n3. When the routine returns, $5B14 swaps back to this ROM and returns to $5B5A.\nKeeps every register for the routine.","comment":"HL = the place of the word; HL kept on the stack"},
        "41": {"comment":"AF kept"},
        "42": {"comment":"The word's low byte"},
        "45": {"comment":"$5B5A = past the word: the return point"},
        "49": {"comment":"HL = the word"},
        "52": {"comment":"Into ROM 1"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1): runs ROM 1's interrupt routine at $0038: the stack gets INT_RETURN,\n$5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy, to come back) and $0038, then $5B00 swaps the ROMs and returns into\nROM 1's $0038. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "57": {"comment":"Back here at the end"},
        "61": {"comment":"Back to this ROM before that"},
        "65": {"comment":"ROM 1's interrupt routine"},
        "69": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs and go"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"HL back, and return from the interrupt."},
        "74": {"synopsis":"Paging back to RAM bank 0, ROM 0 and the normal screen ($5B5C = 0), ERR_NR = $FF, then on at\n$0321. Vector $010C.","comment":"The paging port"},
        "77": {"comment":"Paging byte 0"},
        "81": {"comment":"$5B5C, the paging byte, kept in step"},
        "85": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "89": {"comment":"AFTER_RUN"},
        "92": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM1's second half: the stack gets ROM1_RETURN's copy ($5B14) and the routine's address\n(from $5B58), HL as it was, then SWAP_ROM's copy at $5B00.","comment":"$5B58 = the routine"},
        "95": {"comment":"$5B14 under the caller's HL"},
        "100": {"comment":"The routine's address on top, HL back"},
        "104": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs and go"},
        "107": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5B00 at start-up and run from there (88 bytes, to $00C2): flips the ROM (bit 4 of\nthe paging byte at $5B5C, written to port $7FFD with interrupts off) and returns; a RET made\nwith an address on the stack thus continues in the other ROM. Keeps every register.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "112": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "115": {"comment":"The other ROM"},
        "121": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "127": {"synopsis":"At $5B14: where a ROM 1 routine called by CALL_ROM1 returns to: the ROMs swapped back, then\na return to $5B5A, past the RST's word.","comment":"Back to this ROM ($5B00)"},
        "131": {"comment":"The return point under HL"},
        "135": {"comment":"On at the return point"},
        "136": {"synopsis":"At $5B1D: where ROM 1's error handling returns to (start-up and the editor put $5B1D under\nERR_SP): ROM 0 paged in, then the handler at the address in $5B8B (GO_HANDLER).","comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "137": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "140": {"comment":"Bit 4 clear: ROM 0"},
        "145": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "151": {"comment":"On through GO_HANDLER"},
        "154": {"synopsis":"At $5B2F: channel P's input routine (CHANS_128_INIT): ROM 0's $06D8 through CALL_ROM0.","comment":"ROM 0's RS232_IN"},
        "159": {"synopsis":"At $5B34: channel P's output routine: ROM 0's $07CA through CALL_ROM0.","comment":"ROM 0's RS232_PRINT"},
        "162": {"synopsis":"At $5B37: runs the routine at HL in ROM 0 for a caller in ROM 1: the paging byte kept on the\nstack, ROM 0 paged in with interrupts off, then on at $05E6 in ROM 0; CALL_ROM0_BACK\nrestores the paging. A is passed through the alternate AF.","comment":"A kept in the alternate AF"},
        "163": {"comment":"The paging port"},
        "166": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "169": {"comment":"The paging byte kept"},
        "170": {"comment":"ROM 0"},
        "173": {"comment":"Kept in step"},
        "178": {"comment":"ROM0_CALLED, now in ROM 0"},
        "181": {"synopsis":"At $5B4A: the paging byte back from the stack and written, interrupts on; return with A from\nthe alternate AF.","comment":"The result's AF kept in the alternate set"},
        "182": {"comment":"The old paging byte"},
        "193": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "195": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the address in $5B8B: the editor's current handler (start-up and the main loop set\nit).","comment":"HL = the handler"},
        "199": {"synopsis":"Tests the eight RAM banks, 7 down to 0: each paged in at $C000 (port $7FFD), each byte\nwritten $FF and $00 and read back, then the bank cleared. A failure stops at RAM_FAULT.","comment":"Eight banks"},
        "201": {"synopsis":"One bank.","comment":"A = the bank counter"},
        "202": {"comment":"The counter kept in BC'"},
        "204": {"comment":"Bank B - 1 at $C000"},
        "209": {"comment":"The bank's 16K: HL, DE and BC for the clearing LDIR"},
        "218": {"comment":"$FF written and read back"},
        "222": {"comment":"Not read back: RAM_FAULT"},
        "224": {"comment":"$00 likewise"},
        "227": {"comment":"Not read back: RAM_FAULT"},
        "229": {"comment":"The rest cleared"},
        "231": {"comment":"The counter back"},
        "232": {"comment":"The next bank down"},
        "234": {"comment":"$5B88 = 0"},
        "237": {"comment":"The AY chip: C = $FD, D = $FF (register port $FFFD), E = $BF (data port $BFFD)"},
        "243": {"comment":"Register select"},
        "244": {"comment":"Register 14, the I/O port"},
        "248": {"comment":"Data port"},
        "249": {"comment":"= $FF"},
        "253": {"comment":"On with the setup"},
        "256": {"synopsis":"Jumps into this ROM at fixed addresses for code elsewhere: ROM 1's hooks use $010F, $0112\nand $0115 (HOOK_REPORT, HOOK_STMT_JUMP, HOOK_STMT_NEXT in sp128-1.rom.dis), and $010C is\nRESET_TO_128; the others go to $17AF, $1838, $1ECF, $1F04, $03A2, $182A, $18A8, $012D,\n$0A05, $11A3, $06D8, $07CA, $08A3 and $08F0.","comment":"CHECK_LINE"},
        "259": {"comment":"RUN_EDIT_LINE"},
        "262": {"comment":"BANK7_PUT"},
        "265": {"comment":"BANK7_GET"},
        "268": {"comment":"RESET_TO_128"},
        "271": {"comment":"REPORT_LINE (ROM 1's HOOK_REPORT)"},
        "274": {"comment":"STMT_JUMP (ROM 1's HOOK_STMT_JUMP)"},
        "277": {"comment":"STMT_NEXT (ROM 1's HOOK_STMT_NEXT)"},
        "280": {"comment":"CALL_3B01"},
        "283": {"comment":"PLAY_SETUP"},
        "286": {"comment":"MIDI_OUT"},
        "289": {"comment":"RS232_IN"},
        "292": {"comment":"RS232_PRINT"},
        "295": {"comment":"RS232_OUT"},
        "298": {"comment":"COPY_128"},
        "301": {"synopsis":"Vector $0118: ROM 1's $3B01 (CALL_ROM1).","comment":"ROM 1's KP_TABLE_MORE"},
        "305": {"synopsis":"A bank failed the RAM test: the border shows the bank counter B (the bank + 1, three bits:\nbank 7 gives 0) and the machine stops there.","comment":"B = the bank counter: the bank + 1"},
        "307": {"comment":"Border = the bank counter"},
        "309": {"synopsis":"Forever."},
        "311": {"synopsis":"After the RAM test:\n1. AY register 7 = $FF; SWAP_ROM and the routines after it copied to $5B00-$5B57; $5B5D =\n   $CF; the stack at $5BFF.\n2. Bank 7 (SELECT_BANK 4): $5B83 = $EBEC, with three bytes there set; $5B85 = $2BEC, $5B87 =\n   1; then bank 0 (SELECT_BANK 5).\n3. As a 48K start: P_RAMT = $FFFF, the UDGs copied below it from ROM 1's letters A-U ($3EAF\n   down, ROM 1's $1661), UDG, RASP/PIP, RAMTOP, CHARS = $3C00, the stack below RAMTOP, IM 1,\n   IY = $5C3A; FLAGS bit 4 set (128 BASIC); interrupts on.\n4. The 128K's own variables: $5B5F = $000B, $5B61, $5B63, $5B65 = 0, $FF24 = $EC00, $5B64 =\n   $50, $5B94 and $5B96 = 10.\n5. CHANS from CHANS_128_INIT, the program, variable and edit-line pointers as in the 48K,\n   the colours ($38), border 7, REPDEL 35 and REPPER 5, KSTATE free, STRMS from STRMS_INIT,\n   ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2.\n6. CLS (ROM 1's CLS_CMD), ROM 1's test picture when BREAK is held ($3C04, TEST_SCREEN),\n   COPYRIGHT_MSG printed, then bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), EDITOR_RESET, and the\n   main menu (MAIN_MENU).","comment":"Register select: register 7, the mixer"},
        "317": {"comment":"AY register 7 = $FF"},
        "321": {"comment":"The RAM routines to $5B00"},
        "332": {"comment":"$5B5D = $CF"},
        "337": {"comment":"The stack in the 128K's variables page"},
        "340": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "342": {"comment":"SELECT_BANK"},
        "345": {"comment":"IX = $EBEC: $5B83"},
        "353": {"comment":"Bytes 10-12 there: 0, $C0, 0"},
        "365": {"comment":"$5B85 = $2BEC, $5B87 = 1"},
        "376": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "381": {"comment":"P_RAMT = $FFFF"},
        "387": {"comment":"The UDGs: $A8 bytes from $3EAF down (ROM 1's LDDR at $1661)"},
        "394": {"comment":"The copy (ROM 1's LDDR in MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "398": {"comment":"UDG = the first"},
        "403": {"comment":"RASP/PIP = $40, 0"},
        "410": {"comment":"RAMTOP = the byte below"},
        "413": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00","synopsis":"START_SETUP from CHARS on: where NEW_CMD restarts (interrupts off), keeping P_RAMT, the UDGs\nand RAMTOP's place."},
        "419": {"comment":"The machine stack from RAMTOP down"},
        "424": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "426": {"comment":"IY at ERR_NR, for the system variables"},
        "430": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 set: 128 BASIC"},
        "435": {"comment":"$5B5F = $000B"},
        "441": {"comment":"$5B61, $5B63, $5B65 = 0: no RS232 byte kept, column 0"},
        "451": {"comment":"$FF24 = $EC00"},
        "457": {"comment":"$5B64 = $50"},
        "462": {"comment":"$5B94 = $5B96 = 10"},
        "471": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6"},
        "477": {"comment":"The 21 bytes of CHANS_128_INIT"},
        "487": {"comment":"DATADD = the $80 at the end"},
        "491": {"comment":"PROG, VARS"},
        "498": {"comment":"The variables' end marker"},
        "501": {"comment":"E_LINE: an empty edit line"},
        "507": {"comment":"Its $80 end marker"},
        "510": {"comment":"WORKSP, STKBOT, STKEND"},
        "519": {"comment":"ATTR_P, ATTR_T, BORDCR = $38"},
        "530": {"comment":"$EC13 = 0 (bank 7)"},
        "534": {"comment":"Border 7"},
        "538": {"comment":"REPDEL 35, REPPER 5"},
        "544": {"comment":"KSTATE: both sets free"},
        "550": {"comment":"STRMS from STRMS_INIT"},
        "561": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 cleared"},
        "565": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF"},
        "569": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "573": {"comment":"CLS (ROM 1)"},
        "576": {"comment":"ROM 1's test picture, with BREAK held"},
        "579": {"comment":"The copyright message"},
        "582": {"comment":"PRINT_BIT7_TEXT"},
        "585": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2 again"},
        "589": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "593": {"comment":"$5B81 = $5BFF: the other stack"},
        "599": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "602": {"comment":"$EC11 = $EC0F = $38"},
        "610": {"comment":"EDITOR_RESET"},
        "613": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "616": {"comment":"The main menu"},
        "619": {"synopsis":"What the 128 BASIC editor runs when a line is entered (from $1B11, $1B28, $2CC9): it checks\nthe line and, through ENTER_HANDLER, stores or runs it:\n1. $5B66 bit 0 set, ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2; ERR_SP points at ERROR_RETURN's copy ($5B1D)\n   and $5B8B at ENTER_HANDLER, so a report while checking ends there.\n2. CH_ADD to the line's first character (CH_ADD_TO_LINE). A keyword from $A5 to $C3 other\n   than $AC and $AD, '(', '-', '+', a letter or '.' (KEYWORD_TEST, LETTER_TEST) goes on at\n   CALC_LINE.\n3. Otherwise CHECK_LINE ($17AF), unless $EC0E (bank 7) is 4, the Calculator (0 in 128\n   BASIC): there only a line starting with LET goes on (LET_TEST); anything else does\n   nothing.\nObserved: entering print x in 128 BASIC gave 2 Variable not found, 0:1; 10 print 1 was\nstored and listed as 10 PRINT 1."},
        "622": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 0 set"},
        "624": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF"},
        "628": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "632": {"comment":"A report returns to ERROR_RETURN's copy"},
        "636": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "640": {"comment":"$5B8B = ENTER_HANDLER"},
        "646": {"comment":"The line's first character"},
        "649": {"comment":"A keyword?"},
        "655": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "660": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "665": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "670": {"comment":"A letter or '.'?"},
        "676": {"comment":"Bank 7, for the editor's mode"},
        "679": {"comment":"A = $EC0E"},
        "682": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "685": {"comment":"Not 4: $17AF"},
        "690": {"comment":"$F1 first?"},
        "693": {"comment":"LET with one statement: CHECK_LINE"},
        "696": {"comment":"Nothing: the ERROR_RETURN address dropped"},
        "698": {"synopsis":"Where checking a line ends (GO_HANDLER): with a report pending (ERR_NR bit 7 clear) back to\nthe editor; with none, a line with a number is stored (STORE_LINE) and any other line is\nrun:\n1. EDIT_LINE_NO (ROM 1) reads its number; an empty line does nothing.\n2. The lower screen cleared when FLAGS2 bit 0 asks for it ($21EF) and when TV_FLAG bit 6 is\n   clear (ROM 1's CLS_LOWER); with $EC0D bit 6 clear and $EC0E = 0, $3881.\n3. TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT from S_POSN's line, FLAGS bit 7 set (running), NSPPC = 1;\n   $3E00 stacked as the end marker, ERROR_RETURN's copy above it under ERR_SP, $5B8B =\n   AFTER_RUN; then RUN_EDIT_LINE runs the line.","comment":"A report pending?"},
        "704": {"comment":"Yes: back"},
        "705": {"synopsis":"No report: CH_ADD to the line's start, its number read.","comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE, the line's start"},
        "711": {"comment":"BC = the line's number (ROM 1's EDIT_LINE_NO)"},
        "716": {"comment":"A number: store the line"},
        "719": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "720": {"comment":"An empty line: done"},
        "723": {"comment":"The lower screen cleared if asked ($21EF)"},
        "726": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 set?"},
        "732": {"comment":"No: ROM 1's CLS_LOWER"},
        "735": {"synopsis":"The line is run: TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; in bank 7, $3881 when $EC0D bit 6 is clear and $EC0E\nis 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "739": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "742": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6?"},
        "750": {"comment":"$EC0E = 0?"},
        "753": {"comment":"Then $3881"},
        "756": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; then as RUN_EDIT_LINE expects it: TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT, FLAGS bit 7, NSPPC\n= 1, the stack and ERR_SP, the handler.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "759": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "764": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 25 - S_POSN's line"},
        "772": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "776": {"comment":"NSPPC = 1"},
        "780": {"comment":"$3E00: the end marker"},
        "784": {"comment":"ERROR_RETURN's copy above it"},
        "788": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "792": {"comment":"$5B8B = AFTER_RUN"},
        "798": {"comment":"Run the line"},
        "801": {"synopsis":"Where a run ends, with or without a report (GO_HANDLER, RESET_TO_128 and others): the report\nprinted and the editor resumed:\n1. The machine stack from RAMTOP, $5B81 = $5BFF; a HALT; FLAGS bit 5 cleared; with $5B66 bit\n   2 set, $1D56 on the entry 20 bytes past $5B83 (bank 7).\n2. A = ERR_NR + 1, the report's code. FLAGX, X_PTR's high byte and DEFADD cleared, STRMS for\n   stream 0 = 1; ROM 1's CLEAR_EDIT_WS and CLS_LOWER; TV_FLAG bit 5 set.\n3. The code printed (PRINT_A_DIGIT): 0-9 as a digit, 10-28 as A-S, 29 up as a lowercase\n   letter from a (the 128K's own reports); a space; the message: ROM 1's REPORT_MESSAGES\n   (PRINT_MESSAGE) below 29, REPORT_128_TABLE otherwise (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT); then REPORT_LINE.\nObserved: play \"x\" gave k Invalid note name, 0:1.","comment":"The machine stack: from RAMTOP"},
        "806": {"comment":"The other stack: from $5BFF"},
        "812": {"comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "813": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5: no key"},
        "817": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 2?"},
        "824": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "827": {"comment":"IX = the entry 20 bytes past $5B83's address"},
        "836": {"comment":"RAMDISK_CLOSE on it"},
        "839": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "842": {"synopsis":"A = ERR_NR + 1, kept; the state cleared.","comment":"A = ERR_NR + 1, the report's code"},
        "846": {"synopsis":"Prints report A (REPORT_G_ROOM comes here): the editing state cleared, the code character, a\nspace and the message.","comment":"The code kept"},
        "847": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "850": {"comment":"FLAGX and X_PTR's high byte = 0"},
        "856": {"comment":"DEFADD = 0"},
        "859": {"comment":"STRMS for stream 0 = 1"},
        "865": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "868": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 5 cleared"},
        "872": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLS_LOWER"},
        "875": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "879": {"comment":"The code back"},
        "880": {"comment":"B = the code"},
        "881": {"comment":"0-9: a digit"},
        "885": {"comment":"10-28: a capital"},
        "889": {"comment":"29 up: $14 more, a lowercase letter"},
        "893": {"synopsis":"10-28: 7 more, so that A + \"0\" is A-S."},
        "895": {"synopsis":"The code's character (ROM 1's PRINT_A_DIGIT), a space, then its message.","comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_A_DIGIT: the code's character"},
        "898": {"comment":"A space"},
        "901": {"comment":"The code again"},
        "902": {"comment":"One of the 48K's?"},
        "906": {"comment":"The 128K's: its entry in REPORT_128_TABLE"},
        "911": {"comment":"REPORT_128_TABLE"},
        "916": {"comment":"DE = the message"},
        "919": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT)"},
        "922": {"comment":"On with the line number"},
        "924": {"synopsis":"A 48K report's message: ROM 1's REPORT_MESSAGES through PRINT_MESSAGE.","comment":"ROM 1's REPORT_MESSAGES"},
        "927": {"comment":"Message A (ROM 1's PRINT_MESSAGE)"},
        "930": {"synopsis":"The rest of the report (vector $010F, which ROM 1's REPORT_CHAR hook reaches in 128 BASIC):\n\", \", the line (PPC) and the statement (SUBPPC) through PRINT_BC_NUM, ROM 1's CLEAR_INPUT;\nthen, after a report other than 0 OK, CONTINUE's place: the statement after this one for 9\nSTOP and L BREAK, OLDPPC and OSPCC from NEWPPC and NSPPC or PPC and SUBPPC; NSPPC = $FF,\nFLAGS bit 3 and $5B66 bit 0 cleared; back to the editor (EDITOR_MAIN).","comment":"\", \" (COMMA_MESSAGES)"},
        "934": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MESSAGE"},
        "937": {"comment":"The line"},
        "941": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_BC_NUM"},
        "944": {"comment":"':'"},
        "947": {"comment":"The statement"},
        "952": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_BC_NUM"},
        "955": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_INPUT"},
        "958": {"comment":"0 OK?"},
        "964": {"comment":"9 STOP?"},
        "968": {"comment":"L BREAK?"},
        "972": {"synopsis":"9 STOP and L BREAK: CONTINUE goes on at the next statement."},
        "975": {"synopsis":"OLDPPC and OSPCC set from NEWPPC and NSPPC, or, with NSPPC bit 7 set, from PPC and SUBPPC.","comment":"Three bytes, NSPPC and NEWPPC to OSPCC and OLDPPC, downwards"},
        "984": {"comment":"No jump pending?"},
        "988": {"comment":"HL = SUBPPC: SUBPPC and PPC instead"},
        "989": {"synopsis":"The three bytes copied."},
        "991": {"synopsis":"NSPPC = $FF, FLAGS bit 3 and $5B66 bit 0 cleared; on to EDITOR_MAIN.","comment":"NSPPC = $FF: no jump"},
        "995": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 3 cleared"},
        "999": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 0 cleared"},
        "1004": {"comment":"EDITOR_MAIN"},
        "1007": {"synopsis":"Report G (code $10, \"No room for line\") from STORE_LINE, which stacks this as the place a\nfailed MAKE_ROOM returns to.","comment":"Code $10: report G"},
        "1009": {"comment":"Line 0"},
        "1012": {"comment":"REPORT_PRINT"},
        "1015": {"synopsis":"Stores the edit line as program line BC (the 128K's own, in place of the 48K's):\n1. E_PPC = BC; in bank 7 E_PPC and $EC08 = BC too when BC is not 0.\n2. REPORT_G_ROOM stacked; the line's length from CH_ADD to WORKSP; an old line with that\n   number is removed (ROM 1's FIND_LINE, NEXT_ITEM, RECLAIM).\n3. A line holding only its ENTER is not stored: in bank 7 E_PPC is moved on ($334A).\n4. Otherwise room is made before it (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM, PROG kept), the text copied down,\n   and its number and length written before it.","comment":"E_PPC = BC"},
        "1019": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "1022": {"comment":"Line 0?"},
        "1026": {"comment":"E_PPC and $EC08 = BC"},
        "1034": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; the line looked for.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "1037": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD"},
        "1041": {"comment":"Report G if there is no room"},
        "1045": {"comment":"The line's length"},
        "1051": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "1052": {"comment":"Line BC (ROM 1's FIND_LINE)"},
        "1057": {"comment":"No such line"},
        "1059": {"comment":"The old line removed (NEXT_ITEM, RECLAIM)"},
        "1065": {"synopsis":"Only an ENTER?","comment":"BC = the length: 1, only the ENTER?"},
        "1071": {"comment":"An empty line: E_PPC moved on in bank 7"},
        "1075": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "1078": {"comment":"PREV_LINE_NUM: the line before it"},
        "1085": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "1088": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1090": {"synopsis":"Room for the line and its four-byte head (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM), PROG kept; the text copied;\nthe length and the number written.","comment":"The length kept; BC + 4 for the head"},
        "1095": {"comment":"Before the line found"},
        "1101": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "1105": {"comment":"PROG back"},
        "1108": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "1111": {"comment":"The text, from its end"},
        "1118": {"comment":"DE = E_PPC, the line's number"},
        "1122": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "1123": {"comment":"The length"},
        "1127": {"comment":"The number, high byte first"},
        "1130": {"synopsis":"REPORT_G_ROOM dropped; done."},
        "1132": {"synopsis":"The 128K's own report messages, for codes $1D up (letters a-p): one address per report in\nREPORT_128_MSGS. g and h point at the same message, and p at COPYRIGHT_MSG."},
        "1164": {"synopsis":"Report messages, last letter with bit 7 set: MERGE error, Wrong file type, CODE error, Too\nmany brackets, File already exists, Invalid name, File does not exist, Invalid device,\nInvalid baud rate, Invalid note name, Number too big, Note out of range, Out of range, Too\nmany tied notes."},
        "1377": {"synopsis":"The start-up message, last character with bit 7 set: \"(c) 1986 Sinclair Research Ltd\" (the\nfirst byte is $7F, the copyright sign)."},
        "1405": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it). Changes: AF, DE.","comment":"The next character, bit 7 off"},
        "1407": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "1408": {"comment":"DE kept round RST $10"},
        "1413": {"comment":"Bit 7 was set: done"},
        "1417": {"synopsis":"CHANS as start-up copies it to $5CB6: K (output $09F4, input $10A8), S ($09F4, $15C4), R\n($0F81, $15C4) as in the 48K ROM, then P with output $5B34 (CHAN_P_OUT) and input $5B2F\n(CHAN_P_IN), which reach ROM 0; $80 ends it."},
        "1438": {"synopsis":"STRMS as start-up copies it to $5C10: the offsets of streams -3 to 3 into CHANS."},
        "1452": {"synopsis":"Stops with a report: the byte after the CALL is its code (as ERR_NR holds it, one less than\nthe report's number). Paging byte 0 (RAM bank 0, ROM 0), SP = ERR_SP; the code kept in\n$5B5E. A report the 48K ROM knows (code below $1D) is raised there: CALL_ROM1 runs $5B5D,\nwhich start-up made $CF (RST $08) so that it is followed by the code. The 128K's own: ERR_NR\n= the code, X_PTR = CH_ADD, then ROM 1's CALC_RESET and a return to ERR_SP's address.","comment":"HL = the code's address"},
        "1453": {"comment":"The paging port"},
        "1456": {"comment":"Paging byte 0"},
        "1464": {"comment":"The stack at ERR_SP"},
        "1468": {"comment":"The code"},
        "1469": {"comment":"After RST $08 at $5B5D"},
        "1473": {"comment":"A 48K report?"},
        "1477": {"comment":"RST $08 with the code, in ROM 1"},
        "1480": {"synopsis":"The 128K's own report (or after ROM 1's): ERR_NR = the code, X_PTR = CH_ADD, ROM 1's\nCALC_RESET, then the return to ERR_SP's address.","comment":"Back to the code"},
        "1481": {"comment":"ERR_NR"},
        "1484": {"comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD"},
        "1490": {"comment":"ROM 1's CALC_RESET"},
        "1494": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK: carry unless both SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0) and CAPS SHIFT (port $FEFE bit 0)\nare down. Changes: AF.","comment":"Half-row SPACE to B"},
        "1498": {"comment":"SPACE up: carry"},
        "1500": {"comment":"Half-row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "1504": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT up: carry"},
        "1506": {"comment":"Both down: report L"},
        "1510": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM0's work in this ROM, the routine at HL run for a caller in ROM 1 (channel P's):\nCALL_ROM0_BACK's copy ($5B4A) stacked as the return, TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared; then:\n- Called while ROM 1's editor takes an INPUT line (its error address at ERR_SP is $107F):\n  the routine is called again and again; each character goes into the line (ROM 1's $0F85)\n  and ENTER ends it, the paging set for ROM 1 on the way back.\n- Otherwise once (ROM0_CALL_ONCE): a character returns with carry; none (NC, NZ) is report\n  8.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1511": {"comment":"A back from the alternate AF"},
        "1512": {"comment":"Back through CALL_ROM0_BACK's copy"},
        "1516": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "1520": {"comment":"The routine kept"},
        "1521": {"comment":"The error address at ERR_SP"},
        "1528": {"comment":"ROM 1's editor's ($107F)?"},
        "1535": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "1536": {"comment":"The stack back to ERR_SP; ROM 1's error address dropped"},
        "1541": {"comment":"DE = the word below it, ERR_SP's old value"},
        "1546": {"synopsis":"The routine called, back to ROM0_INPUT_CHAR.","comment":"The routine kept"},
        "1547": {"comment":"Back to $0610 after it"},
        "1551": {"comment":"The routine (channel P's input)"},
        "1552": {"comment":"Carry: a character?"},
        "1554": {"comment":"Z: nothing yet?"},
        "1556": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 7 (report 8, \"End of file\")."},
        "1560": {"synopsis":"No character yet: again."},
        "1563": {"synopsis":"A character: ENTER ends the line; any other goes into it (ROM 1's $0F85, $5B5A kept around\nit).","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "1567": {"comment":"$5B5A kept round the call"},
        "1571": {"comment":"ROM 1's INSERT_CHAR past its MODE clear: A into the line"},
        "1578": {"comment":"The routine back"},
        "1579": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "1581": {"synopsis":"ENTER: back to ROM 1 (the paging byte with bit 4 set) through CALL_ROM0_BACK's copy.","comment":"The routine dropped"},
        "1582": {"comment":"The paging byte with ROM 1"},
        "1587": {"comment":"Stacked for CALL_ROM0_BACK"},
        "1588": {"comment":"CALL_ROM0_BACK's copy"},
        "1591": {"synopsis":"The routine called once, back to $063D: carry or Z returns; otherwise report 8.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "1592": {"comment":"Back to $063D after it"},
        "1597": {"comment":"Carry: a character"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Z: nothing"},
        "1599": {"comment":"Neither: report 8"},
        "1601": {"synopsis":"FORMAT (class $0E): FORMAT \"p\";n sets the RS232 baud rate. The name must be one character\n(report i otherwise) and p or P (report C); ';' and the number (CLASS_6) follow, then the\nstatement's end. A rate of 0 is report j; otherwise the first rate in BAUD_TABLE at or above\nn (9600 for anything above) sets $5B5F.\nObserved: format \"p\";300 made $5B5F 451; format \"p\";1000 made it 110 (1200's); format\n\"p\";20000 left 11 (9600's, the start-up value); format \"p\";0 gave j Invalid baud rate;\nformat \"x\";300 gave C Nonsense in BASIC.","comment":"ROM 1's GET_CHAR"},
        "1604": {"comment":"The name (ROM 1's CLASS_A)"},
        "1607": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "1613": {"comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH"},
        "1616": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "1621": {"comment":"Report i"},
        "1625": {"comment":"p or P?","synopsis":"The name's one character: p or P."},
        "1630": {"comment":"Neither: report C"},
        "1633": {"comment":"';' must follow","synopsis":"';' and the rate."},
        "1642": {"comment":"Past the ';' (ROM 1's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "1645": {"comment":"The rate (ROM 1's CLASS_6)"},
        "1648": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "1654": {"comment":"Kept at $5B71 (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "1661": {"synopsis":"The statement must end here.","comment":"ROM 1's GET_CHAR"},
        "1664": {"comment":"ENTER or ':'"},
        "1670": {"comment":"Neither: report C"},
        "1673": {"synopsis":"Running: the rate looked up.","comment":"STATEMENT_END: checking stops here"},
        "1676": {"comment":"BC = the rate"},
        "1680": {"comment":"0?"},
        "1684": {"comment":"Report j"},
        "1688": {"synopsis":"BAUD_TABLE from the start."},
        "1691": {"synopsis":"The next rate: the last (its high byte $25 or more) or one at or above n is taken.","comment":"DE = the table's rate"},
        "1695": {"comment":"HL = the rate"},
        "1696": {"comment":"The last, 9600 ($2580)?"},
        "1701": {"comment":"At or above n?"},
        "1706": {"comment":"No: past its constant, the next"},
        "1711": {"synopsis":"$5B5F = its constant.","comment":"HL = the constant's place"},
        "1715": {"comment":"$5B5F = the bit time"},
        "1720": {"synopsis":"FORMAT's rates and their bit-time constants: 50 $0AA5, 110 $04D4, 300 $01C3, 600 $00E0, 1200\n$006E, 2400 $0036, 4800 $0019, 9600 $000B."},
        "1752": {"synopsis":"Channel P's input (vector $0121, through CHAN_P_IN's copy): one byte from the RS232 port,\nwhen one comes. A byte kept from last time ($5B61 set, the byte at $5B62) is taken first.\nOtherwise BREAK is tested (BREAK_KEY), interrupts go off, this end signals ready and waits a\nwhile for a start bit; a byte's 8 bits are read at the rate in $5B5F, low bit first, then\nnot ready again; a second byte that starts at once is read too and kept at $5B61-$5B62.\nExit: carry and A = the byte; no carry when none came.\nThe RS232 port is the AY chip's I/O port A (register 14): bit 7 the data in, bit 6 the\nhandshake in (the printer ready when clear), bit 3 the data out, bit 2 the handshake out\n(this end ready when clear).","comment":"A byte kept from last time?"},
        "1759": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "1761": {"comment":"A = the byte kept"},
        "1763": {"comment":"Carry: a byte"},
        "1765": {"comment":"BREAK?","synopsis":"Nothing kept: a byte from the port."},
        "1768": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the timing"},
        "1769": {"comment":"The timing in the alternate set"},
        "1770": {"comment":"DE = the bit time, HL half of it"},
        "1782": {"comment":"B: how long to wait"},
        "1784": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "1785": {"comment":"The AY ports: C = $FD, D = $FF, E = $BF"},
        "1791": {"comment":"Register select"},
        "1792": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "1796": {"comment":"A = the port's bits"},
        "1800": {"comment":"Handshake out clear: ready"},
        "1802": {"comment":"Written back (data port)"},
        "1805": {"comment":"H = the port as written"},
        "1806": {"synopsis":"Waiting for a start bit (the data line low)."},
        "1807": {"comment":"The data line"},
        "1809": {"comment":"Low: a start bit?"},
        "1813": {"synopsis":"Not yet: on waiting; at the end, no byte.","comment":"The wait counter (B') down"},
        "1816": {"comment":"Wait on"},
        "1818": {"comment":"No byte: A = 0, no carry, kept"},
        "1820": {"comment":"Handshake set, done"},
        "1822": {"synopsis":"The start bit, seen three times.","comment":"Still low?"},
        "1828": {"comment":"And again?"},
        "1834": {"comment":"Alternate set: HL = half a bit time, DE = a bit time"},
        "1835": {"comment":"BC' = $FFFD, the register port"},
        "1838": {"comment":"A' = $80: a marker that falls out after eight bits"},
        "1841": {"synopsis":"One bit: a bit time, then the line sampled into A from the top; after eight the byte is in\nA.","comment":"HL + a bit time (half more the first time: mid-bit)"},
        "1842": {"comment":"Padding for the timing"},
        "1846": {"synopsis":"The bit time."},
        "1851": {"comment":"The data line"},
        "1853": {"comment":"Low: a 0?"},
        "1858": {"comment":"A 1, shifted into the byte from the top"},
        "1861": {"comment":"The marker out: eight done?"},
        "1863": {"comment":"Not yet: the next bit"},
        "1867": {"synopsis":"A 0.","comment":"A 0 shifted in"},
        "1870": {"comment":"Eight done?"},
        "1872": {"comment":"Not yet: the next bit"},
        "1876": {"synopsis":"A byte: carry.","comment":"Carry: a byte; kept"},
        "1878": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "1879": {"synopsis":"Handshake out set: not ready; then a look for a second byte that was already on its way.","comment":"The port with the handshake bit set: not ready"},
        "1885": {"comment":"The alternate set"},
        "1886": {"comment":"HL = the bit time - 7, a short wait"},
        "1894": {"synopsis":"A short wait."},
        "1899": {"comment":"BC' = $FFFD"},
        "1902": {"comment":"HL = three bit times"},
        "1905": {"synopsis":"Waiting up to three bit times for another start bit; none: done.","comment":"Line low: another start bit?"},
        "1911": {"comment":"Time up?"},
        "1916": {"comment":"The first byte back; interrupts on"},
        "1919": {"synopsis":"A second start bit.","comment":"Low still?"},
        "1925": {"comment":"And again?"},
        "1931": {"comment":"HL = half the bit time - 2"},
        "1943": {"comment":"BC' = $FFFD"},
        "1946": {"comment":"A' = $80, the marker"},
        "1949": {"synopsis":"The second byte's bits.","comment":"Padding for the timing"},
        "1953": {"comment":"HL + a bit time"},
        "1954": {"synopsis":"The bit time."},
        "1959": {"comment":"The data line"},
        "1961": {"comment":"Low: a 0?"},
        "1966": {"comment":"A 1 shifted in"},
        "1969": {"comment":"Eight done?"},
        "1971": {"comment":"Not yet: the next bit"},
        "1975": {"synopsis":"A 0.","comment":"A 0 shifted in"},
        "1978": {"comment":"Eight done?"},
        "1980": {"comment":"Not yet: the next bit"},
        "1984": {"synopsis":"The second byte kept for next time: $5B61 = 1, $5B62 = it.","comment":"$5B61 = 1: a byte kept"},
        "1989": {"comment":"$5B62 = the byte"},
        "1991": {"comment":"The first byte back, with carry"},
        "1994": {"synopsis":"Channel P's output (vector $0124, through CHAN_P_OUT's copy): prints A on an RS232 printer:\n- after AT or TAB, their numbers ($5B65 counts them, the first kept at $5C0F);\n- keywords ($A3 up) through ROM 1's OUT_UDG_TOKEN, which prints them back through here;\n- characters from space up (codes from $7F as '?'): sent (RS232_OUT), the column ($5B63)\n  counted and a new line after the width ($5B64, 80);\n- ENTER: CR and LF, column 0; the comma control: spaces to the next column of 8; AT and TAB:\n  their two numbers awaited (RS232_AT_TAB); other controls below $10 nothing; colour\n  controls: their numbers taken and dropped.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "1995": {"comment":"Numbers awaited?"},
        "2001": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "2005": {"comment":"The last: AT or TAB done"},
        "2007": {"comment":"The character: AT's or TAB's last number"},
        "2008": {"comment":"RS232_AT_TAB_DO"},
        "2011": {"synopsis":"The first number kept.","comment":"The number"},
        "2012": {"comment":"The first kept"},
        "2016": {"synopsis":"Not a number: the character itself.","comment":"The character"},
        "2017": {"comment":"A keyword?"},
        "2021": {"comment":"$5B5A kept round the call"},
        "2025": {"comment":"ROM 1's OUT_UDG_TOKEN"},
        "2032": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "2034": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0: a space","synopsis":"Below $A3: FLAGS bit 0 set for a space, cleared otherwise."},
        "2039": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "2043": {"comment":"Yes: bit 0 set"},
        "2045": {"comment":"Codes from $7F as '?'","synopsis":"Codes from $7F are printed as '?'."},
        "2049": {"comment":"'?'"},
        "2051": {"comment":"A control?","synopsis":"A character or a control."},
        "2055": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "2056": {"comment":"The column"},
        "2060": {"comment":"Past the width?"},
        "2066": {"comment":"A new line first"},
        "2069": {"comment":"Column 1: this character"},
        "2074": {"synopsis":"Sent.","comment":"The character back"},
        "2075": {"comment":"Sent (RS232_OUT)"},
        "2078": {"synopsis":"A control: ENTER?","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "2082": {"synopsis":"A new line: CR, LF, column 0.","comment":"Column 0"},
        "2086": {"comment":"CR"},
        "2091": {"comment":"LF"},
        "2096": {"synopsis":"The comma control (6): spaces to the next column of 8.","comment":"The comma control (6)?"},
        "2100": {"comment":"C = the column ($5B63), B = the width ($5B64)"},
        "2104": {"comment":"E counts the spaces"},
        "2106": {"synopsis":"Counting the spaces.","comment":"One more space"},
        "2107": {"comment":"The column it reaches"},
        "2109": {"comment":"At the width?"},
        "2112": {"synopsis":"Modulo 8.","comment":"A multiple of 8?"},
        "2116": {"comment":"Not yet: on subtracting"},
        "2118": {"comment":"Not one: another space"},
        "2120": {"synopsis":"E spaces.","comment":"E kept"},
        "2121": {"comment":"A space, through this routine"},
        "2127": {"comment":"All sent?"},
        "2131": {"synopsis":"AT (22), TAB (23), the other controls $10-$1F (two numbers taken, RS232_COLOUR), or nothing\nbelow $10.","comment":"AT?"},
        "2135": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "2139": {"comment":"Other controls below $10 ignored"},
        "2142": {"comment":"$10 up: as a colour control"},
        "2144": {"synopsis":"AT or TAB: kept, two numbers awaited.","comment":"The control kept in $5C0E"},
        "2147": {"comment":"Two numbers awaited"},
        "2153": {"synopsis":"A colour control: two numbers awaited (and dropped).","comment":"The control kept in $5C0E"},
        "2156": {"comment":"Two numbers awaited"},
        "2162": {"synopsis":"The numbers arrived: for AT the second (the column), for TAB the first; for a colour\nnothing. The column is taken modulo the width; 0 is a new line; otherwise spaces up to it.","comment":"D = the last number"},
        "2163": {"comment":"The control"},
        "2166": {"comment":"AT? Its second number is the column"},
        "2170": {"comment":"TAB? A colour returns here"},
        "2174": {"comment":"TAB: its first number, kept at $5C0F"},
        "2178": {"synopsis":"Modulo the width.","comment":"The width"},
        "2181": {"comment":"At or past the width?"},
        "2186": {"synopsis":"Less the width.","comment":"D = the column less the width"},
        "2192": {"synopsis":"Spaces up to the column.","comment":"Column 0?"},
        "2194": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "2197": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"At the column yet?"},
        "2202": {"comment":"D kept"},
        "2203": {"comment":"A space"},
        "2211": {"synopsis":"Sends byte A to the RS232 port (vector $0127): waits for the printer's handshake (bit 6\nclear), testing BREAK meanwhile (BREAK_KEY); then, interrupts off, 11 bits on bit 3, each a\nbit time ($5B5F - 2): a start bit, the eight bits low first, stop bits.\nThe RS232 port is the AY chip's I/O port A (register 14): bit 7 the data in, bit 6 the\nhandshake in (the printer ready when clear), bit 3 the data out, bit 2 the handshake out\n(this end ready when clear).","comment":"The byte kept"},
        "2212": {"comment":"The AY ports: C = $FD, D = $FF, E = $BF"},
        "2218": {"comment":"Register 14, the I/O port, selected"},
        "2223": {"synopsis":"Waiting for the printer.","comment":"BREAK? (BREAK_KEY)"},
        "2226": {"comment":"The port's bits"},
        "2228": {"comment":"Bit 6 set: not ready yet?"},
        "2232": {"comment":"DE = the bit time - 2"},
        "2242": {"comment":"The byte back"},
        "2243": {"comment":"Inverted"},
        "2244": {"comment":"Carry: the start bit first"},
        "2245": {"comment":"11 bits"},
        "2247": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the timing"},
        "2248": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"Count and byte kept"},
        "2250": {"comment":"A = $FE: the port's other bits"},
        "2252": {"comment":"HL = the bit time"},
        "2254": {"comment":"BC = $BFFD, the data port"},
        "2257": {"comment":"No carry: bit 3 set (RS232_OUT_1)"},
        "2260": {"comment":"Carry: bit 3 clear"},
        "2266": {"synopsis":"A 1 (the data inverted: bit 3 set)."},
        "2270": {"comment":"To the next line: the same time as the other path"},
        "2272": {"synopsis":"The bit time."},
        "2277": {"comment":"Padding for the timing"},
        "2280": {"comment":"Byte and count back"},
        "2282": {"comment":"The next bit; 0s after the eighth give the stop bits"},
        "2284": {"comment":"All 11 sent?"},
        "2288": {"synopsis":"COPY (vector $012A): the screen to an RS232 printer as graphics, in 44 strips of 4 pixel\nlines from the top ($5B72 counting down from $2B): for each, COPY_CODES' $1B '1', $1B 'L',\n0, 3 (768 dots), the 256 columns (COPY_STRIP), and a line feed; at the end $1B '2'.","comment":"$5B72 = 43: 44 strips"},
        "2293": {"synopsis":"One strip.","comment":"COPY_CODES: $1B '1', $1B 'L', 0, 3"},
        "2299": {"comment":"The strip's columns (COPY_STRIP)"},
        "2302": {"comment":"A line feed"},
        "2308": {"comment":"The last strip?"},
        "2315": {"comment":"The next strip down"},
        "2318": {"synopsis":"The last: $1B '2'.","comment":"$1B '2'"},
        "2325": {"synopsis":"A strip's 256 columns, from x = 0 up (x = 255 - $5B71, which counts down).","comment":"The count from 255"},
        "2330": {"synopsis":"One column.","comment":"COPY_COLUMN"},
        "2333": {"comment":"The count at 0: done?"},
        "2339": {"comment":"The count down"},
        "2342": {"synopsis":"One column of the strip: its 4 pixels (COPY_POINT), each as 2 dots one above the other, make\na byte, sent 3 times (768 dots in all).","comment":"D = $C0: the top pixel's two dots"},
        "2345": {"comment":"C = the count ($5B71), B = the strip ($5B72)"},
        "2349": {"comment":"B = 4 x strip + 3: the strip's top line"},
        "2355": {"comment":"C = 255 - the count: x from 0 up"},
        "2358": {"comment":"The byte so far: 0"},
        "2359": {"comment":"Byte, dots and position kept"},
        "2362": {"synopsis":"The next pixel down.","comment":"Z: the pixel clear (COPY_POINT)"},
        "2367": {"comment":"E = 0, or the two dots for a set pixel"},
        "2372": {"synopsis":"Its two dots into the byte.","comment":"The dots into the byte"},
        "2375": {"comment":"The next line down"},
        "2376": {"comment":"The next two dots"},
        "2382": {"comment":"Not the fourth pixel yet?"},
        "2386": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "2387": {"comment":"Three times"},
        "2389": {"synopsis":"Sent three times.","comment":"Count and byte kept"},
        "2391": {"comment":"RS232_OUT"},
        "2399": {"synopsis":"Sends the bytes at HL (a count first) through RS232_OUT.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "2401": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "2404": {"comment":"RS232_OUT"},
        "2413": {"synopsis":"Z when the pixel at x = C, y = B is clear (ROM 1's PIXEL_BYTE at $22AA, then its bit).","comment":"ROM 1's PIXEL_BYTE: HL = the byte, A = the bit's place"},
        "2416": {"comment":"B = the place + 1"},
        "2418": {"comment":"A = the pixel's bit, from $80"},
        "2420": {"synopsis":"The pixel's bit."},
        "2423": {"comment":"Z: the pixel clear?"},
        "2425": {"synopsis":"COPY's printer control sequences, each a count then bytes, sent through $08A3: 6 bytes from\n$0979 ($1B '1', $1B 'L', 0, 3), 1 from $0980 ($0A), 2 from $0982 ($1B '2')."},
        "2437": {"synopsis":"Plays B strings (on the calculator stack) together, interrupts off:\n1. Room in the workspace for a 55-byte block per string and a 60-byte shared one (ROM 1's\n   WORK_ROOM): IY at the shared one, IX at each string's, filled with the defaults and the\n   string's place and end (ROM 1's STK_FETCH, the last string first); each block's address\n   into the shared list; TEMPO_CODE copied into the shared block; the AY's mixer set to\n   tones on A-C ($F8) and the envelope period to $FFFF.\n2. PLAY_LOOP: each string's next note (PLAY_NEXT), then until every string has ended: the\n   shortest length now (PLAY_SHORTEST), the notes started (PLAY_START_NOTES), that long\n   waited (PLAY_WAIT), the lengths moved on (PLAY_ADVANCE).\n3. At the end the AY silenced (PLAY_SILENCE) and interrupts on.\nA string's block (IX, 55 bytes): +0 the note sounding, +1 its MIDI channel ($FF none), +2\nits number (0-7; 0-2 are AY channels A-C), +3 the octave's base note (12 x O; 60 at first),\n+4 the volume (15; bit 4 set: the envelope), +5 the length (5), +6 the place in the string,\n+8 its end, +10 flags, +11 the bracket depth and +12 the brackets' places, +22 the repeat\ncount and +23 its places, +33 the notes tied, +34 the lengths to play.\nThe shared block (IY, 60 bytes): +16 a bit for each string that has ended ($FF: all), +17\neach string's block's pointer to its current length, +33 the current string's bit, +34 the\nstrings still to look at, +35 the place in the list of blocks, +37 the shortest length now,\n+39 the tempo's delay, +41 the envelope shape, +42 the strings with a new note, +43\nTEMPO_CODE's copy.\nObserved: play \"1c\" set AY registers 0-1 to $01A8 (note 60's period) and ended with 0 OK,\n0:1; play \"O4cC\" played.","comment":"Interrupts off while it plays"},
        "2438": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "2439": {"comment":"55 bytes a string"},
        "2442": {"comment":"60 shared"},
        "2445": {"synopsis":"55 bytes for each string."},
        "2448": {"comment":"BC = the room"},
        "2450": {"comment":"Room (ROM 1's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "2453": {"comment":"Interrupts off again"},
        "2454": {"comment":"IY = the shared block"},
        "2457": {"comment":"IX = past the room"},
        "2460": {"comment":"No string ended"},
        "2464": {"synopsis":"The next string's block, from the top down: the octave 60, no MIDI channel, volume 15,\nlength 5, nothing tied, no brackets or repeats; its place and end (ROM 1's STK_FETCH); its\naddress into the shared list; its bit into IY + 16."},
        "2469": {"comment":"Octave base 60"},
        "2473": {"comment":"No MIDI channel"},
        "2477": {"comment":"Volume 15"},
        "2481": {"comment":"Length 5"},
        "2485": {"comment":"Nothing tied"},
        "2489": {"comment":"No repeat for ever (bit 0)"},
        "2493": {"comment":"No bracket open"},
        "2497": {"comment":"No ')' kept"},
        "2501": {"comment":"The first ')' slot cleared"},
        "2509": {"comment":"The string (ROM 1's STK_FETCH)"},
        "2513": {"comment":"Its place"},
        "2519": {"comment":"The first bracket's place"},
        "2525": {"comment":"HL = its end: the place + the length"},
        "2527": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "2533": {"comment":"B = the strings left"},
        "2535": {"comment":"C = 2 x (B - 1): its entry in the shared list"},
        "2541": {"comment":"HL = IY + C"},
        "2545": {"comment":"BC = the block"},
        "2548": {"comment":"The block in the list"},
        "2552": {"comment":"A bit for it"},
        "2556": {"comment":"One string fewer"},
        "2559": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "2562": {"comment":"More?"},
        "2564": {"comment":"The count dropped"},
        "2565": {"synopsis":"The tempo's delay ($0B1A), TEMPO_CODE copied to IY + 43; the mixer ($F8: tones on A-C, no\nnoise), the envelope period $FFFF.","comment":"IY + 39-40 = $0B1A, the tempo's delay"},
        "2573": {"comment":"DE = IY + 43"},
        "2581": {"comment":"TEMPO_CODE to IY + 43"},
        "2589": {"comment":"Register 7, the mixer"},
        "2593": {"comment":"AY_WRITE"},
        "2596": {"comment":"Registers 11-12, the envelope period"},
        "2603": {"comment":"Register 12"},
        "2607": {"comment":"PLAY_LOOP"},
        "2609": {"synopsis":"Copied into the shared block and run there with ROM 1 paged in (PLAY_TEMPO): RST $28 and\ncalculator codes stk-ten, exchange, division, a literal, division, end-calc, then RET: the\ntempo's delay from T's number."},
        "2622": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK as BREAK_KEY does. Exit: carry unless SPACE and CAPS SHIFT are both down.","comment":"Half-row SPACE to B"},
        "2628": {"comment":"Half-row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "2634": {"synopsis":"The list of blocks from its pointers to the lengths (IY + 17); then PLAY_LIST_INIT's\nsettings.","comment":"BC = 17: the lengths' list"},
        "2639": {"synopsis":"The list of blocks from the start (IY + 0): IY + 35 at it, IY + 34 = the ended bits, IY + 33\n= 1: the first string.","comment":"BC = 0: the blocks' list"},
        "2642": {"synopsis":"IY + 35 = HL, the strings to look at, the first string's bit.","comment":"HL = IY + BC"},
        "2646": {"comment":"IY + 35 = it"},
        "2652": {"comment":"IY + 34 = the ended bits"},
        "2658": {"comment":"IY + 33 = 1: the first string's bit"},
        "2663": {"synopsis":"IX = the block whose address is at HL.","comment":"DE = the block"},
        "2666": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "2670": {"synopsis":"The list's place moved on to the next block.","comment":"HL = the list's place"},
        "2676": {"comment":"Two on"},
        "2685": {"synopsis":"Each string that has not ended: its next note (PLAY_NEXT).","comment":"The first string"},
        "2688": {"synopsis":"The next string: ended ones are passed by.","comment":"This string's ended bit: ended?"},
        "2694": {"comment":"IX = its block"},
        "2697": {"comment":"PLAY_NEXT"},
        "2700": {"synopsis":"The next string's bit; after the last, PLAY_NOTES.","comment":"The next string's bit; past the last?"},
        "2706": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT"},
        "2711": {"synopsis":"The shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST), the notes started (PLAY_START_NOTES); all ended: the AY\nsilenced, interrupts on, done.","comment":"The shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST)"},
        "2714": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "2715": {"comment":"PLAY_START_NOTES"},
        "2719": {"synopsis":"Have all the strings ended?","comment":"Every bit set: all ended?"},
        "2726": {"comment":"PLAY_SILENCE"},
        "2731": {"synopsis":"The shortest length waited (PLAY_WAIT), the lengths moved on (PLAY_ADVANCE), the next\nshortest; again.","comment":"One unit less"},
        "2732": {"comment":"PLAY_WAIT"},
        "2735": {"comment":"PLAY_ADVANCE"},
        "2738": {"comment":"The next shortest"},
        "2743": {"synopsis":"PLAY's command letters, searched by PLAY_FIND_LETTER (CPIR from here): H Z Y X W U V M T ) (\nN O !. Capitals only: o9c is a note name, and report k."},
        "2757": {"synopsis":"The string's next character, past spaces and ENTERs (PLAY_SKIP_SPACE). Exit: carry at the\nstring's end; otherwise A and the place moved on.","comment":"A = the character (PLAY_SKIP_SPACE)"},
        "2760": {"comment":"The string's end?"},
        "2761": {"comment":"The place on one"},
        "2769": {"synopsis":"A note's name: '#' sharp (+1), '$' flat (-1), any number of each; a capital A-G an octave\nhigher than the small letter; the note from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE. Exit: A = the note within its\noctave, or $80 for '&' (a rest); at the string's end its bit is set in IY + 16. Anything\nelse is report k."},
        "2770": {"comment":"C = the sharps less the flats"},
        "2772": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "2775": {"comment":"The string's end?"},
        "2777": {"comment":"'&', a rest?"},
        "2781": {"comment":"$80: a rest"},
        "2783": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "2785": {"synopsis":"The string's end: its bit set in IY + 16.","comment":"This string's bit"},
        "2788": {"comment":"Into the ended bits"},
        "2796": {"synopsis":"'#': one higher.","comment":"'#'?"},
        "2800": {"comment":"One higher"},
        "2803": {"synopsis":"'$': one lower.","comment":"'$'?"},
        "2807": {"comment":"One lower"},
        "2810": {"synopsis":"A small letter (bit 5 set) as it is; a capital 12 higher.","comment":"A small letter?"},
        "2814": {"comment":"A capital: C + 12"},
        "2820": {"synopsis":"A-G only (report k otherwise): its place in the octave from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE, plus the sharps\nand flats.","comment":"Capital; 0-6 for A-G"},
        "2824": {"comment":"Below A: report k"},
        "2827": {"comment":"Past G: report k"},
        "2832": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "2833": {"comment":"Its entry in PLAY_NOTE_TABLE"},
        "2840": {"comment":"A = its place in the octave"},
        "2842": {"comment":"Plus the sharps and flats"},
        "2845": {"synopsis":"Reads the decimal number at the string's place (none is 0), moving past it. Exit: BC = the\nnumber; over 65535 is report l.","comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "2847": {"comment":"HL = the string's place"},
        "2853": {"comment":"DE = 0, the number"},
        "2856": {"synopsis":"The next digit.","comment":"A digit?"},
        "2865": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "2867": {"comment":"DE x 10 (PLAY_TIMES_TEN)"},
        "2870": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "2876": {"comment":"Past 65535: report l"},
        "2878": {"comment":"DE = the number so far"},
        "2882": {"synopsis":"Report l."},
        "2885": {"synopsis":"The place stored; BC = the number.","comment":"The place after the digits"},
        "2891": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "2896": {"synopsis":"DE = DE x 10; a carry is report l.","comment":"HL = 0"},
        "2899": {"comment":"Ten times"},
        "2901": {"synopsis":"Ten additions.","comment":"Past 65535?"},
        "2906": {"comment":"DE = the result"},
        "2908": {"synopsis":"Reads the current string up to its next note: BREAK stops it all (report L, after\nPLAY_SILENCE); each character: a command letter runs its routine from PLAY_COMMANDS;\nanything else is a note (PLAY_NOTE), which returns past PLAY_NEXT's loop. The string's end\nmarks it ended.","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "2913": {"comment":"Yes: silence"},
        "2917": {"comment":"Report L"},
        "2921": {"comment":"The next character","synopsis":"A character."},
        "2924": {"comment":"The end: the string has ended"},
        "2927": {"comment":"Which command?"},
        "2934": {"comment":"Its routine from PLAY_COMMANDS"},
        "2938": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "2942": {"comment":"Run it; a note returns past the JR"},
        "2948": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "2949": {"synopsis":"'!': everything to the next '!' (or the end) is skipped.","comment":"The next character"},
        "2952": {"comment":"The end: the string has ended"},
        "2955": {"comment":"'!'?"},
        "2960": {"synopsis":"O n: the octave, 0-8 (report n otherwise): the base note 12 x n.","comment":"The number n (PLAY_NUMBER)"},
        "2963": {"comment":"Over 8: report n"},
        "2969": {"comment":"A = 4n, B = 4n"},
        "2974": {"comment":"8n + 4n: 12n"},
        "2977": {"comment":"The octave's base note"},
        "2981": {"synopsis":"N: a separator; nothing to do."},
        "2982": {"synopsis":"'(': one bracket deeper (report d at 5): its place kept, from IX + 12.","comment":"The brackets open"},
        "2985": {"comment":"One more: 5 is report d"},
        "2994": {"comment":"HL = its slot, IX + 12 + 2n"},
        "3000": {"comment":"The string's place kept there"},
        "3010": {"synopsis":"')': the repeat. The first time at a ')' its place is kept and the string goes back to its\n'(' (or the start); the second time it goes on, the bracket closed. With no '(' left open,\nthe repeat goes on for ever.\nObserved: (((((c))))) gave d Too many brackets, 0:1.","comment":"A = the ')' places kept less 1 ($FF: none)"},
        "3013": {"comment":"Their slots from IX + 23"},
        "3016": {"comment":"None kept: a new ')'"},
        "3020": {"comment":"HL = the last one kept"},
        "3023": {"comment":"This ')'? (low byte)"},
        "3029": {"comment":"And the high byte?"},
        "3036": {"comment":"Its second time: one fewer kept"},
        "3039": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "3044": {"comment":"Repeating for ever?"},
        "3049": {"comment":"For ever: kept again"},
        "3053": {"comment":"Bracket 0: the string's start"},
        "3056": {"synopsis":"A new ')': kept (report d at 5), then back to the '('.","comment":"One more ')' kept"},
        "3059": {"comment":"5: report d"},
        "3068": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "3071": {"comment":"The place kept there"},
        "3080": {"comment":"A = the open brackets: back to the last '('"},
        "3083": {"synopsis":"The place back to bracket A's; one bracket less.","comment":"DE = 12: the '(' places from IX + 12"},
        "3086": {"comment":"PLAY_SLOT: HL = bracket A's kept place"},
        "3089": {"comment":"The string's place = the kept one"},
        "3098": {"comment":"One bracket less: any still open?"},
        "3102": {"comment":"None: the count 0, and IX + 10 bit 0 set"},
        "3111": {"synopsis":"HL = IX + DE + 2 x A: an entry of one of the block's lists.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "3114": {"comment":"+ DE, the list's offset"},
        "3115": {"comment":"BC = 2 x A, the entry's offset"},
        "3122": {"synopsis":"T n: the tempo, 60-240 (report n otherwise), set only by the first string: 4 x n stacked\n(ROM 1's STACK_BC) and TEMPO_CODE run in the shared block with ROM 1 paged in, as CALL_ROM1\ndoes; its result (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC) is the delay at IY + 39.\nObserved: T300 gave n Out of range, 0:1.","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3125": {"comment":"Over 255: report n"},
        "3130": {"comment":"60 or more"},
        "3136": {"comment":"Below 241"},
        "3141": {"comment":"Only the first string's"},
        "3146": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "3150": {"comment":"4 x n"},
        "3152": {"comment":"BC = 4 x n"},
        "3154": {"comment":"IY (the shared block) kept"},
        "3156": {"comment":"Stacked (ROM 1's STACK_BC)"},
        "3159": {"comment":"Interrupts off again after ROM 1"},
        "3160": {"comment":"IY = the shared block, kept again"},
        "3164": {"comment":"HL = IY + 43: TEMPO_CODE's copy"},
        "3171": {"comment":"IY for ROM 1"},
        "3175": {"comment":"TEMPO_CODE's address stacked"},
        "3176": {"comment":"Back to $0C76 afterwards"},
        "3182": {"comment":"$5B14 under it: the way back to this ROM"},
        "3186": {"comment":"TEMPO_CODE on top: where $5B00 returns to"},
        "3187": {"comment":"Run TEMPO_CODE"},
        "3190": {"synopsis":"Back: the number as BC (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC) is the delay.","comment":"Back in this ROM: interrupts off"},
        "3191": {"comment":"ROM 1's FP_TO_BC: BC = the delay"},
        "3194": {"comment":"Off again after ROM 1"},
        "3195": {"comment":"IY = the shared block"},
        "3197": {"comment":"The delay at IY + 39"},
        "3204": {"synopsis":"M n: the mixer (AY register 7) = NOT n, n 0-63 (report n otherwise).","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3208": {"comment":"64 up: report n"},
        "3213": {"comment":"NOT n: the mixer's bits turn a tone or noise on when 0"},
        "3217": {"comment":"AY_WRITE: register 7"},
        "3221": {"synopsis":"V n: the volume, 0-15 (report n otherwise), into the block and the string's AY volume\nregister (8 + its number; not checked to be below 3, so a fourth string's V would write\nregister 11).\nObserved: V16 gave n Out of range, 0:1.","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3225": {"comment":"16 up: report n"},
        "3230": {"comment":"The block's volume"},
        "3233": {"comment":"D = 8 + the string's number: its volume register"},
        "3240": {"comment":"E = the volume"},
        "3241": {"comment":"AY_WRITE"},
        "3245": {"synopsis":"U: the volume $1F, the envelope's (bit 4).","comment":"D = the volume register (not written here)"},
        "3252": {"comment":"E = $1F: bit 4, the envelope"},
        "3254": {"comment":"Into the block's volume, used at the next note"},
        "3258": {"synopsis":"W n: the envelope shape, 0-7 (report n otherwise), through PLAY_SHAPES, kept at IY + 41.","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3262": {"comment":"8 up: report n"},
        "3267": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_SHAPES + n"},
        "3273": {"comment":"The shape kept at IY + 41"},
        "3278": {"synopsis":"X n: the envelope period (AY registers 11 and 12) = n.","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3281": {"comment":"Register 11 = the low byte"},
        "3287": {"comment":"Register 12 = the high byte"},
        "3293": {"synopsis":"Y n: the MIDI channel, 1-16 (report n otherwise), kept as n - 1.","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3297": {"comment":"0: report n"},
        "3301": {"comment":"Over 16: report n"},
        "3306": {"comment":"The channel - 1 at IX + 1"},
        "3310": {"synopsis":"Z n: the byte n sent to MIDI (MIDI_OUT).","comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: BC = n"},
        "3313": {"comment":"MIDI_OUT: its low byte sent"},
        "3318": {"synopsis":"H: all the strings ended at once.","comment":"IY + 16: every string's ended bit set"},
        "3323": {"synopsis":"A note, with its length before it: no digit, the current length; 1-9 a length (it becomes\nthe current one), 10-12 a triplet (three notes of the length); '_' ties more lengths to it.\nThe lengths go into the block's list (PLAY_LENGTH), the note sounds (through\nPLAY_START_NOTES); then PLAY_NEXT returns. A length of 0 or over 12 is report n; too many\ntriplet notes report o.","comment":"PLAY_IS_DIGIT: a length first?"},
        "3326": {"comment":"Not a digit: the current length"},
        "3329": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_LIST: HL = the block's list of lengths"},
        "3332": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_PTR: the string's pointer at the list's start"},
        "3335": {"comment":"No lengths yet (IX + 33)"},
        "3339": {"comment":"Back to the digit"},
        "3342": {"comment":"The length"},
        "3346": {"comment":"0: report n"},
        "3350": {"comment":"13 up: report n"},
        "3355": {"comment":"10-12: a triplet"},
        "3359": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_UNITS: DE = the triplet's units"},
        "3362": {"comment":"PLAY_TIE_COUNT: one length"},
        "3365": {"comment":"Stored in the list"},
        "3368": {"synopsis":"A triplet length: twice more in the list.","comment":"PLAY_TIE_COUNT: one more length"},
        "3371": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "3375": {"comment":"The third entry's place"},
        "3376": {"comment":"The third counted, then stored"},
        "3378": {"synopsis":"1-9: the current length.","comment":"The current length = n"},
        "3381": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_UNITS: DE = its units"},
        "3384": {"synopsis":"One more length counted (report o past 10).","comment":"PLAY_TIE_COUNT: one more length (report o)"},
        "3387": {"synopsis":"'_'? Then the next length is added to it.","comment":"PLAY_SKIP_SPACE: A = the next character"},
        "3390": {"comment":"A '_'?"},
        "3394": {"comment":"PLAY_CHAR: past it"},
        "3397": {"comment":"PLAY_NUMBER: the tied length"},
        "3401": {"comment":"Below 10: a plain length"},
        "3405": {"comment":"10-12: the triplet's first note added to the tie"},
        "3416": {"comment":"The tied total stored"},
        "3419": {"comment":"DE = the triplet's units, for two more entries"},
        "3423": {"synopsis":"A tied length added.","comment":"The current length = n"},
        "3426": {"comment":"DE = the total plus its units"},
        "3435": {"comment":"Another '_'?"},
        "3438": {"synopsis":"The length stored; PLAY_NEXT ends.","comment":"The last length stored"},
        "3441": {"comment":"PLAY_RET_PAST: PLAY_NEXT ends"},
        "3444": {"synopsis":"One more length in the list: 11 is report o.","comment":"A = the lengths so far + 1"},
        "3448": {"comment":"11: report o"},
        "3453": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3457": {"synopsis":"No length given: the current one, once.","comment":"PLAY_BACK_CHAR: back to the note's name"},
        "3460": {"comment":"One length"},
        "3464": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_LIST: HL = the list"},
        "3467": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_PTR: the string's pointer at it"},
        "3470": {"comment":"C = the current length"},
        "3474": {"comment":"DE = its units (PLAY_LEN_UNITS)"},
        "3478": {"comment":"Stored as the only length"},
        "3481": {"comment":"PLAY_RET_PAST: PLAY_NEXT ends"},
        "3484": {"synopsis":"Returns two bytes past the call's return: past PLAY_NEXT's JR, which ends it.","comment":"The return address two bytes on"},
        "3489": {"synopsis":"The string's end: its bit set in IY + 16.","comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "3490": {"synopsis":"The bit set.","comment":"A = the string's bit"},
        "3493": {"comment":"Into the ended bits"},
        "3500": {"synopsis":"HL = the block's list of lengths (IX + 34)."},
        "3503": {"comment":"+ 34: the list of lengths"},
        "3508": {"synopsis":"The string's pointer to its current length (in IY's list) = HL.","comment":"The list's address kept"},
        "3509": {"comment":"HL = IY + 17: the strings' pointers"},
        "3516": {"comment":"+ 2 x the string's number"},
        "3524": {"comment":"DE = the list"},
        "3525": {"comment":"Stored as the string's pointer"},
        "3529": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "3530": {"synopsis":"The routines of PLAY's commands, from the index PLAY_FIND_LETTER gives (0 for none): a note\n(PLAY_NOTE), '!', O, N, '(', ')', T, M, V, U, W, X, Y, Z, H."},
        "3560": {"synopsis":"W's envelope shapes for 0-7: 0, 4, 11, 13, 8, 12, 14, 10."},
        "3568": {"synopsis":"Looks A up in PLAY_LETTERS (CPIR). Exit: Z when found; C = its index from the end (H is 14),\n0 when not found.","comment":"15 letters"},
        "3571": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_LETTERS"},
        "3574": {"comment":"A among them?"},
        "3577": {"synopsis":"The notes A-G within an octave from C: 9, 11, 0, 2, 4, 5, 7."},
        "3584": {"synopsis":"DE = length C's units, from PLAY_LENGTHS. Keeps HL."},
        "3585": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "3587": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_LENGTHS + C"},
        "3591": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "3596": {"synopsis":"The lengths' units for 0-12: $80, then 1-9: 6, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 72, 96; 10-12\n(triplets): 4, 8, 16."},
        "3609": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit.","comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "3612": {"comment":"Below ':' (a digit): no carry"},
        "3616": {"synopsis":"Sounds note A (within the octave) on the string's channel: the octave's base added (128 or\nmore is report m); string 0 also sets the noise period (AY register 6) from it; for AY\nchannels A-C the tone period from PLAY_PERIODS (notes below 21 take $0FBF) into registers 2n\nand 2n + 1, and with the envelope in use, register 13 = the shape. Kept at IX + 0.","comment":"C = the note within its octave"},
        "3617": {"comment":"+ the octave's base"},
        "3621": {"comment":"128 up: report m"},
        "3626": {"comment":"C = the note"},
        "3627": {"comment":"The string's number"},
        "3631": {"comment":"Not string 0: no noise"},
        "3633": {"comment":"E = (127 - the note) / 4: the noise period"},
        "3641": {"comment":"Register 6: the noise period"},
        "3644": {"comment":"AY_WRITE"},
        "3647": {"synopsis":"The note kept; a tone for AY channels A-C.","comment":"The note kept at IX + 0"},
        "3650": {"comment":"The string's number"},
        "3653": {"comment":"AY channels A-C only"},
        "3656": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_PERIODS"},
        "3661": {"comment":"A = the note"},
        "3662": {"comment":"Below 21?"},
        "3666": {"comment":"Then period $0FBF"},
        "3671": {"synopsis":"The period from PLAY_PERIODS.","comment":"BC = 2 x (the note - 21)"},
        "3675": {"comment":"DE = its period"},
        "3678": {"synopsis":"Into the channel's two tone registers.","comment":"HL = the period"},
        "3679": {"comment":"Registers 2n, 2n + 1"},
        "3684": {"comment":"Register 2n = the low byte"},
        "3688": {"comment":"Register 2n + 1 = the high byte"},
        "3693": {"comment":"The envelope?"},
        "3698": {"comment":"Register 13: its shape"},
        "3708": {"synopsis":"AY register D = E (ports $FFFD and $BFFD). Keeps BC."},
        "3709": {"comment":"Register D selected"},
        "3714": {"comment":"E written to it"},
        "3721": {"synopsis":"A = AY register A. Keeps BC."},
        "3722": {"comment":"Register A selected"},
        "3727": {"comment":"Read"},
        "3731": {"synopsis":"Silences the AY (mixer $FF, volumes A-C 0) and ends each string's MIDI note (MIDI_NOTE_OFF);\nIY back to $5C3A.","comment":"Register 7 = $FF: tones and noise off"},
        "3738": {"comment":"Registers 8, 9 and 10 = 0: the volumes"},
        "3753": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_INIT: from the first string"},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"Each string.","comment":"This string ended?"},
        "3762": {"comment":"PLAY_BLOCK: IX = its block"},
        "3765": {"comment":"MIDI_NOTE_OFF"},
        "3768": {"synopsis":"The next.","comment":"The next string's bit: past the last?"},
        "3774": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT: the next block"},
        "3779": {"synopsis":"IY = $5C3A.","comment":"IY back for ROM 1's system variables"},
        "3784": {"synopsis":"The string's place moved back to the previous character that is not a space or ENTER. Keeps\nDE, HL."},
        "3786": {"comment":"HL = the string's place"},
        "3792": {"synopsis":"Back one.","comment":"One back"},
        "3794": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3798": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "3802": {"comment":"The place stored"},
        "3811": {"synopsis":"The string's place moved past spaces and ENTERs. Exit: carry at the string's end; A = the\ncharacter. Keeps BC, DE, HL."},
        "3814": {"comment":"HL = the string's place"},
        "3820": {"synopsis":"At the end?","comment":"At the end (high byte)?"},
        "3826": {"comment":"... and the low byte?"},
        "3832": {"comment":"Carry: the end"},
        "3835": {"synopsis":"A space or ENTER is passed.","comment":"A space?"},
        "3840": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "3844": {"comment":"No carry: A = the character"},
        "3845": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "3849": {"synopsis":"Past it.","comment":"One on, stored"},
        "3858": {"synopsis":"PLAY's errors: the AY silenced and interrupts on first, then the report: n Out of range\n(error code $29).","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3862": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "3866": {"synopsis":"l Number too big (error code $27).","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3870": {"comment":"Report l"},
        "3874": {"synopsis":"k Invalid note name (error code $26).\nObserved: play \"x\" gave k Invalid note name, 0:1.","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3878": {"comment":"Report k"},
        "3882": {"synopsis":"d Too many brackets (error code $1F).","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3886": {"comment":"Report d"},
        "3890": {"synopsis":"m Note out of range (error code $28).","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3894": {"comment":"Report m"},
        "3898": {"synopsis":"o Too many tied notes (error code $2A).","comment":"PLAY_SILENCE first"},
        "3902": {"comment":"Report o"},
        "3906": {"synopsis":"Starts every string's note that has not ended: its name read (PLAY_NOTE_NAME); not a rest:\nsounded (PLAY_SOUND), the volume set (AY channels A-C) and MIDI's note on (MIDI_NOTE_ON).","comment":"PLAY_LIST_INIT: from the first string"},
        "3909": {"synopsis":"The next string.","comment":"This string ended?"},
        "3915": {"comment":"PLAY_BLOCK: IX = its block"},
        "3918": {"comment":"PLAY_NOTE_NAME: A = the note"},
        "3921": {"comment":"A rest?"},
        "3925": {"comment":"PLAY_SOUND"},
        "3928": {"comment":"AY channels A-C only"},
        "3935": {"comment":"D = 8 + the number: its volume register"},
        "3939": {"comment":"E = the volume"},
        "3945": {"synopsis":"MIDI's note on.","comment":"MIDI_NOTE_ON"},
        "3948": {"synopsis":"The next string's bit.","comment":"The next string's bit: past the last?"},
        "3953": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT: the next block"},
        "3958": {"synopsis":"Waits DE units, each the tempo's delay (IY + 39) less 100 rounds."},
        "3959": {"comment":"HL = the tempo's delay"},
        "3965": {"comment":"Less 100"},
        "3971": {"comment":"BC = the rounds"},
        "3974": {"synopsis":"One round.","comment":"One round: all done?"},
        "3979": {"comment":"One unit less: any left?"},
        "3985": {"synopsis":"The shortest current length among the strings that have not ended, into IY + 37.","comment":"DE = the shortest so far: $FFFF"},
        "3988": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_TOP: HL = the strings' length pointers"},
        "3991": {"synopsis":"The next string.","comment":"This string ended?"},
        "3997": {"comment":"The shortest so far kept"},
        "3998": {"comment":"HL = the string's pointer to its length"},
        "4002": {"comment":"DE = its current length"},
        "4005": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "4007": {"comment":"BC = the shortest so far"},
        "4008": {"comment":"Shorter? Then DE is the new shortest"},
        "4013": {"comment":"No: DE = the shortest again"},
        "4015": {"synopsis":"On.","comment":"The next string's bit: past the last?"},
        "4021": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT: the next block"},
        "4026": {"synopsis":"Kept.","comment":"The shortest at IY + 37"},
        "4033": {"synopsis":"After the wait: each string's current length less the time waited; one at 0 ends its note\n(volume 0, MIDI_NOTE_OFF) and goes on to its next tied length or, with none left, its next\nnote (PLAY_NEXT), which is started (PLAY_SOUND) and marked in IY + 42; then a short wait,\nand the new notes' volumes and MIDI note on.","comment":"No new notes yet (IY + 42)"},
        "4037": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_INIT: from the first string"},
        "4040": {"synopsis":"The next string.","comment":"This string ended?"},
        "4047": {"comment":"PLAY_BLOCK: IX = its block"},
        "4050": {"comment":"HL = IY + 17 + 2 x its number: its pointer"},
        "4065": {"comment":"HL = its current length's place"},
        "4069": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4070": {"comment":"HL = the length"},
        "4074": {"comment":"DE = the time waited"},
        "4080": {"comment":"HL = what is left"},
        "4083": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "4084": {"comment":"HL = the length's place"},
        "4085": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "4087": {"comment":"No: the rest stored"},
        "4092": {"synopsis":"Its length is over: volume 0, MIDI's note off.","comment":"AY channels A-C only"},
        "4099": {"comment":"Its volume register = 0"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Another tied length?","comment":"MIDI_NOTE_OFF"},
        "4111": {"comment":"HL = IX + 33: the lengths left"},
        "4118": {"comment":"One fewer: any left?"},
        "4121": {"comment":"None: PLAY_NEXT reads the next note"},
        "4124": {"comment":"Has the string ended?"},
        "4132": {"comment":"No: the new note"},
        "4134": {"synopsis":"The next length in its list.","comment":"HL = the string's pointer in IY + 17"},
        "4149": {"comment":"DE = it + 2: the next length"},
        "4154": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "4157": {"synopsis":"A new note: read and sounded, marked in IY + 42.","comment":"PLAY_NOTE_NAME: A = the note"},
        "4160": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "4161": {"comment":"Has the string ended?"},
        "4169": {"comment":"A rest?"},
        "4174": {"comment":"PLAY_SOUND"},
        "4177": {"comment":"Its bit into IY + 42: a volume to set"},
        "4186": {"synopsis":"The next string.","comment":"The next string's bit: past the last?"},
        "4192": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT: the next block"},
        "4198": {"synopsis":"A short wait (1 unit), then each new note's volume and MIDI's note on.","comment":"PLAY_WAIT: one unit"},
        "4204": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_INIT: from the first string"},
        "4207": {"synopsis":"The next string.","comment":"A new note on this string?"},
        "4213": {"comment":"PLAY_BLOCK: IX = its block"},
        "4216": {"comment":"AY channels A-C only"},
        "4223": {"comment":"D = 8 + the number: its volume register"},
        "4227": {"comment":"E = the volume"},
        "4233": {"synopsis":"MIDI's note on.","comment":"MIDI_NOTE_ON"},
        "4236": {"synopsis":"On.","comment":"The next string's bit: past the last?"},
        "4241": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT: the next block"},
        "4246": {"synopsis":"The AY tone periods for notes 21 up (note 21 first, $0FBF, the period notes below 21 also\nget; note 22's is $0EDC), one word each; note 60's is $01A8."},
        "4462": {"synopsis":"A MIDI note on for the string, when it has a MIDI channel: $90 + the channel, the note, the\nvelocity (the volume x 8, bit 4 cleared), each through MIDI_OUT.","comment":"A MIDI channel (bit 7 clear)?"},
        "4467": {"comment":"$90 + the channel: note on"},
        "4472": {"comment":"The note"},
        "4478": {"comment":"The velocity: the volume, bit 4 off, x 8"},
        "4493": {"synopsis":"A MIDI note off for the string, when it has a MIDI channel: $80 + the channel, the note,\n$40.","comment":"A MIDI channel (bit 7 clear)?"},
        "4498": {"comment":"$80 + the channel: note off"},
        "4503": {"comment":"The note"},
        "4509": {"comment":"The velocity $40"},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"Sends byte A out of the AY's I/O port A (register 14), one bit at a time with fixed delays:\na start bit ($FA), the eight bits low first ($FE for a 1, $FA for a 0), a stop bit ($FE).\nVector $011E.","comment":"L = the byte"},
        "4516": {"comment":"Register 14: I/O port A"},
        "4523": {"comment":"The start bit"},
        "4530": {"comment":"Its time"},
        "4532": {"synopsis":"The start bit's time."},
        "4539": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4540": {"comment":"D = 8 bits"},
        "4542": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"The next bit into carry"},
        "4543": {"comment":"The rest kept in L"},
        "4544": {"comment":"A 0?"},
        "4547": {"comment":"A 1: $FE"},
        "4553": {"synopsis":"A 0.","comment":"A 0: $FA"},
        "4557": {"comment":"Takes the 1's JR time"},
        "4559": {"synopsis":"The bit's time.","comment":"E = the bit's delay"},
        "4561": {"synopsis":"Waiting."},
        "4564": {"comment":"Padding to the bit's length"},
        "4567": {"comment":"A = the bits left"},
        "4568": {"comment":"Another bit?"},
        "4571": {"comment":"Padding before the stop bit"},
        "4577": {"comment":"The stop bit"},
        "4581": {"comment":"Its time"},
        "4583": {"synopsis":"The stop bit's time."},
        "4587": {"synopsis":"SAVE (CLASS_B): $5B66 bit 5 set, then TAPE_BANG."},
        "4590": {"comment":"Bit 5: SAVE"},
        "4594": {"synopsis":"LOAD: $5B66 bit 4 set, then TAPE_BANG."},
        "4597": {"comment":"Bit 4: LOAD"},
        "4601": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: $5B66 bit 7 set, then TAPE_BANG."},
        "4604": {"comment":"Bit 7: VERIFY"},
        "4608": {"synopsis":"MERGE: $5B66 bit 6 set, then TAPE_BANG."},
        "4611": {"comment":"Bit 6: MERGE"},
        "4613": {"synopsis":"The four tape commands: $5B66 bit 3 set and the '!' passed when one follows the keyword (the\nRAM disk); then TAPE_COMMAND.","comment":"Bit 3 (the RAM disk) off for now"},
        "4618": {"comment":"The character after the keyword"},
        "4619": {"comment":"A '!'?"},
        "4624": {"synopsis":"'!': the RAM disk.","comment":"Bit 3: the RAM disk"},
        "4629": {"comment":"Past the '!'"},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\").","comment":"Report C"},
        "4637": {"synopsis":"SAVE !, LOAD !, VERIFY ! and MERGE ! (SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD with $5B66 bit 3 set), from the header\nTAPE_COMMAND made at IX and HL (the start):\n1. $5B71 on: the type, the length ($5B72), the start ($5B74), the third word ($5B78, a\n   program's auto-run line) and the fourth ($5B76, a program's own length; an array's name\n   byte); the name to $5B67.\n2. SAVE: RAMDISK_SAVE.\n3. Otherwise the wanted header is kept at $5B7A and the file's read to $5B71\n   (RAMDISK_LOAD_HDR); another type is report b. CODE: RD_CODE; a program or an array: MERGE\n   to RD_MERGE, LOAD to RD_LOAD_PROG, VERIFY to RD_CODE as well.\nObserved: merge !\"c\" and load !\"c\" of a CODE file gave b Wrong file type.","comment":"The start"},
        "4640": {"comment":"The type"},
        "4646": {"comment":"The length"},
        "4655": {"comment":"The third word"},
        "4661": {"synopsis":"The fourth word."},
        "4664": {"comment":"The fourth word"},
        "4673": {"comment":"A program or CODE: as it is"},
        "4680": {"comment":"An array: its name byte"},
        "4686": {"synopsis":"The name to $5B67; SAVE goes to RAMDISK_SAVE."},
        "4689": {"comment":"The name to $5B67"},
        "4701": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "4706": {"comment":"The wanted header kept at $5B7A"},
        "4717": {"comment":"The file's header to $5B71"},
        "4720": {"comment":"B = the type asked for"},
        "4727": {"comment":"The type wanted?"},
        "4730": {"comment":"CODE"},
        "4734": {"comment":"Below 3: a program or an array"},
        "4736": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1D (report b, \"Wrong file type\")."},
        "4740": {"synopsis":"A program or an array: MERGE, LOAD or VERIFY.","comment":"A = the command's bits"},
        "4743": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "4747": {"comment":"VERIFY? Not: LOAD"},
        "4752": {"synopsis":"CODE (and VERIFY of anything): MERGE is report a; a wanted length that is shorter than the\nfile's is report c; the data is read to the wanted start, else the file's, or PROG for a\nprogram. VERIFY therefore reads the data in place; it does not compare it.\nObserved: load !\"c\"code 32768,5 of a 10-byte file gave c CODE error; verify !\"c\"code 32768\nput the file's bytes at 32768.","comment":"MERGE of CODE?"},
        "4759": {"comment":"MERGE: report a"},
        "4763": {"comment":"The wanted length","synopsis":"The wanted length against the file's."},
        "4766": {"comment":"DE = the file's length"},
        "4770": {"comment":"0: any"},
        "4774": {"comment":"Shorter than the file's?"},
        "4778": {"comment":"Shorter: report c"},
        "4782": {"synopsis":"HL = the wanted start, or the file's.","comment":"HL = the wanted start"},
        "4785": {"comment":"0: none given?"},
        "4789": {"comment":"Then the file's"},
        "4792": {"synopsis":"A program: to PROG.","comment":"A program?"},
        "4798": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "4801": {"synopsis":"The data read (RD_READ).","comment":"RD_READ: the file's length to HL"},
        "4805": {"synopsis":"MERGE !: room in the workspace for the program and an $80 after it (ROM 1's WORK_ROOM), the\nprogram read there, then ROM 1's MERGE_LOAD from $08CE puts its lines and variables into\nplace.","comment":"BC = the program's length, kept"},
        "4810": {"comment":"+ 1 for the $80"},
        "4811": {"comment":"ROM 1's WORK_ROOM: the room"},
        "4814": {"comment":"$80 in its last byte"},
        "4816": {"comment":"HL = the room's start"},
        "4817": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "4818": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "4819": {"comment":"RD_READ: the program into it"},
        "4822": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "4823": {"comment":"ROM 1's MERGE_LOAD ($08CE): the lines and variables merged"},
        "4827": {"synopsis":"LOAD ! of a program or an array: the room is checked first (ROM 1's TEST_ROOM, the length +\n5; for an array that is there already, only what it needs beyond its old size); then a\nprogram goes to RD_LOAD_PROGRAM and an array to RD_LOAD_ARRAY.","comment":"DE = the file's length"},
        "4831": {"comment":"HL = the wanted start: 0 for a program or a new array"},
        "4834": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4835": {"comment":"0?"},
        "4839": {"comment":"+ 3 (the name and length bytes)"},
        "4842": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "4845": {"synopsis":"An existing array: only the difference.","comment":"HL = the old array's length"},
        "4848": {"comment":"HL = the file's, DE = the old"},
        "4849": {"comment":"Not longer than the old: no test"},
        "4854": {"synopsis":"The room tested (ROM 1's TEST_ROOM).","comment":"+ 5"},
        "4858": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "4860": {"comment":"ROM 1's TEST_ROOM: report 4 when it does not fit"},
        "4863": {"synopsis":"A program, or an array: the old one removed (ROM 1's RECLAIM), room made at E_LINE - 1 (ROM\n1's MAKE_ROOM), its name byte and length written, the data read.","comment":"HL = the wanted start"},
        "4864": {"comment":"A program?"},
        "4870": {"comment":"A new array?"},
        "4874": {"comment":"BC = the old array's length"},
        "4878": {"comment":"HL = its name byte"},
        "4879": {"comment":"+ 3: its name and length too"},
        "4882": {"comment":"ROM 1's RECLAIM: the old array removed"},
        "4885": {"synopsis":"The new array's room before E_LINE.","comment":"HL = E_LINE - 1"},
        "4889": {"comment":"BC = the file's length, kept"},
        "4894": {"comment":"+ 3"},
        "4897": {"comment":"A = the array's name byte"},
        "4901": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "4904": {"comment":"HL = the room's first byte"},
        "4905": {"comment":"The name byte"},
        "4907": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "4908": {"comment":"After it"},
        "4912": {"comment":"HL = the data's place"},
        "4913": {"synopsis":"The data read (RD_READ).","comment":"RD_READ: DE bytes to HL"},
        "4917": {"synopsis":"A program: the old program and variables removed (ROM 1's RECLAIM_DE_HL), room made at PROG\nfor the new (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM), VARS = PROG + its own length; an auto-run line (one whose\ntop two bits are clear) goes into NEWPPC with NSPPC = 0 and $5B66 bit 1 set; DATADD = PROG -\n1; then the data read.","comment":"No auto-run yet ($5B66 bit 1)"},
        "4922": {"comment":"DE = PROG, HL = E_LINE - 1"},
        "4930": {"comment":"ROM 1's RECLAIM_DE_HL: the old program and variables gone"},
        "4933": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "4937": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "4940": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM: the room at PROG"},
        "4943": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "4944": {"comment":"VARS = PROG + the program's own length"},
        "4952": {"comment":"H = the auto-run line's high byte"},
        "4956": {"comment":"Top two bits set: no auto-run"},
        "4960": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "4964": {"comment":"NEWPPC = it"},
        "4967": {"comment":"NSPPC = 0"},
        "4971": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 1: a line to run"},
        "4976": {"synopsis":"DATADD, and the program read.","comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "4979": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "4983": {"comment":"DATADD = PROG - 1"},
        "4988": {"comment":"RD_LOAD_DATA"},
        "4990": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes of the open file to HL (RAMDISK_LOAD); none when DE is 0.","comment":"Nothing to read?"},
        "4993": {"comment":"RAMDISK_LOAD"},
        "4997": {"synopsis":"A string expression (ROM 1's CLASS_A); when running it is taken off the stack (ROM 1's\nSTK_FETCH: DE its start, BC its length). Exit: Z when checking. Keeps AF.","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A: a string expression"},
        "5000": {"comment":"Checking only?"},
        "5005": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "5006": {"comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH: DE = the start, BC = the length"},
        "5011": {"synopsis":"The name after the next character (ERASE !): STRING_NAME; when running it must be 1-10\ncharacters (report f otherwise) and goes to $5B67, padded with spaces.","comment":"Past the '!'"},
        "5012": {"comment":"STRING_NAME"},
        "5015": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "5016": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "5017": {"comment":"Empty: report f"},
        "5021": {"comment":"Over 10: report f"},
        "5028": {"comment":"The name's start and length kept"},
        "5030": {"comment":"$5B67's 10 bytes"},
        "5035": {"comment":"A = a space"},
        "5037": {"synopsis":"$5B67 filled with spaces."},
        "5041": {"comment":"BC = the length, HL = the name"},
        "5043": {"comment":"Copied to $5B67"},
        "5048": {"comment":"A back"},
        "5050": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $21 (report f, \"Invalid name\").","comment":"Report f"},
        "5054": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (CLASS_B; T_ADDR's low byte tells which: 0 SAVE, 1 LOAD, 2\nVERIFY, 3 MERGE): the 48K ROM's TAPE_COMMAND, the same steps with ROM 1's routines:\n1. The name (a string, ROM 1's CLASS_A) into a 17-byte header in the workspace (34 for the\n   others: the second 17 take the header read), its first byte $FF for no name; for SAVE an\n   empty name, or one longer than 10, is report F; for the others an empty name keeps $FF\n   and a longer one is cut to 10.\n2. DATA, SCREEN$, CODE or LINE / nothing (a program) fill in the type, length, start and the\n   rest (SE_KIND on).\n3. SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD: with '!' the RAM disk (RD_COMMAND); SAVE ROM 1's SAVE_CONTROL; the\n   others ROM 1's SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD at $0761.\nObserved: save \"t\" printed Start tape, then press any key.","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A: the name"},
        "5057": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "5063": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "5066": {"comment":"T_ADDR's low byte: 0, SAVE?"},
        "5072": {"comment":"34 for the others"},
        "5074": {"synopsis":"The header's room (ROM 1's WORK_ROOM), IX at it.","comment":"ROM 1's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "5078": {"comment":"IX = the header"},
        "5080": {"comment":"11 spaces: the type and the name"},
        "5084": {"synopsis":"The name filled with spaces; its first byte $FF (no name)."},
        "5088": {"comment":"The name's first byte $FF: no name yet"},
        "5092": {"comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "5095": {"comment":"Carry when the length is 0 or over 10"},
        "5103": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "5109": {"comment":"SAVE: an empty or long name is report F"},
        "5113": {"synopsis":"Not SAVE: an empty name keeps $FF; a longer one is cut to 10. (For SAVE either is report F,\njust before.)","comment":"Empty: nothing copied"},
        "5117": {"comment":"Long: the first 10 characters"},
        "5120": {"synopsis":"The name copied after the type byte.","comment":"DE = IX + 1, HL = the name"},
        "5125": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "5127": {"synopsis":"What follows the name: DATA, SCREEN$, CODE, or else a program.","comment":"The character after the name"},
        "5128": {"comment":"DATA?"},
        "5135": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "5140": {"comment":"Past DATA"},
        "5141": {"comment":"The array (ROM 1's LOOK_VARS)"},
        "5144": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "5146": {"comment":"HL = 0: a new array"},
        "5149": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "5155": {"comment":"Then C bit 7 set as well"},
        "5157": {"synopsis":"A new array: only LOAD may make one (report 2 otherwise).","comment":"LOAD?"},
        "5163": {"comment":"Report 2"},
        "5167": {"synopsis":"The array must be followed by '(' (report C); its length and name into the header.","comment":"NZ: report C"},
        "5170": {"comment":"Checking only?"},
        "5176": {"comment":"C = the array's name byte"},
        "5177": {"comment":"Its length into the header (IX + 11)"},
        "5188": {"synopsis":"The array's name byte at IX + 14.","comment":"The name byte at IX + 14"},
        "5191": {"comment":"A = 1: numbers"},
        "5193": {"comment":"A string array (bit 6)?"},
        "5197": {"comment":"2: strings"},
        "5198": {"synopsis":"Type 1 (numbers) or 2 (strings, C bit 6).","comment":"The type"},
        "5201": {"synopsis":"Past ')', the statement ends.","comment":"The array's place kept in DE"},
        "5202": {"comment":"The next: ')'? (report C otherwise)"},
        "5207": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "5208": {"comment":"STATEMENT_END: checking ends here"},
        "5211": {"comment":"HL = the array's data (0 for a new one)"},
        "5212": {"comment":"SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD"},
        "5215": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$: 6912 ($1B00) bytes from $4000, type 3. Not for MERGE.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "5219": {"comment":"Not for MERGE (report C)"},
        "5227": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "5228": {"comment":"STATEMENT_END"},
        "5231": {"comment":"The length $1B00"},
        "5239": {"comment":"The start $4000"},
        "5248": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "5250": {"synopsis":"CODE: start and length; SAVE needs both; for the others a missing one is 0, taken from the\nfile. Not for MERGE.","comment":"CODE?"},
        "5254": {"comment":"Not for MERGE (report C)"},
        "5262": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "5263": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_END_Z2: ENTER or ':' next?"},
        "5266": {"comment":"No: a start follows"},
        "5268": {"comment":"SAVE needs one (report C)"},
        "5275": {"comment":"ROM 1's USE_ZERO: the start 0"},
        "5278": {"comment":"And the length 0"},
        "5280": {"synopsis":"The start (ROM 1's CLASS_6).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the start"},
        "5283": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "5288": {"comment":"No length: SAVE needs one (report C)"},
        "5295": {"synopsis":"No length: 0.","comment":"ROM 1's USE_ZERO: the length 0"},
        "5300": {"synopsis":"',' and the length.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "5301": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the length"},
        "5304": {"synopsis":"The length and start into the header (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD twice); HL = the start.","comment":"STATEMENT_END: checking ends here"},
        "5307": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_WORD: BC = the length"},
        "5310": {"comment":"Into IX + 11"},
        "5316": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_WORD: BC = the start"},
        "5319": {"comment":"Into IX + 13"},
        "5325": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "5327": {"synopsis":"Type 3, then SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD.","comment":"Type 3: CODE"},
        "5331": {"comment":"SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD"},
        "5333": {"synopsis":"A program: LINE (SAVE only) or nothing; without LINE the header's line is $80xx (no\nauto-run).","comment":"LINE?"},
        "5337": {"comment":"STATEMENT_END: checking ends here"},
        "5340": {"comment":"IX + 14 = $80: no auto-run line"},
        "5344": {"comment":"The header's program fields"},
        "5346": {"synopsis":"LINE n: the auto-run line into the header (SAVE only, else report C).","comment":"Not SAVE: report C"},
        "5353": {"comment":"Past LINE"},
        "5354": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the line"},
        "5357": {"comment":"STATEMENT_END: checking ends here"},
        "5360": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_WORD: BC = the line"},
        "5363": {"comment":"Into IX + 13"},
        "5369": {"synopsis":"Type 0: the length (E_LINE - PROG - 1, the program and its variables) and the program's own\nlength (VARS - PROG) into the header; HL = PROG.","comment":"Type 0: a program"},
        "5373": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE, DE = PROG"},
        "5380": {"comment":"The length: E_LINE - PROG - 1"},
        "5383": {"comment":"Into IX + 11"},
        "5389": {"comment":"VARS - PROG: the program alone"},
        "5394": {"comment":"Into IX + 15"},
        "5400": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "5401": {"synopsis":"With '!' ($5B66 bit 3) the RAM disk (RD_COMMAND); otherwise SAVE: ROM 1's SAVE_CONTROL, and\nthe others ROM 1's SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD from $0761 (with HL the destination).","comment":"'!': the RAM disk?"},
        "5409": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "5415": {"comment":"ROM 1's SAVE_CONTROL"},
        "5419": {"synopsis":"LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE from tape: ROM 1's.","comment":"ROM 1's tape LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE ($0761)"},
        "5423": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the editing rows from the program and draws them; the cursor goes to E_PPC's line\nwhen it is among them. An editing row is 35 bytes ($EC16 + 35 x row): 32 characters (0 an\nempty cell), a flags byte (bit 0: the first row of a line, bit 3: its last), then the line's\nnumber, high byte first. The rows above the screen are kept at $F9DB (a count, then the\nrows), those below at $F6F5; $FC9A is the number of the line the rows above belong to.\n1. $EEF5 bit 0 cleared, bit 1 set (E_PPC's line looked for); when E_PPC is 0, $EC06 = 0.\n2. The rows above are made again: both buffers emptied ($3222, $30D6), $F9D7 = the line\n   before $FC9A ($334A), then as many rows as were above taken from the program ($30DF) and\n   put back above ($326A).\n3. Rows 0 to $EC15 filled with the next rows ($30DF). In E_PPC's first row (flags bit 0, the\n   number matching) the search succeeds ($EEF5 bit 0); from there the cursor moves $EC06\n   places on through the line's characters, row by row, and is stored (CURSOR_STORE) at the\n   row and column reached, no further than a row's last character ($2E63); $EEF5 = 0 then.\n4. E_PPC not found: $FC9A = E_PPC and the rows above emptied, so that its line comes at the\n   top (when E_PPC is 0: $FC9A = 0 and E_PPC = the program's first line, $3352); then the\n   whole again from ROWS_REBUILD_GO.\n5. The rows drawn (ROWS_DRAW).\nExit: Z.","comment":"$EEF5: E_PPC's line not found yet, looked for"},
        "5430": {"synopsis":"Again from here (RB_AGAIN), with E_PPC changed.","comment":"E_PPC 0?"},
        "5437": {"comment":"Then no places to move the cursor on"},
        "5440": {"synopsis":"The count of rows above the screen kept; $F9D7 = the line before $FC9A; both buffers\nemptied.","comment":"A = how many rows were above the screen"},
        "5444": {"comment":"$F9D7 = the line before $FC9A: rows are taken from the line after it"},
        "5453": {"comment":"The rows above and below emptied"},
        "5459": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "5460": {"synopsis":"One row from the program put back above the screen, until the count is used up.","comment":"None left?"},
        "5464": {"comment":"The next row from the program "},
        "5468": {"comment":"... above the screen"},
        "5472": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "5475": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15: B = the row, C = $EC15, DE = the row's place; the first two kept on the\nstack.","comment":"C = row 0"},
        "5477": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS: DE = row 0's place"},
        "5480": {"comment":"B = row 0"},
        "5481": {"comment":"C = $EC15: the last row"},
        "5485": {"comment":"Both kept"},
        "5487": {"synopsis":"One row: the next from the program ($30DF); while E_PPC is looked for, is this E_PPC's first\nrow?","comment":"HL = the next row from the program"},
        "5490": {"comment":"E_PPC's line still looked for?"},
        "5499": {"comment":"The row's flags byte"},
        "5503": {"comment":"The first row of a line?"},
        "5507": {"comment":"DE = its line number"},
        "5515": {"comment":"E_PPC's?"},
        "5519": {"comment":"Found"},
        "5524": {"synopsis":"Not E_PPC's first row."},
        "5526": {"synopsis":"The row copied into the editing rows (35 bytes); DE = the next row's place.","comment":"The row copied in"},
        "5535": {"comment":"The next row's place kept"},
        "5537": {"comment":"DE = the row copied from (for TEXT_FROM_COL)"},
        "5538": {"comment":"In E_PPC's line?"},
        "5545": {"comment":"B = column 0"},
        "5547": {"synopsis":"The cursor $EC06 places on: while there are places left and the row has a character at or\nafter column B ($2E41), one more column.","comment":"Places left?"},
        "5555": {"comment":"Anything at or after column B?"},
        "5561": {"comment":"One place used: one column on"},
        "5568": {"synopsis":"No places left: past the row's last character, B goes back to just after it ($2E63); the\nsearch ends ($EEF5 = 0)."},
        "5571": {"comment":"Nothing from column B on: back to the last character"},
        "5574": {"comment":"The search ends"},
        "5579": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored at this row, column B, remembered column B (CURSOR_STORE).","comment":"A = the column"},
        "5580": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "5584": {"comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "5587": {"synopsis":"The next row, up to $EC15.","comment":"B = the row, C = the last row"},
        "5589": {"comment":"A = $EC15, the last row"},
        "5594": {"comment":"Still looked for "},
        "5601": {"comment":"... and not found?"},
        "5605": {"comment":"E_PPC 0?"},
        "5612": {"comment":"$FC9A = E_PPC, nothing above: its line at the top"},
        "5620": {"synopsis":"E_PPC 0: $FC9A = 0, and E_PPC = the program's first line ($3352).","comment":"$FC9A = 0"},
        "5623": {"comment":"NEXT_LINE_NUM: HL = the program's first line"},
        "5626": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "5629": {"synopsis":"Again (ROWS_REBUILD_GO).","comment":"The stack tidied"},
        "5631": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD_GO"},
        "5634": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15 drawn (ROWS_DRAW, with Z).","comment":"The kept rows dropped"},
        "5636": {"comment":"Z"},
        "5637": {"synopsis":"Draws editing rows B to C on the screen, each through $3604 (which draws nothing while $EEF5\nbit 2 is set). With NZ on entry the cursor would then be moved $EC06 places on ($2B78 each)\nand stored (CURSOR_STORE); both callers (RB_DRAW and $3008) enter with Z, so that part\n($161B-$162E) is never run.\nEntry: B = the first row, C = the last, F's Z flag as above.\nExit: Z; HL = the place after the last row drawn.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "5638": {"comment":"A = the last row C, C = the first row B"},
        "5640": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS: DE = the first row's place"},
        "5643": {"comment":"HL = row C's place"},
        "5644": {"synopsis":"One row drawn ($3604); the next, up to A."},
        "5645": {"comment":"SHOW_ROW: the row drawn"},
        "5649": {"comment":"HL = the next row's place"},
        "5653": {"comment":"The next row: past the last?"},
        "5657": {"comment":"Z: done"},
        "5659": {"comment":"The cursor "},
        "5662": {"synopsis":"One place on ($2B78), $EC06 times, then the cursor stored.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: one place on"},
        "5665": {"comment":"One place fewer: none left?"},
        "5676": {"comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "5679": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "5680": {"synopsis":"Clears editing rows 0 to $EC15 on the screen ($3B5E).\nExit: through $3B5E.","comment":"B = row 0"},
        "5682": {"comment":"D = $EC15: the last row"},
        "5686": {"comment":"CLEAR_LINES"},
        "5689": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows up by one: row 0 goes to the rows above the screen ($326A; when\nthere is no room there, nothing is done), the next row from the program ($30DF) comes in at\nrow $EC15 (ROWS_UP_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled; HL kept when not.","comment":"B = row 0"},
        "5691": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5692": {"comment":"C = row 0"},
        "5693": {"comment":"DE = row 0's place"},
        "5696": {"comment":"Row 0 above the screen: no room?"},
        "5699": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5701": {"comment":"HL = the next row from the program"},
        "5704": {"synopsis":"Rows B+1 to $EC15 moved up by one into rows B to $EC15 - 1, the screen scrolled the same way\n($3618), and the row at HL copied into row $EC15. $2FB9 jumps here.\nEntry: B = the row that goes, DE = its place, HL = the row that comes in at the bottom.\nExit: carry. Keeps BC."},
        "5705": {"comment":"The incoming row kept"},
        "5706": {"comment":"HL = row B + 1's place"},
        "5710": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "5714": {"comment":"Only the last row?"},
        "5717": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5718": {"synopsis":"One row up."},
        "5719": {"comment":"One row moved up"},
        "5725": {"comment":"Up to the last row?"},
        "5731": {"synopsis":"The screen scrolled up ($3618); the new row into the last row.","comment":"HL = the incoming row"},
        "5732": {"comment":"The screen's rows B to C scrolled up"},
        "5735": {"comment":"The new row in"},
        "5740": {"comment":"Carry: scrolled"},
        "5743": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows down by one: the last row above the screen comes back ($322B; when\nthere is none, nothing is done) and goes in at row 0 (ROWS_DOWN_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled.","comment":"B = row 0"},
        "5745": {"comment":"HL = the last row above the screen: none?"},
        "5749": {"synopsis":"Row $EC15 goes to the rows below the screen ($311E; when there is no room there, nothing is\ndone), rows B to $EC15 - 1 move down by one, the screen is scrolled the same way ($362C),\nand the row at HL is copied into row B. $2EDB comes here to put in a blank row.\nEntry: B = the row, HL = the row that comes in.\nExit: carry when done. Keeps BC.","comment":"BC and the incoming row kept"},
        "5751": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "5755": {"comment":"DE = the last row's place"},
        "5758": {"comment":"The last row below the screen: no room?"},
        "5763": {"comment":"DE = the end of the last row, HL = the end of the row before"},
        "5769": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5771": {"comment":"Only the last row?"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"One row down (copied from its end)."},
        "5775": {"comment":"One row moved down"},
        "5781": {"comment":"Down to row B?"},
        "5786": {"synopsis":"DE = row B's place; the screen scrolled down ($362C); the new row into row B.","comment":"DE = row B's place"},
        "5788": {"comment":"B = the row, HL = the incoming row"},
        "5790": {"comment":"The screen's rows B to C scrolled down"},
        "5793": {"comment":"The new row in"},
        "5798": {"comment":"Carry: scrolled"},
        "5801": {"synopsis":"No room below: no carry.","comment":"The stack tidied; no carry"},
        "5804": {"synopsis":"Puts character A in column B of the row at DE, moving columns B to 30 one to the right.\nExit: A = E = the character pushed out of column 31; Z when that was 0 (an empty cell); HL =\nthe row's flags byte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "5809": {"comment":"D = the character carried"},
        "5810": {"comment":"A = column B"},
        "5811": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried, up to column 31.","comment":"This column's character out, the carried one in"},
        "5814": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "5815": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "5820": {"comment":"The character pushed out: 0?"},
        "5825": {"synopsis":"Takes the character in column B out of the row at DE, moving columns B+1 to 31 one to the\nleft; character A comes in at column 31.\nExit: A = E = the character taken out; Z when it was 0 (an empty cell); HL = the row's flags\nbyte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"The row kept"},
        "5826": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte, kept"},
        "5830": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5831": {"comment":"D = the character coming in"},
        "5832": {"comment":"From column 31 down"},
        "5836": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried; column B ends it.","comment":"This column's character out, the carried one in"},
        "5839": {"comment":"Column B?"},
        "5842": {"comment":"One column to the left"},
        "5843": {"synopsis":"One column to the left."},
        "5846": {"synopsis":"Column B's character in A; Z when it was 0.","comment":"A = column B's character: 0?"},
        "5849": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "5852": {"synopsis":"Syntax offsets: 50 bytes, one for each command keyword in token order, $CE (DEF FN) to $FF\n(COPY); each is a relative pointer (this byte's address plus its value) to the keyword's\nentry in SYNTAX_ENTRIES. SPECTRUM and PLAY have none: STMT_START finds theirs at $17A9 and\n$17AC."},
        "5902": {"synopsis":"Each command's syntax entry: items read one by one by SYNTAX_ITEM: a character or token the\nline must have next, or an operand class below $20 (CLASS_TABLE). Classes 0, 3 and 5 are\nfollowed by the address of a routine in ROM 1, classes $0C, $0D and $0E by one in this ROM;\nclasses 2, 7 and $0B end an entry with no address. Several entries share their tails.\nRoutines in ROM 1: GO TO, STOP, NEXT, POKE, RANDOMIZE, CONTINUE, CLS, PLOT, PAUSE, RESTORE,\nBEEP, INK to OUT, BORDER, OPEN # and CLOSE #; in this ROM: IF $1967, GO SUB $1A53, RETURN\n$1A6F, FOR $1981, PRINT $2178, INPUT $218C, DIM $21D5, REM $1862, NEW $21AA, RUN $1A02, LIST\n$1B75, CLEAR $1A0D, READ $19AB, DATA $19EB, DRAW $21BE, COPY $21A7, LPRINT $2174, LLIST\n$1B71, CIRCLE $21AE, DEF FN $1A8C, FORMAT $0641, MOVE $1AF0, ERASE $1C0C, CAT $1BE5,\nSPECTRUM $1B2B (at $17A9), PLAY $2317 (at $17AC); SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE through class\n$0B."},
        "6063": {"synopsis":"Checks the edit line's syntax (vector $0100; LINE_ENTER comes here): FLAGS bit 7 cleared\n(check, do not run), the line number read (ROM 1's EDIT_LINE_NO), SUBPPC = 0, ERR_NR = $FF,\nthen the statements one by one (STMT_START). A syntax error raises its report.","comment":"Checking, not running"},
        "6067": {"comment":"Past the line number"},
        "6070": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 0"},
        "6074": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF"},
        "6080": {"synopsis":"The statement loop: past the ':' (or THEN) to the next statement."},
        "6081": {"synopsis":"One statement, checked or run (FLAGS bit 7):\n1. The workspace and the calculator stack emptied (ROM 1's CLEAR_WS), SUBPPC + 1 (128\n   statements is report C).\n2. ENTER ends the line (LINE_END); another ':' is an empty statement.\n3. STMT_RET stacked as the return; the command's keyword: $CE-$FF through SYNTAX_OFFSETS,\n   $A3 (SPECTRUM) and $A4 (PLAY) their own entries; anything else is report C. Its entry is\n   read by SYNTAX_ITEM.\nObserved: print 1:: print 4 printed 1 and 4 and reported 0:3.","comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_WS"},
        "6084": {"comment":"SUBPPC + 1"},
        "6087": {"comment":"128 statements: report C"},
        "6090": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "6093": {"comment":"ENTER: the end of the line"},
        "6098": {"comment":"':': an empty statement"},
        "6102": {"comment":"STMT_RET: where the command returns"},
        "6106": {"comment":"C = the keyword"},
        "6107": {"comment":"Past the keyword"},
        "6108": {"comment":"A = the keyword"},
        "6109": {"comment":"$CE and up?"},
        "6113": {"comment":"Below $CE: A back to the keyword"},
        "6115": {"comment":"SPECTRUM's entry"},
        "6122": {"comment":"PLAY's entry"},
        "6129": {"comment":"Not a command: report C"},
        "6132": {"synopsis":"A keyword from $CE: its entry from SYNTAX_OFFSETS.","comment":"BC = the keyword - $CE"},
        "6133": {"comment":"HL = its offset byte"},
        "6137": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "6138": {"comment":"HL = its entry"},
        "6141": {"synopsis":"SYNTAX_ITEM again from T_ADDR: the return address every item leaves.","comment":"HL = the place in the syntax entry (T_ADDR)"},
        "6144": {"synopsis":"Reads the entry's next item at HL, T_ADDR following it: below $20 an operand class, its\nroutine from CLASS_TABLE entered with A = the line's current character, NZ, and SYNTAX_NEXT\nas its return; otherwise a character the line must have next (SYNTAX_CHAR).","comment":"A = the item"},
        "6145": {"comment":"T_ADDR past it"},
        "6149": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT as the return"},
        "6153": {"comment":"C = the item, BC its offset in CLASS_TABLE"},
        "6154": {"comment":"A character?"},
        "6158": {"comment":"The class's routine from CLASS_TABLE"},
        "6166": {"comment":"Its address as the return"},
        "6167": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "6168": {"comment":"B = $FF: NZ"},
        "6170": {"synopsis":"The character or keyword (in C) must be the line's next, else report C; then past it.","comment":"Is the current character the one asked for?"},
        "6172": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "6175": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6177": {"synopsis":"Where a command returns to: BREAK_KEY first (it raises report L itself, so the report L at\n$1826 is never reached); then, with no jump (NSPPC bit 7 set), the next statement\n(STMT_NEXT); otherwise the jump: to the edit line (NEWPPC's bit 15 set, RUN_EDIT_LINE) or a\nprogram line (LINE_NEW).","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "6182": {"comment":"Report L (never reached: BREAK_KEY stops first)"},
        "6186": {"synopsis":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)?","comment":"NSPPC bit 7 set: no jump pending?"},
        "6190": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "6193": {"comment":"HL = NEWPPC"},
        "6196": {"comment":"A program line?"},
        "6200": {"synopsis":"Runs the edit line as a direct command (vector $0103; RUN_SETUP comes here): PPC = $FFFE\n(reports print it as 0), HL = WORKSP - 1 (so the line after it is none), DE = E_LINE - 1,\nfrom statement NSPPC (NEXT_LINE).","comment":"PPC = $FFFE: the edit line"},
        "6206": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - 1: no line after it"},
        "6210": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE - 1, before its text"},
        "6215": {"comment":"A = NSPPC, the statement"},
        "6218": {"comment":"On at NEXT_LINE"},
        "6220": {"synopsis":"Goes to line NEWPPC, statement NSPPC: the line found (ROM 1's FIND_LINE) when it is there; a\nmissing line asked for with a statement stops with report N; a missing line otherwise runs\nthe next one, and past the program ends with 0 OK.\nObserved: go to 5 with no program reported 0 OK, 0:1.","comment":"ROM 1's FIND_LINE for line HL: Z when it is there"},
        "6223": {"comment":"A = NSPPC"},
        "6226": {"comment":"Found: run it"},
        "6228": {"comment":"A statement asked for?"},
        "6232": {"comment":"Past the program?"},
        "6235": {"comment":"A = the statement (0)"},
        "6236": {"comment":"A line there: run it"},
        "6238": {"comment":"0 OK: the program ends"},
        "6242": {"synopsis":"REM: the rest of the line is skipped (LINE_END), the return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped.\nObserved: print 1: rem x: print 3 printed 1 and reported 0:2.","comment":"The return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6243": {"synopsis":"The end of a line: when checking, done. When running, the next line (NXTLIN), from its first\nstatement, unless it is past the program (bits 6-7 of its first byte), which returns, ending\nthe run.","comment":"Checking: done"},
        "6248": {"comment":"HL = NXTLIN"},
        "6251": {"comment":"Past the program?"},
        "6254": {"comment":"Past it: the run ends"},
        "6255": {"comment":"From statement 1"},
        "6256": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at HL from statement A (at least 1): PPC = its number, NXTLIN = the line after\nit.","comment":"A at least 1"},
        "6260": {"comment":"PPC = the line's number"},
        "6267": {"comment":"DE = its length"},
        "6272": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "6274": {"synopsis":"NXTLIN = HL, CH_ADD = DE (before the text), NSPPC = $FF; statement D: the first at once\n(STMT_LOOP), a later one found by ROM 1's FIND_STATEMENT, or report N when the line has\nfewer. RUN_EDIT_LINE comes here.","comment":"NXTLIN = the next line"},
        "6278": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
        "6281": {"comment":"D = the statement"},
        "6284": {"comment":"NSPPC = $FF: no jump"},
        "6288": {"comment":"D = the statement - 1"},
        "6289": {"comment":"SUBPPC = statement - 1"},
        "6292": {"comment":"Statement 1: at once"},
        "6295": {"comment":"D = the statement again"},
        "6296": {"comment":"Statement D (ROM 1's FIND_STATEMENT)"},
        "6299": {"comment":"Found: on at STMT_NEXT"},
        "6301": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $16 (report N, \"Statement lost\").","comment":"Report N: the line has fewer statements"},
        "6305": {"synopsis":"The end of a statement's operands. Running: returns, and the command's routine runs.\nChecking: the two returns are dropped and the statement must end here (STMT_NEXT).","comment":"Running?"},
        "6309": {"comment":"Yes: back to the command's routine"},
        "6310": {"comment":"Checking: both returns dropped"},
        "6312": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "6313": {"comment":"ENTER: the line's end"},
        "6317": {"comment":"':': the next statement"},
        "6322": {"comment":"Anything else: report C"},
        "6325": {"synopsis":"Operand classes: 15 bytes, one for each class 0-$0E, each a relative pointer to the class's\nroutine (this byte's address plus its value): CLASS_0 to CLASS_B as in the 48K ROM, then\nCLASS_C, CLASS_D and CLASS_E, which run a routine in this ROM."},
        "6340": {"synopsis":"Class $0D, an optional number (RUN, CLEAR), then as class $0C.","comment":"ROM 1's FETCH_NUM"},
        "6343": {"synopsis":"Class $0C: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_E.","comment":"Z: the statement ends here"},
        "6344": {"synopsis":"Class $0E: the command's routine in this ROM, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now,\nwhen checking and when running; class $0C enters with Z, which ends the statement first\n(STATEMENT_END).","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6345": {"comment":"Class $0C: the statement ends here"},
        "6348": {"comment":"HL kept in DE"},
        "6349": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "6355": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6356": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "6358": {"synopsis":"Class 3, an optional number (RANDOMIZE, RESTORE): ROM 1's FETCH_NUM, then as class 0."},
        "6361": {"synopsis":"Class 0: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_5.","comment":"Z: the statement ends here"},
        "6362": {"synopsis":"Class 5: the command's routine in ROM 1, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now (class 0\nends the statement first): as CALL_ROM1 does, with $18F8 as the return point.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6363": {"comment":"Class 0: the statement ends here"},
        "6366": {"comment":"HL kept in DE"},
        "6367": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "6373": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6374": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "6375": {"comment":"$5B5A: back here"},
        "6381": {"comment":"ROM1_RETURN's copy under it"},
        "6384": {"comment":"HL back; $5B14 on the stack as the return"},
        "6385": {"comment":"HL kept again"},
        "6386": {"comment":"The routine's address on top"},
        "6389": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs and go"},
        "6392": {"synopsis":"Back from ROM 1: returns."},
        "6393": {"synopsis":"Class 1: ROM 1's CLASS_1 (a variable to assign to).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_1: the variable"},
        "6397": {"synopsis":"Class 2: the value assigned (ROM 1's VAL_FETCH) and the statement's end; the entry ends\nhere.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6398": {"comment":"ROM 1's VAL_FETCH: the value"},
        "6401": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "6405": {"synopsis":"Class 4: ROM 1's CLASS_4 (a FOR or NEXT variable).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_4: the FOR or NEXT variable"},
        "6409": {"synopsis":"Past the current character, then CLASS_8.","comment":"Past the current character"},
        "6410": {"synopsis":"Class 8: ROM 1's CLASS_8 (two numbers separated by ',').","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_8: two numbers"},
        "6414": {"synopsis":"Class 6: ROM 1's CLASS_6 (a number).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: a number"},
        "6418": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\").","comment":"Report C"},
        "6422": {"synopsis":"Class $0A: ROM 1's CLASS_A (a string).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A: a string"},
        "6426": {"synopsis":"Class 7, INK to OVER as statements: when running, the temporary colours from the permanent\nones (ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP); the item set by ROM 1's COL_TEMP_ITEM, with A from T_ADDR's\nlow byte - $A7 (the keyword's token, as each entry is one byte); the statement's end; then\nthe permanent colours from the temporary ones: ATTR_P and MASK_P, and P_FLAG's permanent\nbits.\nObserved: ink 2 made ATTR_P 58 (it was 56).","comment":"Running? (the RES keeps Z)"},
        "6430": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "6436": {"comment":"Running: ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "6439": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped","synopsis":"The item."},
        "6440": {"comment":"A = the keyword"},
        "6443": {"comment":"A = the keyword's token"},
        "6445": {"comment":"ROM 1's COL_TEMP_ITEM"},
        "6448": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "6451": {"comment":"ATTR_P, MASK_P = ATTR_T, MASK_T"},
        "6457": {"comment":"P_FLAG: the temporary bits into the permanent ones"},
        "6468": {"synopsis":"Class 9: ROM 1's CLASS_9 (PLOT, DRAW, CIRCLE).","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_9"},
        "6472": {"synopsis":"Class $0B, the tape and disk commands: $5B66's high bits cleared; T_ADDR's low byte - $74\ntells which (each entry one byte): SAVE $11EB, LOAD $11F2, VERIFY $11F9, MERGE $1200.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6473": {"comment":"$5B66: its top four bits cleared"},
        "6481": {"comment":"Which command?"},
        "6484": {"comment":"0 SAVE, 1 LOAD, 2 VERIFY, 3 MERGE"},
        "6486": {"comment":"T_ADDR = the command's number"},
        "6489": {"comment":"0: SAVE_128"},
        "6492": {"comment":"1: LOAD_128"},
        "6496": {"comment":"2: VERIFY_128"},
        "6500": {"comment":"3: MERGE_128"},
        "6503": {"synopsis":"IF: when running, the condition taken off the calculator stack: false (0, ROM 1's IS_ZERO)\nskips the rest of the line (LINE_END); true runs it, THEN acting as ':' (STMT_START).\nObserved: if 0 then print 1 printed nothing; if 1 then print 2 printed 2 and reported 0:2.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "6504": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "6510": {"comment":"The condition dropped"},
        "6513": {"comment":"DE = -5: one value"},
        "6520": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "6523": {"comment":"False: the rest skipped"},
        "6526": {"synopsis":"True, or checking: the rest of the line as statements.","comment":"The rest of the line: THEN acts as ':'"},
        "6529": {"synopsis":"FOR (class $0E, after the variable, '=', the value, TO and the limit): STEP and its number\n(CLASS_6), or 1 stacked when there is none; the statement's end; then ROM 1's FOR_VALUES\ndoes the rest, as in the 48K ROM.\nObserved: for i=1 to 3: print i;: next i printed 123.","comment":"STEP?"},
        "6533": {"comment":"Past STEP"},
        "6534": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "6537": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "6540": {"comment":"On"},
        "6542": {"synopsis":"No STEP: the statement's end, and 1 as a small integer onto the calculator stack (STKEND\nmoved on 5).","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "6545": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "6548": {"comment":"0, 0, 1, 0, 0 at STKEND"},
        "6554": {"comment":"0, 0, 1, 0, 0: the step 1"},
        "6563": {"comment":"STKEND moved on 5"},
        "6566": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's FOR_VALUES.","comment":"ROM 1's FOR_VALUES: the loop set up"},
        "6570": {"synopsis":"Past the ',' to the next variable.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "6571": {"synopsis":"READ: as the 48K ROM's: for each variable (CLASS_1), when running, the next DATA item: after\na ',' at DATADD, or the first of the next DATA statement (ROM 1's LOOK_PROG for $E4); none\nis report E. It is evaluated with the variable's type (ROM 1's VAL_FETCH), DATADD moves past\nit, and CH_ADD comes back to the READ statement (kept in X_PTR).\nObserved: read a: print a: data 7 as a direct command gave E Out of DATA, 0:1 (only the\nprogram is searched).","comment":"The variable (CLASS_1)"},
        "6574": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "6580": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "6581": {"comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD"},
        "6584": {"comment":"HL = DATADD"},
        "6587": {"comment":"A = the byte at DATADD"},
        "6588": {"comment":"Another item here?"},
        "6592": {"comment":"The next DATA (ROM 1's LOOK_PROG)"},
        "6597": {"comment":"Found"},
        "6599": {"comment":"None: report E"},
        "6603": {"synopsis":"The item at HL: CH_ADD there, evaluated and assigned (ROM 1's VAL_FETCH); DATADD = past it;\nCH_ADD back from X_PTR, whose high byte is cleared.","comment":"Past the ',' or DATA"},
        "6604": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the item"},
        "6607": {"comment":"A = its first character"},
        "6608": {"comment":"ROM 1's VAL_FETCH: evaluated and assigned"},
        "6611": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD, past the item"},
        "6612": {"comment":"DATADD = there"},
        "6615": {"comment":"HL = X_PTR, the place in the READ statement"},
        "6618": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte cleared"},
        "6622": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "6626": {"synopsis":"A ',' and another variable, or the statement's end.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "6627": {"comment":"Another variable?"},
        "6631": {"comment":"No: the statement's end"},
        "6635": {"synopsis":"DATA: checking, each item is an expression (ROM 1's SCAN_EXPR) up to the end of the\nstatement; running, the statement is skipped (DATA_RUN).","comment":"Running?"},
        "6639": {"comment":"Yes: the statement skipped"},
        "6641": {"synopsis":"One item, then ',' and the next.","comment":"ROM 1's SCAN_EXPR: one item"},
        "6644": {"comment":"No ','? Then the statement must end"},
        "6649": {"comment":"Past the ','"},
        "6652": {"synopsis":"Running: A = DATA's token, then DATA_SKIP_A.","comment":"DATA's token"},
        "6654": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's DATA_SKIP: the statement whose keyword is A skipped (DEF FN comes here too).","comment":"ROM 1's DATA_SKIP"},
        "6658": {"synopsis":"RUN: GO TO line n (ROM 1's GO_TO_CMD), RESTORE to the first line (ROM 1's RESTORE_BC with BC\n= 0), then CLEAR with RAMTOP unchanged (CLEAR_RUN).","comment":"ROM 1's GO_TO_CMD"},
        "6661": {"comment":"BC = 0: from the first line"},
        "6664": {"comment":"ROM 1's RESTORE_BC"},
        "6669": {"synopsis":"CLEAR: CLEAR_RUN with BC = n (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD).\nObserved: clear 30000 made RAMTOP 30000.","comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_WORD: BC = n"},
        "6672": {"synopsis":"As the 48K ROM's: the variables removed (ROM 1's RECLAIM_DE_HL from VARS to E_LINE), the\nscreen cleared (ROM 1's CLS_CMD); the new RAMTOP (BC, or the old one for 0) must be above\nSTKEND + 50 and not above P_RAMT, else report M; then the machine stack starts again under\nit, with the GO SUB end marker and the error address, ERR_SP pointing at it.","comment":"0: RAMTOP as it is"},
        "6676": {"comment":"BC = RAMTOP"},
        "6680": {"synopsis":"The new RAMTOP kept; the variables and screen cleared; the limits tested.","comment":"The new RAMTOP kept"},
        "6681": {"comment":"DE = VARS"},
        "6685": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE - 1"},
        "6689": {"comment":"The variables removed"},
        "6692": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLS_CMD"},
        "6695": {"comment":"STKEND + 50"},
        "6702": {"comment":"DE = the new RAMTOP"},
        "6703": {"comment":"Below it?"},
        "6707": {"comment":"P_RAMT"},
        "6711": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "6715": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $15 (report M, \"RAMTOP no good\").","comment":"Report M"},
        "6719": {"synopsis":"RAMTOP = DE; the return, the error address and the marker taken off the stack, then put back\nunder the new RAMTOP, ERR_SP following.","comment":"RAMTOP = DE"},
        "6723": {"comment":"The return"},
        "6724": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "6725": {"comment":"The GO SUB end marker"},
        "6726": {"comment":"The stack from RAMTOP"},
        "6730": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP + 1"},
        "6731": {"comment":"The marker back"},
        "6732": {"comment":"The error address back"},
        "6733": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "6737": {"comment":"The return back"},
        "6739": {"synopsis":"GO SUB (class $0C): as the 48K ROM's: the place to return to kept below the ERR_SP slot (the\nnext statement, SUBPPC + 1, one byte, and the line, PPC), the error address back on top and\nERR_SP at it; then GO TO (ROM 1's GO_TO_CMD), and room for 20 more bytes must be left (ROM\n1's TEST_ROOM, report 4).","comment":"DE = the return"},
        "6740": {"comment":"H = SUBPPC + 1"},
        "6744": {"comment":"Under the error address"},
        "6745": {"comment":"One byte of it"},
        "6746": {"comment":"BC = PPC"},
        "6750": {"comment":"PPC under it"},
        "6751": {"comment":"The error address on top"},
        "6752": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "6756": {"comment":"The return back"},
        "6757": {"comment":"ROM 1's GO_TO_CMD"},
        "6760": {"comment":"20 bytes (ROM 1's TEST_ROOM)"},
        "6763": {"comment":"ROM 1's TEST_ROOM: report 4 when there is too little"},
        "6767": {"synopsis":"RETURN (class $0C): as the 48K ROM's: the statement and line GO SUB kept taken from below\nthe ERR_SP slot, the error address and ERR_SP moved up, NEWPPC and NSPPC set for the jump.\nThe end marker ($3E) instead is report 7.\nObserved: return as a direct command gave 7 RETURN without GOSUB, 0:1.","comment":"BC = the return"},
        "6768": {"comment":"HL = the error address"},
        "6769": {"comment":"DE = the line kept"},
        "6770": {"comment":"A = its high byte"},
        "6771": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "6775": {"comment":"Back to the statement byte"},
        "6776": {"comment":"H = the statement; the error address in its place"},
        "6777": {"comment":"HL = the line, D = the statement"},
        "6778": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "6783": {"comment":"NEWPPC"},
        "6786": {"comment":"NSPPC"},
        "6790": {"synopsis":"No GO SUB: the stack as it was, report 7 (\"RETURN without GOSUB\").","comment":"The marker back"},
        "6791": {"comment":"The error address back"},
        "6792": {"comment":"Report 7"},
        "6796": {"synopsis":"DEF FN (class $0E): as the 48K ROM's: running, the statement is skipped (DATA_SKIP_A with\nDEF FN's token). Checking: a letter (and '$'), '(', the parameters (each a letter, maybe\nwith '$'), ')', '=' and an expression of the name's type (report C otherwise). After each\nparameter 6 bytes are made (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM), the marker $0E and room for its value, which\nFN fills.\nObserved: def fn f(x)=x*2: print fn f(4) as a direct command gave P FN without DEF, 0:2 (FN\nlooks in the program)."},
        "6800": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "6802": {"comment":"Running: skipped"},
        "6807": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number so far","synopsis":"Checking: the name, a letter (ROM 1's ALPHA) and maybe '$'."},
        "6811": {"comment":"A letter (ROM 1's ALPHA)?"},
        "6814": {"comment":"Not a letter: report C"},
        "6816": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6817": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "6821": {"comment":"A string"},
        "6825": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6826": {"synopsis":"'(' must follow; ')' at once means no parameters.","comment":"'('?"},
        "6828": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "6830": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6831": {"comment":"')' at once: no parameters?"},
        "6835": {"synopsis":"A parameter: a letter (report C otherwise), maybe '$', then 6 bytes of room with the marker\n$0E.","comment":"ROM 1's ALPHA: a letter?"},
        "6838": {"synopsis":"Not a letter: report C."},
        "6841": {"comment":"DE = the letter's place"},
        "6842": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6843": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "6847": {"comment":"DE = the '$''s place; past it"},
        "6849": {"synopsis":"The 6 bytes: room made (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM), $0E first; then ',' and the next parameter.","comment":"HL = the parameter's last character"},
        "6850": {"comment":"6 bytes (ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "6856": {"comment":"The marker $0E two bytes on"},
        "6860": {"comment":"','? Then the next parameter"},
        "6864": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6867": {"synopsis":"')', '=' and the expression, of the name's type.","comment":"')'?"},
        "6871": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6872": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "6876": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6877": {"comment":"FLAGS kept: the name's type"},
        "6881": {"comment":"The expression (ROM 1's SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "6884": {"comment":"A = FLAGS as the name left it"},
        "6885": {"comment":"The same type?"},
        "6890": {"synopsis":"Report C when the syntax is wrong.","comment":"Not: report C"},
        "6893": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "6896": {"synopsis":"MOVE (class $0C, two strings): does nothing; the statement has already been checked.\nObserved: move \"a\",\"b\" gave 0 OK, 0:1."},
        "6897": {"synopsis":"Runs LOAD \"\" as a command (from $284E): $EC0E = $FF; bank 0 and the machine stack; the edit\nline emptied (ROM 1's CLEAR_EDIT_WS) and LOAD_LINE copied into it; then LINE_ENTER checks\nand runs it."},
        "6900": {"comment":"$EC0E = $FF"},
        "6902": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "6905": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "6908": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6911": {"comment":"Room for 3 bytes in the edit line"},
        "6914": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "6917": {"comment":"LOAD \"\" into it"},
        "6920": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "6929": {"comment":"Checked and run"},
        "6932": {"synopsis":"Runs LLIST as a command (from $2862): bank 0, the edit line emptied, LLIST's token ($E1) put\ninto it, then LINE_ENTER.","comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "6935": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_EDIT_WS: the edit line emptied"},
        "6938": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6941": {"comment":"Room for one byte"},
        "6944": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "6947": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6950": {"comment":"LLIST's token"},
        "6952": {"comment":"LINE_ENTER: checked and run"},
        "6955": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM (class $0C): to 48 BASIC for good: channel P takes channel S's routines\n(CHANS_P_FROM_S), FLAGS bit 4 cleared; the stack from ERR_SP with ROM 1's REPORT ($1303)\nunder $0013 and $0008; the paging byte $20 (paging locked), then SWAP_ROM, which pages ROM 1\nin and returns to its RST $08 with $0013's $FF as the code: 0 OK, and the 48K ROM's REPORT\ngoes on in 48 BASIC.\nObserved: spectrum gave 0 OK, 0:1, with FLAGS bit 4 clear and the paging byte $30.","comment":"CHANS_P_FROM_S: channel P made as channel S"},
        "6958": {"comment":"The stack from ERR_SP"},
        "6962": {"comment":"The error address dropped"},
        "6963": {"comment":"ROM 1's REPORT"},
        "6967": {"comment":"The code's place: ROM 1's $0013 holds $FF"},
        "6971": {"comment":"ROM 1's RST $08"},
        "6975": {"comment":"Paging locked, ROM 0 for now"},
        "6980": {"comment":"Into ROM 1"},
        "6983": {"synopsis":"The menu's 48 BASIC (MENU_ACTIONS item 3): the paging byte $20 (paging locked), then\nSWAP_ROM returns to $0000 in ROM 1: the 48K ROM starts from the beginning.","comment":"The return: $0000 in ROM 1"},
        "6987": {"comment":"Paging locked, ROM 0 for now"},
        "6992": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM: into ROM 1 at $0000"},
        "6995": {"synopsis":"Copies channel S's output and input addresses (CHANS + 5) over channel P's (CHANS + 15);\nFLAGS2 bit 3 and FLAGS bit 4 cleared.","comment":"HL = CHANS + 5: channel S's addresses"},
        "7002": {"comment":"DE = CHANS + 15: channel P's"},
        "7008": {"comment":"Its output and input addresses"},
        "7013": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 3 cleared"},
        "7017": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 cleared"},
        "7022": {"synopsis":"LOAD \"\" as tokens ($EF, '\"', '\"'), copied into the edit line by RUN_LOAD_LINE."},
        "7025": {"synopsis":"LLIST (class $0E): LIST to stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "7029": {"synopsis":"LIST (class $0E): as the 48K ROM's: stream 2 (or LLIST's 3), TV_FLAG = 0; when running, that\nstream (ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT); a '#' stream instead (ROM 1's STREAM_ALTER), then ';' or ','\nand the line number, or none; or the line number alone; the statement's end; then ROM 1's\nLIST at $1825 lists.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "7031": {"synopsis":"The stream in A; TV_FLAG = 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG = 0"},
        "7035": {"comment":"Checking? (ROM 1's SYNTAX_Z)"},
        "7040": {"comment":"Running: the stream (ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "7043": {"synopsis":"'#' and a stream (ROM 1's STREAM_ALTER), or the line number at once.","comment":"ROM 1's GET_CHAR"},
        "7046": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_ALTER: '#' and a stream?"},
        "7049": {"comment":"No '#': the line number, if any"},
        "7051": {"comment":"After the stream"},
        "7054": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "7058": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7062": {"synopsis":"Past the separator; the line number (CLASS_6).","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_SKIP: past it"},
        "7065": {"comment":"The line number (CLASS_6)"},
        "7070": {"synopsis":"No number: 0 (ROM 1's USE_ZERO).","comment":"ROM 1's USE_ZERO"},
        "7075": {"synopsis":"An optional number (ROM 1's FETCH_NUM).","comment":"ROM 1's FETCH_NUM"},
        "7078": {"synopsis":"The statement's end, then ROM 1's LIST from $1825.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "7081": {"comment":"ROM 1's LIST at $1825"},
        "7085": {"synopsis":"SAVE ! (from $125F): the header at $5B71 (9 bytes: its length word at $5B72, start at $5B74)\nand the data saved as a new file named by $5B67, on the stack at $5BFF: the entry made\n(RAMDISK_NEW), 9 + the length taken from the free bytes (RAMDISK_FREE_ADD, report 4 when\nthere are too few), the header and the data written (RAMDISK_WRITE), the file closed\n(RAMDISK_CLOSE), bank 0.\nObserved: save !\"bb\"code 0,100 took 129 bytes (100, the 9-byte header and the 20-byte entry)\noff the 76780 free at start-up.","comment":"The other stack"},
        "7089": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "7092": {"comment":"The new entry"},
        "7095": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7099": {"comment":"HL = -(9 + the length)"},
        "7102": {"comment":"A = $FF, the high byte; carry clear"},
        "7106": {"comment":"Taken from the free bytes"},
        "7109": {"comment":"The header"},
        "7115": {"comment":"RAMDISK_WRITE: the header"},
        "7118": {"comment":"The data"},
        "7125": {"comment":"RAMDISK_WRITE: the data"},
        "7128": {"comment":"Closed"},
        "7131": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7136": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "7141": {"synopsis":"CAT (class $0E): only CAT ! (the RAM disk): '!' must follow (report C otherwise); the\nstatement's end; stream 2; then, on the other stack ($5BFF), the catalogue ($20D2) and bank\n0 (SELECT_BANK 5).\nObserved: cat ! gave 0 OK, 0:1; cat alone was refused by the syntax check.","comment":"ROM 1's GET_CHAR"},
        "7144": {"comment":"'!'?"},
        "7146": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7149": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_SKIP: past it"},
        "7152": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "7155": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "7157": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "7160": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "7164": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "7167": {"comment":"The catalogue"},
        "7170": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7175": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "7180": {"synopsis":"ERASE (class $0E): only ERASE ! (the RAM disk): '!' must follow (report C otherwise), then\nthe name ($1393); the statement's end; then, on the other stack, the file erased ($1F5F) and\nbank 0.","comment":"ROM 1's GET_CHAR"},
        "7183": {"comment":"'!'?"},
        "7185": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7188": {"comment":"The name"},
        "7191": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "7194": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "7198": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "7201": {"comment":"Erased"},
        "7204": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7209": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"LOAD ! (from $126D): the file named by $5B67 opened (RAMDISK_OPEN, report h when there is\nnone) and its 9-byte header read to $5B71 (RAMDISK_READ), bank 0; on the stack at $5BFF.\nObserved: load !\"zz\"code with no such file gave h File does not exist, 0:1.","comment":"The other stack"},
        "7218": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "7221": {"comment":"RAMDISK_OPEN: report h when there is none"},
        "7224": {"comment":"The 9-byte header to $5B71"},
        "7230": {"comment":"RAMDISK_READ"},
        "7233": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7238": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "7243": {"synopsis":"LOAD ! (from $1381): DE bytes of the open file read to HL (RAMDISK_READ), then RAMDISK_CLOSE\nand bank 0, on the stack at $5BFF.","comment":"The other stack"},
        "7247": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "7250": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "7252": {"comment":"RAMDISK_READ: to HL"},
        "7255": {"comment":"RAMDISK_CLOSE"},
        "7258": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7263": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "7268": {"synopsis":"Pages in the RAM bank BANK_NUMBERS gives for A (0-5: banks 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 0) at $C000,\nkeeping the rest of the paging byte ($5B5C), with interrupts off. Keeps BC and HL."},
        "7270": {"comment":"HL = BANK_NUMBERS + A"},
        "7277": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "7279": {"comment":"A = the paging byte"},
        "7282": {"comment":"The old bank's bits cleared"},
        "7284": {"comment":"The bank in"},
        "7288": {"comment":"To port $7FFD"},
        "7297": {"synopsis":"SELECT_BANK's banks for A = 0-5: 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 0."},
        "7303": {"synopsis":"Compares the name at $5B67 with the entry at IX (10 bytes). Exit: Z when they are the same;\notherwise the flags of the first difference (carry when $5B67's byte is lower).","comment":"DE = the name"},
        "7306": {"synopsis":"The same for the name at DE.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "7309": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "7311": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"A = the name's character"},
        "7313": {"comment":"The entry's the same?"},
        "7315": {"comment":"No: the flags say which is lower"},
        "7319": {"synopsis":"Makes a catalogue entry for the name at $5B67 at $5B83: an existing file of that name is\nreport e; a full catalogue (the entry below $C014) or too few free bytes for its 20 is\nreport 4. The name copied, bit 0 of the flags set, the current place = the start (the end of\nthe previous file), the length 0; $5B66 bit 2 set (a file being written); bank 0; $5B83 down\n20.\nA catalogue entry (20 bytes, in bank 7, the catalogue growing down from $EBEC to the free\nentry at $5B83): +0 the name (10 bytes), +10 the start, +13 the length, +16 the current\nplace, +19 flags (bit 0: being written). Places are three bytes: an address in $C000-$FFFF\nand a bank number for SELECT_BANK (0-4: banks 1, 3, 4, 6, 7); lengths are plain 3-byte\nnumbers.\nObserved: save !\"aa\" a second time gave e File already exists, 0:1.","comment":"Already there?"},
        "7324": {"comment":"Report e"},
        "7328": {"synopsis":"Room in the catalogue and 20 free bytes.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "7330": {"comment":"The entry below $C014?"},
        "7337": {"comment":"Then report 4"},
        "7339": {"comment":"20 bytes fewer free"},
        "7342": {"comment":"A:HL = -20"},
        "7344": {"comment":"RAMDISK_FREE_ADD"},
        "7347": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 2: a file being written"},
        "7352": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "7355": {"comment":"The name"},
        "7363": {"comment":"Being written"},
        "7367": {"comment":"The current place = the start"},
        "7385": {"comment":"The length 0"},
        "7395": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7400": {"comment":"$5B83 = the next entry"},
        "7411": {"synopsis":"Adds A:HL (a signed 24-bit number) to the free bytes ($5B85-$5B87). Taking away more than\nthere are is report 4.","comment":"DE = the free bytes' low word"},
        "7415": {"comment":"C = their high byte"},
        "7421": {"comment":"Taking away?"},
        "7425": {"comment":"Adding: A:HL + C:DE"},
        "7427": {"synopsis":"The new count stored."},
        "7434": {"synopsis":"A negative number: there must be a carry, or there were too few.","comment":"A:HL + C:DE; no carry means too few"},
        "7436": {"comment":"Enough: stored"},
        "7438": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 3 (report 4, \"Out of memory\").","comment":"Report 4"},
        "7442": {"synopsis":"Looks for the name at $5B67 in the catalogue (bank 7 paged in), from $EBEC down to $5B83.\nExit: NZ and IX at its entry when found; Z (IX at $5B83) when not.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7447": {"comment":"IX = the first entry"},
        "7451": {"synopsis":"The free entry: not found.","comment":"DE = the free entry"},
        "7456": {"comment":"Reached it?"},
        "7461": {"comment":"Yes: not found (Z)"},
        "7462": {"comment":"NAME_MATCH: the same name?"},
        "7465": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "7467": {"comment":"Found: NZ"},
        "7470": {"synopsis":"The next entry down.","comment":"20 bytes down"},
        "7477": {"synopsis":"Finds the file named by $5B67 (report h when there is none) and sets its current place to\nits start; bank 0.","comment":"RAMDISK_FIND"},
        "7480": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "7482": {"comment":"Report h"},
        "7486": {"synopsis":"The current place = the start."},
        "7504": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7510": {"synopsis":"Closes the file at IX when it is being written (flags bit 0, cleared, and $5B66 bit 2): its\nlength = the current place less the start, the bank numbers turned into the two top bits of\n16K pages; the next entry's start = this current place. Bank 7 is left paged in.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7515": {"comment":"Being written?"},
        "7520": {"comment":"No longer being written"},
        "7524": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 2 cleared"},
        "7529": {"comment":"A:HL = the current place"},
        "7538": {"comment":"B:DE = the start"},
        "7547": {"comment":"The current place less the start"},
        "7551": {"comment":"Banks to 16K units"},
        "7563": {"comment":"The length"},
        "7572": {"comment":"A:HL = the current place"},
        "7581": {"comment":"The next entry's start"},
        "7596": {"synopsis":"Writes BC bytes from HL to the file at IX's current place, moving it on. The source may be\nin the $C000 window, which the RAM disk pages out: up to 32 bytes at a time are first copied\nto $5B98 (or a whole run from below $C000 at once). Each byte goes to the current bank; at\n$FFFF the next bank number and $C000.","comment":"Done?"},
        "7599": {"comment":"The source kept"},
        "7600": {"comment":"From below $C000?"},
        "7604": {"comment":"HL = $C000 - the source"},
        "7606": {"comment":"At or above $C000: through the buffer"},
        "7610": {"comment":"The bytes below $C000 kept"},
        "7611": {"comment":"All of them below it?"},
        "7615": {"comment":"No: HL = the count"},
        "7617": {"comment":"BC = the part below $C000"},
        "7619": {"comment":"HL = the rest"},
        "7621": {"comment":"The rest kept; HL = the source"},
        "7622": {"comment":"Then on from $C000"},
        "7626": {"comment":"This part first"},
        "7628": {"synopsis":"All of it below $C000: in one go.","comment":"The count below $C000 dropped"},
        "7629": {"comment":"HL = the source"},
        "7630": {"comment":"Nothing after it"},
        "7637": {"synopsis":"From the $C000 window: 32 bytes (or fewer) through the buffer at $5B98.","comment":"HL = the count"},
        "7639": {"comment":"More than 32?"},
        "7645": {"comment":"No: the last part"},
        "7647": {"comment":"The rest kept; HL = the source"},
        "7648": {"comment":"BC = 32"},
        "7652": {"synopsis":"The last part.","comment":"HL = the source"},
        "7653": {"comment":"Nothing after it"},
        "7657": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5B98.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7658": {"comment":"Copied to $5B98"},
        "7664": {"comment":"The next source kept"},
        "7665": {"comment":"From the buffer"},
        "7668": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 for the entry; then the file's bank paged in for the bytes.","comment":"Bank 7: the entry"},
        "7673": {"comment":"DE = the current place"},
        "7679": {"comment":"A = its bank (an index into BANK_NUMBERS)"},
        "7682": {"comment":"That bank in"},
        "7685": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "7687": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "7691": {"synopsis":"More to write? Otherwise the current place stored, bank 0, and the next part.","comment":"More?"},
        "7696": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7701": {"comment":"The current place stored"},
        "7707": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7712": {"comment":"HL = the next source"},
        "7713": {"comment":"BC = what is left"},
        "7714": {"comment":"The next part"},
        "7716": {"synopsis":"The next bank, from $C000.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7721": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "7727": {"comment":"DE = $C000"},
        "7730": {"comment":"That bank in"},
        "7735": {"synopsis":"Reads BC bytes from the file at IX's current place to HL, moving it on; as RAMDISK_WRITE the\nother way: a destination in the $C000 window is filled through $5B98, 32 bytes at a time.","comment":"Done?"},
        "7738": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "7743": {"comment":"HL = $C000 - the destination"},
        "7745": {"comment":"At or above $C000: through the buffer"},
        "7749": {"comment":"The bytes below $C000 kept"},
        "7750": {"comment":"All of them below it?"},
        "7754": {"comment":"No: HL = the count"},
        "7756": {"comment":"BC = the part below $C000"},
        "7758": {"comment":"HL = the rest"},
        "7760": {"comment":"The rest kept; HL = the destination"},
        "7761": {"comment":"Nothing from the buffer"},
        "7765": {"comment":"Then on to $C000"},
        "7769": {"comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "7772": {"synopsis":"All of it below $C000: in one go.","comment":"The count below $C000 dropped"},
        "7773": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "7774": {"comment":"Nothing after it, nothing from the buffer"},
        "7780": {"comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "7783": {"synopsis":"Into the $C000 window: through $5B98.","comment":"HL = the count"},
        "7785": {"comment":"More than 32?"},
        "7791": {"comment":"No: the last part"},
        "7793": {"comment":"The rest kept; HL = the destination"},
        "7794": {"comment":"BC = 32"},
        "7798": {"synopsis":"The last part.","comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "7799": {"comment":"Nothing after it"},
        "7803": {"synopsis":"To $5B98 first.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7804": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "7805": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "7808": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 for the entry; then the file's bank for the bytes.","comment":"Bank 7: the entry"},
        "7813": {"comment":"HL = the current place"},
        "7819": {"comment":"A = its bank (an index into BANK_NUMBERS)"},
        "7822": {"comment":"That bank in"},
        "7825": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "7827": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "7831": {"synopsis":"More to read? Otherwise the current place stored, bank 0, and the buffer's bytes to their\nplace.","comment":"More?"},
        "7836": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7841": {"comment":"The current place stored"},
        "7847": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7852": {"comment":"DE = the buffer's destination"},
        "7853": {"comment":"BC = the buffer's count"},
        "7857": {"comment":"Any?"},
        "7861": {"comment":"Copied there"},
        "7863": {"synopsis":"The next part.","comment":"HL = the next destination"},
        "7864": {"comment":"BC = what is left"},
        "7868": {"synopsis":"The next bank, from $C000.","comment":"Bank 7"},
