        "8224": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8227": {"comment":"A back"},
        "8228": {"synopsis":"To the destination bank; at $FFFF the next bank.","comment":"The destination's registers"},
        "8230": {"comment":"The destination's bank"},
        "8232": {"comment":"The byte stored"},
        "8233": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8239": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "8244": {"comment":"E = its paging byte"},
        "8248": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8251": {"synopsis":"The next byte.","comment":"The source's registers"},
        "8254": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; 20 bytes back to the free bytes; DE, C = the length in bank form.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8259": {"comment":"A:HL = 20: the entry's bytes"},
        "8264": {"comment":"RAMDISK_FREE_ADD"},
        "8267": {"comment":"C:DE = the erased file's length"},
        "8276": {"comment":"C = its 16K units"},
        "8283": {"comment":"D = the rest"},
        "8287": {"comment":"IX kept: the erased entry"},
        "8289": {"synopsis":"Each later entry: its start and current place lowered by the length (a place that drops\nbelow $C000 goes to the previous bank).","comment":"DE kept"},
        "8290": {"comment":"IX = the entry below"},
        "8296": {"comment":"A:HL = its start"},
        "8305": {"comment":"Less the length"},
        "8309": {"comment":"Still at $C000 or above?"},
        "8313": {"comment":"No: $4000 on, in the bank before"},
        "8316": {"synopsis":"The start stored."},
        "8325": {"comment":"A:HL = its current place"},
        "8334": {"comment":"Less the length"},
        "8338": {"comment":"Still at $C000 or above?"},
        "8342": {"comment":"No: $4000 on, in the bank before"},
        "8345": {"synopsis":"The current place stored; the next entry, up to $5B83; then the entries moved up by 20\n(LDDR) and $5B83 up 20."},
        "8354": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8357": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "8358": {"comment":"The free entry?"},
        "8366": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "8368": {"comment":"DE = the free entry"},
        "8372": {"comment":"HL = the erased entry"},
        "8375": {"comment":"BC = the bytes of the entries below it"},
        "8379": {"comment":"HL = the erased entry"},
        "8381": {"comment":"DE = 20 bytes higher"},
        "8387": {"comment":"From the byte below each"},
        "8389": {"comment":"Moved up 20, over the erased entry"},
        "8391": {"comment":"The free entry 20 higher"},
        "8402": {"synopsis":"CAT ! (CAT_CMD): lists the files in name order, with bank 7 paged in: each pass looks\nthrough the catalogue for the lowest name above the last one listed (CAT_LOW_NAME at first),\nagainst CAT_HIGH_NAME as the bound, and prints it (CAT_PRINT_NAME); a pass that finds none\nends it. BREAK is tested each time (BREAK_KEY).\nObserved: with bb saved before aa, cat ! listed aa then bb.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8407": {"comment":"HL = the last listed: CAT_LOW_NAME"},
        "8410": {"synopsis":"A pass: BC = the best so far, CAT_HIGH_NAME at first."},
        "8413": {"comment":"IX = the first entry"},
        "8417": {"synopsis":"The next entry, up to $5B83.","comment":"BREAK_KEY: report L on BREAK"},
        "8420": {"comment":"HL = the entry; the last listed kept"},
        "8423": {"comment":"The free entry?"},
        "8430": {"comment":"HL = the last listed"},
        "8431": {"comment":"Yes: the pass ends"},
        "8433": {"comment":"DE = the last listed"},
        "8437": {"comment":"NAME_COMPARE: the last listed below the entry?"},
        "8442": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "8444": {"comment":"DE = the best so far"},
        "8448": {"comment":"The best so far below the entry?"},
        "8453": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "8455": {"comment":"BC = this entry, the best now"},
        "8458": {"synopsis":"Down to the next entry.","comment":"20 bytes down"},
        "8465": {"synopsis":"None found above the last: done; otherwise it is printed and becomes the last.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "8466": {"comment":"Still the high bound ($212B): none found?"},
        "8473": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8474": {"comment":"HL = it: the last listed now"},
        "8476": {"comment":"CAT_PRINT_NAME"},
        "8479": {"comment":"The next pass"},
        "8481": {"synopsis":"RAMDISK_CAT's bounds: ten bytes of $00, lower than any name, then (from $212B) ten of $FF,\nhigher than any."},
        "8501": {"synopsis":"Prints the name of the entry at BC: copied to $5B67, bank 0 and the machine stack, its 10\ncharacters and ENTER through RST $10 (ROM 1's), ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP; then back to the\nother stack and bank 7.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "8502": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8504": {"comment":"Its name to $5B67"},
        "8512": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8517": {"comment":"The machine stack"},
        "8525": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8528": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "8530": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A = one"},
        "8533": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_A"},
        "8541": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8543": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_A"},
        "8546": {"comment":"ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "8549": {"comment":"Back to the other stack"},
        "8557": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8562": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "8564": {"synopsis":"LPRINT (class $0E): PRINT to stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "8568": {"synopsis":"PRINT (class $0E): stream 2 (or LPRINT's 3) when running (ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT), the\ntemporary colours (ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP), the items (ROM 1's PRINT_LIST), then the\nstatement's end.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "8570": {"synopsis":"The stream in A, when running (ROM 1's SYNTAX_Z).","comment":"ROM 1's SYNTAX_Z: checking?"},
        "8575": {"comment":"Running: ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8578": {"synopsis":"The colours and the items.","comment":"ROM 1's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "8581": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_LIST: the items"},
        "8584": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8588": {"synopsis":"INPUT (class $0E): when running, stream 1 (the lower screen) and ROM 1's CLS_LOWER; TV_FLAG\n= 1; the items (ROM 1's INPUT_ITEM, then INPUT_ITEMS' end from $20A0) and the statement's\nend.","comment":"ROM 1's SYNTAX_Z: checking?"},
        "8593": {"comment":"Stream 1: the lower screen"},
        "8595": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8598": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8601": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG = 1: the lower screen; the items."},
        "8605": {"comment":"ROM 1's INPUT_ITEM: the items"},
        "8608": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8611": {"comment":"ROM 1's INPUT_ITEMS' end at $20A0"},
        "8615": {"synopsis":"COPY (class $0C): the 128K's own screen copy at $08F0 (vector $012A).","comment":"COPY_128"},
        "8618": {"synopsis":"NEW (class $0C): interrupts off and start-up again from $019D (START_SETUP's CHARS onwards),\nwhich keeps RAMTOP, the UDGs and the RAM disk, and ends at the menu."},
        "8619": {"comment":"START_SETUP from CHARS on"},
        "8622": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE (class $0E, after x and y): ',' and the radius (CLASS_6, report C without the ','),\nthe statement's end, then ROM 1's CIRCLE_CMD from $232D.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "8623": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8625": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8627": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8628": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the radius"},
        "8631": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8634": {"comment":"ROM 1's CIRCLE_CMD from $232D"},
        "8638": {"synopsis":"DRAW (class $0E, after x and y): without a ',' a straight line (ROM 1's LINE_DRAW); with\none, the angle (CLASS_6) and an arc (ROM 1's DRAW_ARC from $2394). The statement's end\nfirst.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "8639": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8643": {"comment":"No: the statement's end"},
        "8646": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_DRAW: a straight line"},
        "8650": {"synopsis":"',' and the angle: an arc.","comment":"Past it"},
        "8651": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the angle"},
        "8654": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8657": {"comment":"ROM 1's arc from $2394"},
        "8661": {"synopsis":"DIM (class $0E): as the 48K ROM's: the array's name (ROM 1's LOOK_VARS; a name that cannot\nbe an array is report C); checking, its subscripts (ROM 1's VAR_SUBSCRIPTS) and the\nstatement's end; then ROM 1's DIM_RUN makes it.","comment":"ROM 1's LOOK_VARS: the array's name"},
        "8664": {"comment":"Not an array's name: report C"},
        "8666": {"comment":"ROM 1's SYNTAX_Z: running?"},
        "8669": {"comment":"Yes: DIM_RUN"},
        "8673": {"comment":"ROM 1's VAR_SUBSCRIPTS"},
        "8676": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8679": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's DIM_RUN.","comment":"ROM 1's DIM_RUN"},
        "8683": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\").","comment":"Report C"},
        "8687": {"synopsis":"When FLAGS2 bit 0 asks for it, the whole screen cleared (ROM 1's CLEAR_SCREEN).","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 0: the screen to clear?"},
        "8692": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_SCREEN"},
        "8696": {"synopsis":"An edit line that starts like an expression (LINE_ENTER): it is evaluated, and its value\nreplaces it in the editor:\n1. Checked as an expression (ROM 1's SCAN_EXPR, PPC = $FFFE): it must be a number followed\n   by ENTER, else report Q.\n2. Evaluated (FLAGS bit 7 set), $5B8B = AFTER_RUN; the result copied from the calculator\n   stack to $5B8D.\n3. ENTER, then the number's characters (ROM 1's PRINT_FP through channel R into the\n   workspace) fed to the editor one by one as if typed (KEY_INTO_EDITOR).\nObserved: 1+2 entered in 128 BASIC or in the Calculator became 3, with 0 OK, 0:0; x in 128\nBASIC gave 2 Variable not found, 0:1.","comment":"PPC = $FFFE"},
        "8702": {"comment":"Checking"},
        "8706": {"comment":"From the line's start"},
        "8709": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "8712": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "8718": {"comment":"Then ENTER?"},
        "8723": {"comment":"Running"},
        "8727": {"comment":"From the line's start again"},
        "8730": {"comment":"$5B8B = AFTER_RUN"},
        "8736": {"comment":"Evaluated"},
        "8739": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "8745": {"comment":"The result to $5B8D"},
        "8748": {"comment":"HL = STKEND - 5: the result"},
        "8759": {"comment":"Into the editor"},
        "8762": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"Parameter error\").","comment":"Report Q"},
        "8766": {"synopsis":"ENTER fed to the editor, then the number printed into the workspace (one byte of room, K_CUR\nat it, stream -1: channel R; ROM 1's PRINT_FP), the channel put back, and each character fed\nin turn.","comment":"ENTER to the editor (KEY_INTO_EDITOR)"},
        "8771": {"comment":"Room for it (ROM 1's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "8777": {"comment":"K_CUR: where channel R writes"},
        "8780": {"comment":"The number's place kept"},
        "8781": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "8785": {"comment":"Stream -1: channel R"},
        "8790": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_FP"},
        "8793": {"comment":"HL = the old CURCHL"},
        "8794": {"comment":"The channel back"},
        "8797": {"comment":"DE = the number's place"},
        "8798": {"comment":"HL = the characters' count"},
        "8804": {"synopsis":"One character to the editor.","comment":"A = one character"},
        "8805": {"comment":"KEY_INTO_EDITOR"},
        "8809": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "8810": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "8815": {"synopsis":"Feeds character A to the editor as a key (KEY_DISPATCH), in bank 7 on its stack, with stream\n2; $EC0D bit 3 cleared before and after. Keeps DE, HL.","comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "8817": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK"},
        "8820": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "8825": {"comment":"The key kept"},
        "8826": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "8828": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8831": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "8832": {"comment":"KEY_DISPATCH: the key handled"},
        "8835": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared again"},
        "8840": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK"},
        "8846": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = E_LINE - 1, then the line's first character (RST $20).","comment":"HL = E_LINE - 1"},
        "8850": {"comment":"CH_ADD there"},
        "8853": {"comment":"A = the line's first character"},
        "8855": {"synopsis":"Whether the edit line starts with LET ($F1) and has only one statement. Exit: Z when it does\n(ENTER found before any ':').","comment":"CH_ADD at the line's start"},
        "8858": {"comment":"LET?"},
        "8860": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "8861": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "8864": {"synopsis":"The next byte: ENTER (Z) or ':' (NZ) ends it.","comment":"A = the next byte"},
        "8866": {"comment":"ENTER: one statement (Z)"},
        "8869": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "8873": {"comment":"Another statement: NZ"},
        "8875": {"synopsis":"Whether A is one of OPERATORS. Exit: Z when it is; A kept.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "8876": {"comment":"HL = OPERATORS"},
        "8879": {"synopsis":"The next operator.","comment":"A = the next operator"},
        "8881": {"comment":"The list's end?"},
        "8884": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "8887": {"comment":"Yes: A back, Z"},
        "8889": {"synopsis":"Not an operator: NZ.","comment":"None: NZ"},
        "8891": {"comment":"A back"},
        "8893": {"synopsis":"OPERATOR_TEST's list: + - * / ^ = > <, the tokens <= >= <> OR AND ($C7 $C8 $C9 $C5 $C6),\nended by 0."},
        "8907": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a function keyword (a token from $A5 to $C3, other than AT and TAB). Exit: Z\nwhen it is; NZ otherwise, with carry below $A5.","comment":"Below $A5?"},
        "8911": {"comment":"$C4 or above?"},
        "8915": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "8919": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "8923": {"comment":"A function keyword: Z"},
        "8925": {"synopsis":"Not one: NZ.","comment":"NZ; carry when below $A5"},
        "8928": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a letter, or '.'. Exit: Z when it is; otherwise NUMBER_TEST.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "8929": {"comment":"Capitals made small"},
        "8931": {"comment":"Below 'a'?"},
        "8935": {"comment":"Past 'z'?"},
        "8939": {"comment":"A letter: Z"},
        "8941": {"synopsis":"Otherwise: whether a number starts here: digits (each passed with RST $20), then '.', 'E',\n'e' or an operator (OPERATOR_TEST). Exit: Z when it does.","comment":"A back"},
        "8942": {"comment":"'.'?"},
        "8945": {"comment":"DIGIT_TEST: a digit?"},
        "8948": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "8950": {"synopsis":"Past the digits.","comment":"The next character"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Another digit?"},
        "8956": {"comment":"'.'?"},
        "8959": {"comment":"'E'?"},
        "8962": {"comment":"'e'?"},
        "8965": {"comment":"Otherwise an operator? (OPERATOR_TEST)"},
        "8967": {"synopsis":"Not a number: NZ."},
        "8970": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a digit. Exit: Z when it is; NZ otherwise, with carry below '0'.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "8974": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "8978": {"comment":"A digit: Z"},
        "8980": {"synopsis":"Not a digit: NZ.","comment":"NZ; carry when below '0'"},
        "8983": {"synopsis":"PLAY (class $0E): 1 to 8 strings (ROM 1's CLASS_A each) separated by ','; more is report p\n(error code $2B, whose message entry is the copyright message); the statement's end; then\nPLAY_RUN with B = the number of strings.\nObserved: nine strings were refused when the line was entered.","comment":"B = 0 strings"},
        "8985": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "8986": {"synopsis":"One string; ',' and another.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8987": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A: a string"},
        "8991": {"comment":"One more"},
        "8992": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8996": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8999": {"synopsis":"B strings: at most 8.","comment":"More than 8?"},
        "9004": {"comment":"Report p"},
        "9008": {"synopsis":"The statement's end, then PLAY_RUN.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9011": {"comment":"PLAY_RUN"},
        "9014": {"synopsis":"$5B81 = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), then EDITOR_MAIN. Nothing in this ROM\njumps or calls here.","comment":"$5B81 = $5BFF: the other stack"},
        "9020": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK"},
        "9023": {"comment":"EDITOR_MAIN"},
        "9026": {"synopsis":"BC = HL - DE; then DE = the given HL and HL = the given DE. Nothing in this ROM calls it.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = HL - DE"},
        "9031": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9032": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "9034": {"synopsis":"Opens one byte of room before HL: ROOM_CHECK for one byte, then ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM. Nothing\nin this ROM calls it.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9037": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "9039": {"comment":"ROOM_CHECK"},
        "9044": {"comment":"ROM 1's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "9048": {"synopsis":"Tests that BC bytes fit between STKEND and the machine stack with $82 bytes to spare; when\nthey do not, ERR_NR = 3 (report 4, \"Out of memory\") and on at AFTER_RUN.\nExit: carry; DE = STKEND + BC.","comment":"HL = STKEND + BC"},
        "9052": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "9054": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "9055": {"comment":"$82 more"},
        "9059": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "9061": {"comment":"Below the stack?"},
        "9063": {"comment":"Yes: it fits (carry)"},
        "9064": {"synopsis":"Report 4: ERR_NR = 3, then AFTER_RUN.","comment":"ERR_NR = 3: report 4"},
        "9068": {"comment":"AFTER_RUN"},
        "9071": {"synopsis":"HL = A x 32 (A x 4 must fit in a byte).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A x 4"},
        "9073": {"synopsis":"HL = A x 8.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = A"},
        "9076": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "9080": {"synopsis":"HL = SP - STKEND, the room between the calculator stack and the machine stack. Nothing in\nthis ROM calls it.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = SP"},
        "9084": {"comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "9088": {"comment":"HL = SP - STKEND"},
        "9092": {"synopsis":"Draws row A of the character buffer at ($FF24) (32 bytes a row) on the screen: $5C01 bit 0\ncleared, the row's attributes from the buffer (BUF_ATTRS, 32 cells, from ATTR_T's colour),\nthen its 32 characters (BUF_DRAW_CHARS) at the row's display address. Nothing in this ROM\ncalls it, nor the buffer's other routines (BUF_FILL_ROW, BUF_DRAW_ALL, GLYPH_RAM_SETUP).","comment":"$5C01 bit 0: the inverse state"},
        "9096": {"comment":"HL = A x 32: the row's offset"},
        "9099": {"comment":"The offset kept"},
        "9100": {"comment":"The row's place in the buffer"},
        "9105": {"comment":"DE = it too"},
        "9107": {"comment":"The row kept; HL = the offset"},
        "9108": {"comment":"The offset kept"},
        "9109": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "9110": {"comment":"DE = its attribute address"},
        "9115": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "9116": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "9119": {"comment":"A = ATTR_T"},
        "9122": {"comment":"BUF_ATTRS"},
        "9125": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "9126": {"comment":"DE = its display address: $4000 + 2K x third + the offset's low byte"},
        "9138": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "9139": {"comment":"32 characters"},
        "9141": {"comment":"BUF_DRAW_CHARS"},
        "9144": {"synopsis":"Fills BC bytes of the character buffer at ($FF24), from row A on, with $FF (each cell then\ngets ATTR_P from BUF_ATTRS).\nEntry: BC = the count (at least 2).","comment":"D = $FF, the filler"},
        "9146": {"comment":"HL = A x 32"},
        "9149": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "9150": {"comment":"HL = the place in the buffer"},
        "9155": {"comment":"DE = the next byte"},
        "9158": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "9159": {"comment":"The rest copied from it"},
        "9163": {"synopsis":"Draws the character buffer at ($FF24) on screen rows 0-21: the attributes (BUF_ATTRS_ALL),\nthen the characters (BUF_DRAW_CHARS) of each third: 256, 256 and 192.","comment":"BUF_ATTRS_ALL"},
        "9166": {"comment":"DE = the display file"},
        "9169": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "9172": {"comment":"B = 0: 256 characters"},
        "9173": {"comment":"The top third"},
        "9176": {"comment":"The middle third, from $4800"},
        "9181": {"comment":"The bottom third, from $5000"},
        "9183": {"comment":"192 characters"},
        "9185": {"synopsis":"Draws B characters from HL on the screen from display address DE on (one pixel row of 8 per\ncharacter). Each character's 8 bytes come from: $FE-$FF, GLYPH_OWN + 8 x (code - $FE);\n$00-$1F, GLYPH_CONTROL; $20-$7F, the character set at CHARS, read in ROM 1 through the copy\nat $FF28 (GLYPH_RAM_SETUP); $80-$8F, GLYPH_OWN + 8 x (code - $7F); $90 up, the UDGs (UDG + 8\nx (code - $90)), read with bank 0 and the machine stack (BANK0_STACK, then BANK7_STACK).\nExit: HL and DE past the characters.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "9186": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "9188": {"comment":"$FE or $FF?"},
        "9192": {"comment":"$FE, $FF: 0, 1"},
        "9194": {"comment":"BUF_CHAR_OWN"},
        "9196": {"synopsis":"Below $FE: a control code ($00-$1F) gets GLYPH_CONTROL.","comment":"A control code?"},
        "9200": {"comment":"HL = GLYPH_CONTROL"},
        "9203": {"comment":"NC kept in F'"},
        "9205": {"comment":"BUF_GLYPH_COPY"},
        "9207": {"synopsis":"$20 up: $20-$7F from the character set at CHARS, through the RAM copy at $FF28 (ROM 1 paged\nin for the copy).","comment":"$80 up?"},
        "9209": {"comment":"Yes: BUF_CHAR_HIGH"},
        "9211": {"comment":"HL = CHARS + 8 x code"},
        "9214": {"comment":"DE = CHARS"},
        "9219": {"comment":"DE = the display address back"},
        "9220": {"comment":"The copier at $FF28: the 8 bytes read with ROM 1 paged in"},
        "9223": {"comment":"On to the next character"},
        "9225": {"synopsis":"$80 up: $80-$8F from GLYPH_OWN + 8 x (code - $7F).","comment":"A UDG ($90 up)?"},
        "9229": {"comment":"A = code - $7F: the picture's number after GLYPH_OWN"},
        "9233": {"synopsis":"$90 up: the UDGs, read in bank 0 (BANK0_STACK; carry kept in F' to page bank 7 back).","comment":"A = the UDG's number"},
        "9235": {"comment":"TIMES_8: HL = 8 x the number"},
        "9238": {"comment":"DE off this stack: BANK0_STACK swaps stacks"},
        "9239": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0, where the UDGs are"},
        "9242": {"comment":"DE kept on the other stack"},
        "9243": {"comment":"DE = UDG, the UDGs' address"},
        "9247": {"comment":"Carry: bank 7 to be paged back afterwards"},
        "9250": {"synopsis":"HL = GLYPH_OWN + 8 x A; no carry in F' (no paging back).","comment":"DE = GLYPH_OWN"},
        "9253": {"comment":"TIMES_8: HL = 8 x A"},
        "9256": {"comment":"No carry: no paging back"},
        "9257": {"synopsis":"HL = the 8 bytes' address.","comment":"The paging flag kept in F'"},
        "9258": {"comment":"HL = the picture's 8 bytes"},
        "9259": {"synopsis":"DE = the display address back; the 8 bytes to 8 pixel rows (BUF_GLYPH_8); then bank 7 back\n(BANK7_STACK) when F' has carry.","comment":"DE = the display address"},
        "9260": {"synopsis":"The 8 bytes, pixel row by pixel row (these 32 bytes, to $244B, are also the middle of\nGLYPH_RAM_SETUP's copy at $FF28).","comment":"C = the display address's high byte, for afterwards"},
        "9261": {"comment":"Pixel row 0 to the screen"},
        "9264": {"comment":"D + 1: the pixel row below"},
        "9291": {"comment":"D back to the character's top pixel row"},
        "9292": {"comment":"Carry from F': paging back wanted?"},
        "9293": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and the editor's stack again"},
        "9296": {"synopsis":"The next character and column.","comment":"HL = the character's place in the buffer"},
        "9297": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9298": {"comment":"The next column on the screen"},
        "9299": {"comment":"B characters"},
        "9302": {"synopsis":"Not run here: the first and last parts of the routine GLYPH_RAM_SETUP builds at $FF28. Its\nfirst part (14 bytes, $2456-$2463) keeps BC and flips the ROM (bit 4 of the paging byte) at\nport $7FFD with interrupts off, A kept in A'; BUF_GLYPH_8's 32 bytes ($242C-$244B) copy the\n8 bytes; the last part (11 bytes, $2464-$246E) flips the ROM back and returns.","comment":"BC kept: the port is in it"},
        "9303": {"comment":"No interrupts while the ROM is switched"},
        "9304": {"comment":"BC = the paging port"},
        "9307": {"comment":"A = the paging byte"},
        "9310": {"comment":"Bit 4 flipped: the other ROM"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Paged"},
        "9315": {"comment":"The paging byte kept in A' during the copy"},
        "9316": {"comment":"The paging byte back in A"},
        "9317": {"comment":"No interrupts again"},
        "9318": {"comment":"BC = $7FFD again (B kept)"},
        "9320": {"comment":"Bit 4 back: this ROM again"},
        "9325": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "9327": {"synopsis":"Builds the glyph copier at $FF28 (57 bytes): GLYPH_RAM_CODE's first part, the copying loop\nat $242C (32 bytes), then GLYPH_RAM_CODE's last part.","comment":"HL = GLYPH_RAM_CODE's first part"},
        "9330": {"comment":"DE = the copier's place, $FF28"},
        "9333": {"comment":"14 bytes"},
        "9338": {"comment":"The copying loop from $242C"},
        "9342": {"comment":"32 bytes"},
        "9346": {"comment":"The last part from $2464"},
        "9347": {"comment":"11 bytes, to its RET at $246E"},
        "9352": {"synopsis":"The attributes of screen rows 0-21 ($02C0 cells) from the character buffer at ($FF24): $5C01\nbit 0 cleared, ATTR_T = ATTR_P, then BUF_ATTRS from ATTR_P.","comment":"$5C01 bit 0 cleared: no INVERSE yet"},
        "9356": {"comment":"DE = the attribute area"},
        "9359": {"comment":"BC = 704 cells: rows 0-21"},
        "9362": {"comment":"HL = the character buffer"},
        "9365": {"comment":"A = ATTR_P, the colour to start with"},
        "9368": {"comment":"ATTR_T = it"},
        "9371": {"synopsis":"Writes BC attribute bytes to DE from the buffer cells at HL, starting with colour A: each\ncell gets the current colour; an $FF cell gets ATTR_P; a colour control $10-$14 changes the\ncurrent colour by the next cell's value: INK (bits 0-2), PAPER (bits 3-5), FLASH (bit 7),\nBRIGHT (bit 6), INVERSE (when it differs from $5C01 bit 0, that bit is flipped and ink and\npaper swap, SWAP_INK_PAPER).\nExit: ATTR_T = the colour reached.","comment":"The current colour in A'"},
        "9372": {"synopsis":"One cell: $FF?","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9373": {"comment":"A = the cell"},
        "9374": {"comment":"An $FF cell?"},
        "9378": {"comment":"$FF: ATTR_P"},
        "9382": {"comment":"The next cell"},
        "9384": {"comment":"The current colour unchanged"},
        "9386": {"synopsis":"The current colour; then is the character a colour control ($10-$14)?","comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9387": {"comment":"To the cell's attribute"},
        "9389": {"comment":"A = the cell again"},
        "9390": {"comment":"HL past it"},
        "9391": {"comment":"Above $14: not a colour control"},
        "9395": {"comment":"Below $10?"},
        "9399": {"comment":"INK?"},
        "9402": {"comment":"INK: bits 0-2"},
        "9403": {"comment":"A = the INK value"},
        "9404": {"comment":"C = the new bits"},
        "9405": {"comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9406": {"comment":"Its INK bits cleared"},
        "9408": {"comment":"The new ones put in"},
        "9410": {"synopsis":"PAPER: bits 3-5.","comment":"PAPER?"},
        "9414": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "9416": {"comment":"Times 8: to bits 3-5"},
        "9420": {"comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9421": {"comment":"Its PAPER bits cleared"},
        "9425": {"synopsis":"FLASH: bit 7.","comment":"FLASH?"},
        "9429": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "9431": {"comment":"Bit 0 to bit 7"},
        "9433": {"comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9434": {"comment":"FLASH cleared"},
        "9438": {"synopsis":"BRIGHT: bit 6.","comment":"BRIGHT?"},
        "9442": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "9444": {"comment":"Bit 0 to bit 6"},
        "9447": {"comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9448": {"comment":"BRIGHT cleared"},
        "9452": {"synopsis":"INVERSE: when the value differs from $5C01 bit 0, the bit flipped and ink and paper swapped.","comment":"INVERSE?"},
        "9454": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "9455": {"comment":"Never taken: the code is $14 by now"},
        "9457": {"comment":"C = the INVERSE value"},
        "9458": {"comment":"Same as before?"},
        "9462": {"comment":"Bit 0 differs?"},
        "9465": {"comment":"Flipped"},
        "9473": {"comment":"A = the current colour"},
        "9474": {"comment":"Ink and paper swapped"},
        "9477": {"synopsis":"The value's bits into the current colour.","comment":"The new bits in"},
        "9478": {"comment":"Kept in A' as the current colour"},
        "9479": {"synopsis":"The next cell, BC times.","comment":"BC = the count"},
        "9480": {"comment":"One cell fewer"},
        "9481": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "9486": {"comment":"A = the colour reached"},
        "9487": {"comment":"ATTR_T = it"},
        "9491": {"synopsis":"A = A with ink (bits 0-2) and paper (bits 3-5) swapped, bits 6-7 kept.\nExit: C = A without the new ink bits; B = the given A.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"B = the colour"},
        "9492": {"comment":"C = its FLASH and BRIGHT bits"},
        "9495": {"comment":"Ink moved up to bits 3-5"},
        "9501": {"comment":"With FLASH and BRIGHT"},
        "9502": {"comment":"C = them"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Paper moved down to bits 0-2"},
        "9509": {"comment":"A = the swapped colour"},
        "9511": {"synopsis":"BUF_DRAW_CHARS's 8 bytes for control codes $00-$1F: a capital G-like letter (rows $00 $3C\n$62 $60 $6E $62 $3E $00)."},
        "9519": {"synopsis":"BUF_DRAW_CHARS's 8 bytes for code $FE: a small figure with spread legs (rows $00 $6C $10 $54\n$BA $38 $54 $82). Codes $FF and $80-$8F read past it, into KEY_TABLE_A and on."},
        "9527": {"synopsis":"A key table for TABLE_DISPATCH: a count ($15), then for each key its code and the address of\nits routine."},
        "9591": {"synopsis":"A key table for TABLE_DISPATCH: a count (4), then code and routine for each key."},
        "9604": {"synopsis":"Clears the editor's state: $28BE, $FC9A = 0, $EC0D = $82, E_PPC = 0, $35BC, $365E\n(KEY_DEFAULTS).","comment":"UPPER_SETUP: the upper screen's rows and window"},
        "9607": {"comment":"$FC9A, a line number, = 0"},
        "9613": {"comment":"$EC0D = $82: bits 7 and 1 set"},
        "9618": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0: no current line"},
        "9624": {"comment":"ROW_SETUP: the indent of a line's later rows"},
        "9627": {"comment":"KEY_DEFAULTS: MODE, REPPER and the key mode"},
        "9631": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu: $5B81 = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), stream 2; the menu's\nactions MENU_ACTIONS and text (at $2754) into $F6EA and $F6EC; $EC0D bit 1 set, bit 4 clear,\n$EC0C = 0; the menu drawn (DRAW_MENU), then the key loop (MAIN_KEY_LOOP).","comment":"$5B81 = $5BFF, the stack BANK7_STACK swaps in"},
        "9637": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7, the editor's data"},
        "9640": {"comment":"Stream 2: the screen"},
        "9642": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2 current"},
        "9645": {"comment":"The menu's actions","synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions and text set and the menu drawn, with bank 7 and its stack\nalready in place (EDITOR_TO_MENU comes here)."},
        "9651": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "9657": {"comment":"The text's address kept"},
        "9658": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), bit 4 cleared"},
        "9665": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the bar on the first item"},
        "9668": {"comment":"HL = the menu's text"},
        "9669": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "9672": {"comment":"MAIN_KEY_LOOP"},
        "9675": {"synopsis":"The 128 BASIC editor (REPORT_DONE and $233F come here): IX = $FD6C, $5B81 = $5BFF, bank 7\nand its stack, stream 2, the key mode; it waits for a key (FLAGS bit 5), then redraws and\ncontinues.","comment":"IX = the window at $FD6C"},
        "9679": {"comment":"$5B81 = $5BFF, the stack BANK7_STACK swaps in"},
        "9685": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7, the editor's data"},
        "9688": {"comment":"Stream 2: the screen"},
        "9690": {"comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "9693": {"comment":"KEY_MODE: FLAGS and $5B66 set for the editor"},
        "9696": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9699": {"synopsis":"Until a key arrives (FLAGS bit 5).","comment":"A key yet?"},
        "9703": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared; the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6)?"},
        "9712": {"comment":"The mode: Calculator?"},
        "9719": {"comment":"Not 128 BASIC: back to the menu"},
        "9724": {"comment":"The \"128 BASIC\" bar"},
        "9729": {"synopsis":"Calculator: its bar ($384D)."},
        "9732": {"synopsis":"The rows above and below the screen emptied ($30D6, $3222); the Calculator goes straight to\nthe key loop. MENU_SET_GO jumps here.","comment":"BELOW_RESET: no rows kept below the window"},
        "9735": {"comment":"ABOVE_INIT: no rows kept above it"},
        "9738": {"comment":"The Calculator? Straight to the keys"},
        "9745": {"comment":"E_PPC 0?"},
        "9752": {"comment":"No program (PROG = VARS)?"},
        "9764": {"comment":"Then $EC08 = 0"},
        "9770": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC08 in place of E_PPC."},
        "9773": {"synopsis":"E_PPC = the number of the first line at or after HL (bank 0; ROM 1's FIND_LINE and LINE_NO);\nthen, unless $EC0D bit 5 is set, $EC06 = 0, the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), the cursor\nshown (CURSOR_ON) and KEY_ENTER run; on to MAIN_KEY_LOOP.","comment":"Bank 0 for the program"},
        "9776": {"comment":"ROM 1's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line at or after HL"},
        "9779": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "9782": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "9785": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "9789": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 5 set: straight to the keys"},
        "9796": {"comment":"The cursor at the line's start"},
        "9802": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD: the rows from the program"},
        "9805": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "9808": {"comment":"KEY_ENTER"},
        "9811": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key (WAIT_KEY), clicks (CLICK_A with PIP), and handles it (KEY_DISPATCH);\nforever, the stack reset to $5BFF each time.","comment":"The stack reset each time round"},
        "9814": {"comment":"The key mode"},
        "9817": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "9820": {"comment":"The key kept"},
        "9821": {"comment":"The click"},
        "9827": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "9828": {"comment":"Handled"},
        "9831": {"comment":"Forever"},
        "9833": {"synopsis":"Handles key A: looked up in KEY_TABLE_B when $EC0D bit 1 is set (a menu is up), else in\nKEY_TABLE_A (TABLE_DISPATCH); a key found runs its routine (and a click when that returns no\ncarry). A key not found: with $EC0D bit 1 set, MODE = 0; otherwise, with $EC0D bit 0 set, a\nclick; below $A3, on at $28F1.","comment":"HL = the editor's flags"},
        "9836": {"comment":"A menu up?"},
        "9838": {"comment":"The answer kept (Z: no menu)"},
        "9839": {"comment":"A menu up: its keys"},
        "9844": {"comment":"Otherwise the editor's"},
        "9847": {"comment":"Found: run","synopsis":"The key looked up (TABLE_DISPATCH)."},
        "9852": {"comment":"A click when the routine returns no carry"},
        "9857": {"synopsis":"Not in the table.","comment":"Z: no menu up?"},
        "9860": {"comment":"A menu up: MODE = 0"},
        "9865": {"synopsis":"No menu up.","comment":"No menu: $EC0D bit 0 set?"},
        "9872": {"comment":"Set: just a click"},
        "9876": {"synopsis":"Below $A3: on at $28F1; otherwise ignored.","comment":"A character key?"},
        "9880": {"comment":"KEY_INSERT"},
        "9883": {"synopsis":"Key $A9 and the editor's menu item 2 (MENU_SCREEN): moves editing between the upper screen\nand the two-row lower screen. Not in the Calculator ($EC0E = 4: returns with no carry). The\nrows cleared on the screen (ROWS_CLEAR), $EC0D bit 3 cleared and bit 6 flipped; bit 6 now\nset: SCREEN_TO_LOWER, clear: SCREEN_TO_UPPER.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Calculator: nothing"},
        "9889": {"comment":"ROWS_CLEAR: the rows off the screen"},
        "9892": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "9897": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 flipped: the lower screen now?"},
        "9905": {"comment":"SCREEN_TO_LOWER"},
        "9908": {"comment":"Carry and back"},
        "9910": {"synopsis":"Now the upper screen.","comment":"SCREEN_TO_UPPER"},
        "9913": {"synopsis":"Carry."},
        "9915": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: rows 21-23 cleared ($3881), $EC0D bit 6 set, two editing rows\n($2E2D: TV_FLAG bit 0 set, AT 0,0, $EC15 = 1), the window at $FD6C for lines 22-23 ($3A88),\nthe cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_LOWER); then SCREEN_REFILL.","comment":"CLEAR_LOW_3: lines 21-23 cleared"},
        "9918": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set: editing in the lower screen"},
        "9923": {"comment":"EDIT_IN_LOWER: TV_FLAG bit 0, AT 0,0, $EC15 = 1"},
        "9926": {"comment":"WINDOW_LOWER: the window for the lower screen"},
        "9929": {"comment":"CURSOR_SET_LOWER"},
        "9932": {"comment":"SCREEN_REFILL"},
        "9934": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: $EC0D bit 6 cleared, UPPER_SETUP, the \"128 BASIC\" bar ($3848).","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "9939": {"comment":"UPPER_SETUP"},
        "9942": {"comment":"TITLE_128_BASIC: its bar"},
        "9945": {"synopsis":"When $FC9A is not 0, the line before it is looked up ($334A; HL is not kept, so $FC9A\nstays); the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), and the cursor shown (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"$FC9A 0?"},
        "9950": {"comment":"Not: PREV_LINE_NUM (its HL is not kept)"},
        "9953": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD"},
        "9956": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "9959": {"synopsis":"A click of RASP / 2 (CLICK_A).","comment":"A = RASP / 2"},
        "9964": {"synopsis":"A short tone: DE = A, HL = $0C80, through ROM 1's TONE_OUT. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "9966": {"comment":"DE = A"},
        "9969": {"comment":"HL = $0C80: the pitch"},
        "9972": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's TONE_OUT; IX back.","comment":"ROM 1's TONE_OUT"},
        "9975": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9978": {"synopsis":"A tone of 49 cycles with HL = $0300 (a higher pitch than CLICK_A's $0C80), through ROM 1's\nTONE_OUT. Called from $2CE7. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "9980": {"comment":"DE = $0030"},
        "9983": {"comment":"HL = $0300: a higher pitch than CLICK_A's"},
        "9986": {"comment":"On through TONE_OUT"},
        "9988": {"synopsis":"Key $07 (EDIT) in the editor: the cursor off (CURSOR_OFF), $EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), the\nbar on the first item ($EC0C = 0), and the current menu (its text at ($F6EC)) drawn\n(DRAW_MENU).\nExit: carry.\nObserved: EDIT in 128 BASIC opens Options: 128 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print, Exit.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "9991": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set: a menu up"},
        "9996": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the first item"},
        "9999": {"comment":"HL = the current menu's text"},
        "10002": {"comment":"DRAW_MENU"},
        "10005": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10007": {"synopsis":"Keys $0D (ENTER) and $07 (EDIT) with a menu up: $EC0D bit 1 cleared, the screen under the\nmenu put back (MENU_AREA_BACK), the item $EC0C's routine from the actions at ($F6EA) run\n(TABLE_DISPATCH), then the cursor shown (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"$EC0D bit 1 cleared: no menu up"},
        "10012": {"comment":"A = the item"},
        "10014": {"comment":"HL = the menu's actions"},
        "10017": {"comment":"Both kept"},
        "10019": {"comment":"MENU_AREA_BACK: the screen under the menu put back"},
        "10022": {"comment":"A = the item, HL = the actions"},
        "10024": {"comment":"TABLE_DISPATCH: the item's routine run"},
        "10027": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10030": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (up) with a menu up: the bar one item up (MENU_MOVE with carry).","comment":"Carry: up"},
        "10033": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (down) with a menu up: the bar one item down (MENU_MOVE without carry).","comment":"No carry: down"},
        "10034": {"synopsis":"The bar moved from item $EC0C, up ($37A7) with carry, down ($37B6) without, both wrapping\nround, in the menu whose text is at ($F6EC); $EC0C = the new item.\nExit: carry.","comment":"A = the bar's item"},
        "10038": {"comment":"Its address kept"},
        "10039": {"comment":"HL = the menu's text"},
        "10042": {"comment":"Up: MENU_BAR_UP"},
        "10045": {"comment":"Down: MENU_BAR_DOWN"},
        "10049": {"comment":"$EC0C = the new item"},
        "10050": {"synopsis":"Item 0 of the editor's and the Calculator's menus (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, CALC_MENU_ACTS): nothing;\nthe menu is just gone.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10052": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions: a count (5), then for each item its number and routine: 0\n$2831, 1 $286C, 2 $2885, 3 $1B47, 4 $2816. The text follows at $2754: a count (6), the title\n\"128\" padded with spaces and ended by $FF."},
        "10078": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's items, last letter with bit 7 set: Tape Loader, 128 BASIC, Calculator,\n48 BASIC, Tape Tester, and a blank one."},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu: a count (5) and five item numbers and routines, then a count (6) and the\ntitle \"Options \" ended by $FF."},
        "10154": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu items: 128 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print, Exit, and a blank one."},
        "10187": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu (MENU_CALCULATOR): a count (2), item 0 MENU_STAY, item 1 MENU_EXIT;\nthen ($27D2) a count (3) and the title \"Options \" ended by $FF."},
        "10204": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu items, last letter with bit 7 set: Calculator, Exit, and a blank one."},
        "10219": {"synopsis":"MENU_TAPE_LOAD's text for the lower screen (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT): AT 1,0, INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT\n0, then \"To cancel - press BREAK twice\", its last letter with bit 7 set."},
        "10257": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 2: editing moved to the other screen (SCREEN_TOGGLE), then\nEDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"SCREEN_TOGGLE"},
        "10260": {"comment":"EDITOR_MENU_SET"},
        "10262": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 4: the \"Tape Tester\" bar ($3857), the tape test ($3BE9), then\nMENU_EXIT.","comment":"TITLE_TAPE_TEST: its bar"},
        "10265": {"comment":"TAPE_TESTER"},
        "10268": {"synopsis":"Back to the start-up menu (the editor's menu item 4, the Calculator's item 1, and\nMENU_TAPE_TEST): $EC0D bit 6 cleared, UPPER_SETUP, screen lines 0-23 cleared ($3B5E), bank 0\nand the machine stack (BANK0_STACK), then MAIN_MENU.","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "10273": {"comment":"UPPER_SETUP"},
        "10276": {"comment":"Lines 0 to 23 cleared"},
        "10280": {"comment":"CLEAR_LINES"},
        "10283": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "10286": {"comment":"MAIN_MENU"},
        "10289": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 0: the \"Tape Loader\" bar ($3852), LOADER_MSG in the lower screen\n(TV_FLAG bit 0 set meanwhile), TV_FLAG bit 6 set, $EC0E = 7, AT 0,0, then RUN_LOAD_LINE.","comment":"TITLE_TAPE_LOAD: its bar"},
        "10292": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0: the lower screen"},
        "10297": {"comment":"DE = LOADER_MSG"},
        "10300": {"comment":"PRINT_BIT7_TEXT"},
        "10303": {"comment":"Back to the upper screen; TV_FLAG bit 6 set"},
        "10307": {"comment":"$EC0E = 7: the Tape Loader's mode"},
        "10312": {"comment":"AT 0,0 (PRINT_AT_BC)"},
        "10318": {"comment":"RUN_LOAD_LINE"},
        "10321": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 1: the program renumbered ($3888; a click when that returns no\ncarry), E_PPC = 0, $EC08 = 0, then MENU_BAR_BACK.\nObserved: lines 1 and 2 become 10 and 20.","comment":"RENUMBER"},
        "10324": {"comment":"A click when it returns no carry"},
        "10327": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0 and $EC08 = 0"},
        "10336": {"comment":"MENU_BAR_BACK"},
        "10338": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 3: RUN_LLIST_LINE, then MENU_BAR_BACK.","comment":"RUN_LLIST_LINE: the program printed"},
        "10341": {"synopsis":"Unless editing is in the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6), the \"128 BASIC\" bar again (as\nMENU_128_BASIC); then EDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "10348": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 1: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, the \"128 BASIC\" bar ($3848), then\nEDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "10353": {"comment":"TITLE_128_BASIC: its bar"},
        "10356": {"synopsis":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared; mode 0 (128 BASIC), the editor's menu (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, its text\nat $27A0); then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared"},
        "10363": {"comment":"Mode 0: 128 BASIC"},
        "10365": {"comment":"HL = EDIT_MENU_ACTS"},
        "10368": {"comment":"DE = its text"},
        "10371": {"comment":"MENU_SET_GO"},
        "10373": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 2: $EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared; UPPER_SETUP; the\n\"Calculator\" bar ($384D); $EC0E = 4; E_PPC = 0; the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD); the cursor\nat row 0, column 0 (CURSOR_PUT); mode 4 and the Calculator's menu (CALC_MENU_ACTS, its text\nat $27D2), then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared"},
        "10382": {"comment":"UPPER_SETUP"},
        "10385": {"comment":"TITLE_CALC: its bar"},
        "10388": {"comment":"$EC0E = 4: the Calculator"},
        "10393": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "10399": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD"},
        "10402": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0, remembered column 0"},
        "10406": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10409": {"comment":"Mode 4"},
        "10411": {"comment":"HL = CALC_MENU_ACTS"},
        "10414": {"comment":"DE = its text, at $27D2"},
        "10417": {"synopsis":"$EC0E = A (the mode), $F6EA = HL (the menu's actions), $F6EC = DE (its text), then on in\nEDITOR_MAIN at EDITOR_ROWS.","comment":"$EC0E = the mode"},
        "10420": {"comment":"$F6EA = the menu's actions"},
        "10423": {"comment":"$F6EC = its text"},
        "10427": {"comment":"On at EDITOR_ROWS"},
        "10430": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: 21 editing rows ($2E1F: $EC15 = 20, TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared), IX\nand the window at $FD6C for lines 0-20 ($3A7F), and the cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_UPPER).","comment":"EDIT_IN_MAIN: $EC15 = 20, TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "10433": {"comment":"WINDOW_MAIN: IX and the window at $FD6C"},
        "10436": {"comment":"CURSOR_SET_UPPER"},
        "10439": {"synopsis":"EDITOR_MAIN with a mode other than 0 or 4: screen lines 0-23 cleared ($3B5E), then\nMAIN_MENU_SET (the start-up menu set up and drawn).","comment":"Lines 0 to 23 cleared"},
        "10443": {"comment":"CLEAR_LINES"},
        "10446": {"comment":"MAIN_MENU_SET"},
        "10449": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_UPPER's block for $3FBA: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 4, $10, $14\n(row, column and remembered column 0, then three bytes for the upper screen)."},
        "10456": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_LOWER's block: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1."},
        "10463": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_LOWER_INIT ($3FBA copies a counted block).","comment":"HL = CURS_LOWER_INIT"},
        "10466": {"comment":"DE = the cursor's row, $F6EE, on"},
        "10469": {"comment":"COPY_COUNTED"},
        "10472": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_UPPER_INIT.","comment":"HL = CURS_UPPER_INIT"},
        "10475": {"comment":"DE = the cursor's row, $F6EE, on"},
        "10478": {"comment":"COPY_COUNTED"},
        "10481": {"synopsis":"A character key (KEY_CHAR, codes below $A3): with $EC0D bit 0 set it is ignored (the cursor\nshown again). Otherwise $EC0D bit 7 cleared and bit 3 set (the line changed), the cursor\noff, the character put in at the cursor ($2E81), the cursor one place on ($2B78), $EC0D bit\n7 set again; the cursor stored with its column as the remembered one and shown (CURSOR_PUT),\nor, when it could not move, shown where it was (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"HL = the editor's flags"},
        "10484": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "10486": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set: only the cursor shown again"},
        "10491": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 cleared, bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "10495": {"comment":"The flags' address kept"},
        "10496": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "10497": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10500": {"comment":"A = the character, kept again"},
        "10502": {"comment":"The character in"},
        "10505": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10506": {"comment":"One place on"},
        "10510": {"comment":"HL = $EC0D"},
        "10511": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set again"},
        "10513": {"comment":"Not moved?"},
        "10516": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "10517": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT, the column remembered"},
        "10520": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "10523": {"synopsis":"Key $AA: $EC0D bit 3 set, the cursor off, the character under it taken out ($2F12), then the\ncursor shown (CURSOR_PUT, the column remembered).","comment":"$EC0D bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "10528": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10531": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR: the character under it out"},
        "10534": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10535": {"comment":"The column remembered"},
        "10536": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10539": {"synopsis":"Key $0C (DELETE): $EC0D bit 0 cleared and bit 3 set, the cursor off, one place back ($2B5B;\nat the start nothing more, CURSOR_ON); the character there taken out ($2F12), then the\ncursor shown (CURSOR_PUT, the column remembered).","comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared, bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "10546": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10549": {"comment":"One place back: not possible?"},
        "10553": {"comment":"Then only CURSOR_ON"},
        "10556": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR: the character there out"},
        "10559": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10560": {"comment":"The column remembered"},
        "10561": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10564": {"synopsis":"Key $0D (ENTER), and EDITOR_MAIN's last step: the cursor off. A row that is empty and is a\nwhole line by itself (flags bits 0 and 3) does nothing. Otherwise, when the line was changed\n($EC0D bit 3), it is entered ($2C8E; nothing more when that returns no carry); then the\ncursor goes to the line's end ($2C4C), one place on ($2B78), a blank row is made there\n($2ECE), and the cursor is stored at its column 0 (CURSOR_PUT).\nExit: carry.\nObserved: after `1 PRINT 1` and ENTER the line's row has flags $19 and the rows below stay\nempty ($09).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10567": {"comment":"The remembered column kept"},
        "10568": {"comment":"DE = the cursor row's place"},
        "10572": {"comment":"Anything on the row?"},
        "10578": {"comment":"Text: the line entered if changed"},
        "10580": {"comment":"Empty: a line of one row (flags bits 0 and 3)?"},
        "10590": {"synopsis":"Changed ($EC0D bit 3)? Then the line entered ($2C8E)."},
        "10595": {"comment":"Unchanged: on to the next line"},
        "10597": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "10600": {"comment":"A report: the cursor shown only"},
        "10602": {"synopsis":"The cursor to the line's end ($2C4C), one place on, a blank row there ($2ECE), column 0.","comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "10605": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: one place on"},
        "10608": {"comment":"NEW_BLANK_ROW: a blank row there"},
        "10611": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "10613": {"comment":"A = the remembered column back"},
        "10615": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10618": {"synopsis":"An empty one-row line: only the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "10620": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10623": {"synopsis":"Not entered: the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "10624": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10627": {"synopsis":"Key $A6: E_PPC = the program's first line (bank 0; ROM 1's FIND_LINE from 0 and LINE_NO);\nthe cursor's colour $0F ($3A96), the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), the cursor shown\n(CURSOR_ON). Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "10633": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10636": {"comment":"From line 0"},
        "10639": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: the program in bank 0"},
        "10642": {"comment":"ROM 1's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line"},
        "10645": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "10648": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK"},
        "10651": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "10655": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "10657": {"comment":"CURSOR_COLOUR"},
        "10660": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD"},
        "10663": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10664": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10667": {"synopsis":"Key $A5: E_PPC = the line before the first one numbered 9999 or more (FIND_LINE's DE, then\nLINE_NO), normally the program's last; the cursor's colour $0F, the rows rebuilt, the cursor\nshown. Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "10673": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10676": {"comment":"Line 9999"},
        "10679": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: the program in bank 0"},
        "10682": {"comment":"ROM 1's FIND_LINE: DE = the line before"},
        "10685": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "10686": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "10689": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK"},
        "10692": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "10696": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "10698": {"comment":"CURSOR_COLOUR"},
        "10701": {"comment":"ROWS_REBUILD"},
        "10704": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "10705": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10708": {"synopsis":"Key $AF: the cursor off, back to the start of the previous word ($2BEA); stored with the\ncolumn remembered (CURSOR_PUT), or, when it did not move, shown again (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10711": {"comment":"WORD_LEFT"},
        "10714": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10717": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10721": {"synopsis":"Key $AE: the cursor off, on to the start of the next word ($2C09); stored (CURSOR_PUT), or,\nwhen it did not move, shown again.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10724": {"comment":"WORD_RIGHT"},
        "10727": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10729": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10732": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off the screen: its place (CURSOR_GET), the cell's attribute put back\n($364F).\nExit: C = the row, B = the column, A = the remembered column, HL = $F6F1.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "10735": {"comment":"CELL_CURSOR_OFF: the cell's attribute back"},
        "10738": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at its place (CURSOR_GET, then $3640: the cell's attribute kept, the\ncursor's colour put in).\nExit: as CURSOR_GET.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "10741": {"comment":"CELL_CURSOR_ON"},
        "10744": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to row C, column B, remembered column A (CURSOR_STORE), sets its colour to\n$0F ($3A96: ink 7 on paper 1), and shows it ($3640). Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "10747": {"comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "10749": {"comment":"Ink 7 on paper 1"},
        "10751": {"comment":"CURSOR_COLOUR"},
        "10754": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "10756": {"comment":"CELL_CURSOR_ON"},
        "10759": {"synopsis":"C = the cursor's row ($F6EE), B = its column ($F6EF), A = the remembered column ($F6F0), the\none up and down movement aim for.\nExit: HL = $F6F1.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "10762": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "10764": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "10766": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10767": {"comment":"HL = $F6F1"},
        "10769": {"synopsis":"The other way: $F6EE = C, $F6EF = B, $F6F0 = A.\nExit: HL = $F6F0.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "10772": {"comment":"The row"},
        "10774": {"comment":"The column"},
        "10776": {"comment":"The remembered column"},
        "10778": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS); 0 is no character.\nExit: DE = the row. Keeps BC, HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "10779": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "10782": {"comment":"HL = B"},
        "10785": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "10786": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "10789": {"synopsis":"Key $AC (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor down ten rows. Each step is ROW_DOWN, the cursor kept as\nnear the remembered column ($F6F0) as the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_R) and stored at once\n(the cursor at $F6EE, $2A11). A row with no text sends it back up one row (ROW_UP); the last\nrow stops it.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($29F8); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway, or did not move at all ($29F2).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10792": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "10795": {"synopsis":"One row down."},
        "10796": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "10800": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10802": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10803": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "10806": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "10810": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "10812": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "10815": {"comment":"Ten rows: done"},
        "10816": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10818": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back up one row, the column placed (COL_PLACE_R); no carry."},
        "10819": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up one"},
        "10823": {"comment":"Column E"},
        "10824": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "10827": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10828": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "10829": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10831": {"synopsis":"Key $AD (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor up ten rows, as ED_KEY_TEN_DOWN in the other direction\n(ROW_UP, COL_PLACE_L). A row with no text sends it back down one row, to the start of that\nrow's text.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($29F8); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10834": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "10837": {"synopsis":"One row up."},
        "10838": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "10842": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10844": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10845": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "10848": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "10849": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_L"},
        "10852": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "10854": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "10857": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10858": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10861": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back down one row, to the start of its text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from\ncolumn 0).","comment":"The flags (no carry) kept"},
        "10862": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down one"},
        "10865": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "10867": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "10871": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10874": {"synopsis":"Key $A7 (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor to the end of its line's text (TO_LINE_END); that column\nbecomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10877": {"comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "10880": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10883": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "10884": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10887": {"synopsis":"Key $A8 (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor to the start of its line's text (TO_LINE_START); that\ncolumn becomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10890": {"comment":"TO_LINE_START"},
        "10893": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10896": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "10897": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10900": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor up one row (ROW_UP), as near the remembered column ($F6F0)\nas the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); the remembered column is kept. A row with no text\nsends the cursor back down, to the column placed there (COL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($29F8); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10903": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "10905": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "10909": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10912": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "10916": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "10917": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10920": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "10921": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down"},
        "10924": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "10926": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "10930": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10933": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor down one row (ROW_DOWN), as near the remembered column as\nthe row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); a row with no text sends it back up (ROW_UP,\nCOL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($29F8); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10936": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "10938": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "10942": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "10945": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "10949": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "10950": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10954": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "10958": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_R)"},
        "10962": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "10963": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "10964": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10967": {"synopsis":"Key $08 (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor one place left (CURSOR_LEFT); the new column becomes the\nremembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10970": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "10973": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10976": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "10979": {"synopsis":"Key $09 (KEY_TABLE_A): the cursor one place right (CURSOR_RIGHT); the new column becomes the\nremembered one. When that fails after going down a row, the cursor goes back up to the end\nof that row's text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "10982": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "10985": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "10988": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "10989": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "10992": {"comment":"From column 31: the end of the row's text"},
        "10994": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "10997": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "10998": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "11001": {"synopsis":"Places column B of row C in the row's text: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT, and TEXT_END_LEFT when that\nfails.\nExit: carry when the row has text (B moved onto or next to it); no carry for a row with\nnone. Keeps DE."},
        "11002": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "11005": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "11010": {"synopsis":"As COL_PLACE_R, the other way round: TEXT_END_LEFT first, then TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT.\nExit: carry when the row has text. Keeps DE."},
        "11011": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "11014": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "11019": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C up one:\n1. Leaving the first row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_FIRST_ROW); a report there\n   stops the move.\n2. Row C, when it holds no text, is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW).\n3. With C greater than ($F6F1), C goes up one; otherwise the window scrolls down a row\n   (L166F) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes up unless it is row 0.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled); no carry otherwise. Keeps B.","comment":"LEAVE_FIRST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "11022": {"comment":"A report while entering the line: no move"},
        "11025": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11028": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed"},
        "11037": {"comment":"Above row ($F6F1)?"},
        "11044": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "11045": {"comment":"The window scrolled down a row"},
        "11049": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "11050": {"comment":"Row 0: no move"},
        "11053": {"synopsis":"C one row up; carry."},
        "11055": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "11056": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C down one: a row C with no text is removed instead\n(REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW), the rows below moving up into it. Otherwise ROW_DOWN_TEXT.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled). Keeps B."},
        "11057": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11060": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed instead"},
        "11066": {"comment":"Text: on down"},
        "11068": {"comment":"REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW"},
        "11071": {"synopsis":"Leaving the last row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_LAST_ROW; a report stops the\nmove). With C less than ($F6F2), C goes down one; otherwise the window scrolls up a row\n($1639) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes down unless it is already row ($F6F3).","comment":"LEAVE_LAST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "11074": {"comment":"A report: no move"},
        "11076": {"comment":"Below row ($F6F2)?"},
        "11084": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "11086": {"comment":"The window scrolled up a row"},
        "11091": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "11092": {"comment":"Row ($F6F3): no move"},
        "11096": {"synopsis":"C one row down; carry."},
        "11098": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "11099": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place left within the text: to the column before, or\npast the gaps before it (TEXT_END_LEFT); from column 0 (or with nothing to the left) up a\nrow (ROW_UP), to the end of that row's text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved; no carry, B = 0 and A as on entry\notherwise.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "11100": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "11104": {"comment":"E = the column"},
        "11105": {"comment":"Back to the text"},
        "11108": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "11110": {"synopsis":"Nothing to the left on this row: up a row, to the end of its text."},
        "11111": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "11115": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "11116": {"comment":"No row above: no carry"},
        "11117": {"comment":"The end of the row above's text"},
        "11122": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "11123": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "11124": {"comment":"Not moved: A back, B = 0"},
        "11128": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place right within the text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT). Past\nthe row's end:\n1. With $EC0D bit 7 clear and row C not continued (flags bit 1), the row is marked as\n   continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared), the cursor goes down a row (ROW_DOWN) and a blank\n   row flagged as the line's last row is inserted there (INSERT_ROW), the first ($FD6B)\n   columns of a row then cleared ($35F4); carry and A = column.\n2. Otherwise down a row (ROW_DOWN) to the start of its text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "11129": {"comment":"One column right"},
        "11130": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "11135": {"comment":"E = the new column"},
        "11136": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT: text there?"},
        "11139": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "11141": {"synopsis":"Past the row's end.","comment":"B back to column 31"},
        "11142": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "11144": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set?"},
        "11151": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11154": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11159": {"comment":"Row C continued already?"},
        "11163": {"comment":"Now continued, no longer the line's last row"},
        "11167": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "11172": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "11174": {"comment":"Row C's old flags kept"},
        "11175": {"comment":"Down a row"},
        "11178": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "11179": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11182": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "11187": {"comment":"Flags: not the first row, the last"},
        "11191": {"comment":"A blank row inserted at row C"},
        "11194": {"comment":"The first ($FD6B) columns of the row at DE cleared"},
        "11197": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "11198": {"comment":"Carry: moved"},
        "11200": {"synopsis":"Down a row, to the start of its text; no carry (A = E, B = 0) when it has none.","comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "11203": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "11207": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "11208": {"comment":"No row below: no carry"},
        "11209": {"comment":"The start of the new row's text"},
        "11211": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "11214": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "11215": {"comment":"Text: carry"},
        "11216": {"comment":"None: A = E, B = 0, no carry"},
        "11220": {"synopsis":"TEXT_FROM_COL on window row C: carry when column B is in or just after the row's text, or\ntext follows it (B moved to it). Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11222": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11225": {"comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL"},
        "11228": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "11231": {"synopsis":"TEXT_BACK_FROM on window row C: carry when column B holds a character, or B moved back to\njust after the last character before it. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11233": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11236": {"comment":"TEXT_BACK_FROM"},
        "11239": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "11242": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the word before it: left (CURSOR_LEFT) past any spaces,\nthen on left to the space before the word, then right one place (CURSOR_RIGHT).\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry when it ran out of text. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11244": {"synopsis":"Left past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "11249": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "11252": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "11256": {"synopsis":"Left to the space before the word.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "11259": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "11261": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "11264": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "11268": {"comment":"Right onto the word's first character"},
        "11271": {"synopsis":"No more text: no carry.","comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "11273": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the next word: right (CURSOR_RIGHT) to the next space, then\npast the spaces to a character.\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry (one place back left) when no word follows on the\nrow. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11275": {"synopsis":"Right to a space.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "11278": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "11280": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "11283": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "11287": {"synopsis":"Right past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "11290": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "11292": {"comment":"More text on the row?"},
        "11297": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "11300": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "11304": {"comment":"Carry: at the word"},
        "11305": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "11307": {"synopsis":"No word follows: back one place, no carry.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT: back one place"},
        "11310": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "11311": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "11313": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor up (ROW_UP) to its line's first row (flags bit 0) and there to the start of\nthe text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from column 0).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11315": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11318": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11322": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "11326": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "11329": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "11331": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "11333": {"synopsis":"First row: the start of its text.","comment":"From column 0"},
        "11335": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "11338": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "11340": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor down (ROW_DOWN) to its line's last row (flags bit 3) and there to just\nafter the text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "11342": {"synopsis":"The line's last row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11345": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11349": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "11353": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "11356": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "11358": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "11360": {"synopsis":"Last row: the end of its text.","comment":"From column 31"},
        "11362": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "11365": {"synopsis":"HL and DE restored.","comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "11368": {"synopsis":"Before the cursor leaves row C downwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C\nis its last row (flags bit 3), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "11371": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "11375": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11378": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11382": {"comment":"Row C its line's last?"},
        "11386": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "11388": {"synopsis":"As LEAVE_LAST_ROW, upwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C is its first\nrow (flags bit 0), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "11391": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "11395": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11398": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11402": {"comment":"Row C its line's first?"},
        "11406": {"synopsis":"Enters the edited line the cursor is on:\n1. Up from row C to the line's first row (flags bit 0): the reader LINE_ROWS_CHAR is set to\n   start there in state 2 (the window's rows); when the line starts above the window, in\n   state 1 at row 0 (the rows kept above). $EC00-$EC02 (state with bit 7 set, column 0, row)\n   and a copy in $EC03-$EC05; $EC06 = 0.\n2. L335F and $3C67, then LINE_ENTER in bank 0 (on its stack) reads, checks and stores or\n   runs the line.\n3. No report (ERR_NR = $FF): $EC0D bit 3 cleared, KEY_DEFAULTS, $152F unless in Calculator\n   mode ($EC0E = 4), a tone ($26FA), the cursor reloaded; carry.\n4. A report: ENTER_FAILED.\nExit: carry when the cursor may move on.","comment":"State 2: the window's rows"},
        "11408": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11411": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11415": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "11419": {"comment":"Up a row"},
        "11420": {"comment":"Still in the window?"},
        "11423": {"comment":"Above the window: state 1, row 0"},
        "11427": {"synopsis":"The reader's state, column 0 and row, twice.","comment":"HL = the reader, $EC00"},
        "11430": {"comment":"DE = its copy, $EC03"},
        "11433": {"comment":"Bit 7: counting to the cursor"},
        "11435": {"comment":"The state"},
        "11439": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "11445": {"comment":"Row C"},
        "11448": {"comment":"No characters counted yet"},
        "11454": {"comment":"EXPAND_INIT"},
        "11457": {"comment":"TOKENIZE_LINE: the rows into the edit line"},
        "11460": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "11462": {"comment":"LINE_ENTER in bank 0"},
        "11468": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK"},
        "11471": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "11473": {"comment":"A report (ERR_NR not $FF)?"},
        "11479": {"comment":"No report: the line no longer edited"},
        "11484": {"comment":"KEY_DEFAULTS"},
        "11487": {"comment":"Calculator mode?"},
        "11492": {"comment":"Not the Calculator: ROWS_REBUILD"},
        "11495": {"comment":"A tone"},
        "11498": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET: the cursor reloaded"},
        "11501": {"comment":"Carry: entered"},
        "11503": {"synopsis":"A report while the line was entered: the reader set back to the line's start ($EC03-$EC05\ncopied to $EC00-$EC02, bit 7 cleared), BC from $3C63 (or $EC06 when it gives no carry), and\nthe cursor moved by the difference: left (CURSOR_LEFT) $EC06 - BC places, or right\n(CURSOR_RIGHT, $EC0D bit 7 cleared) BC - $EC06 places, each stopping when the cursor cannot\nmove. Then $EC0D bit 7 set, the cursor stored, the cursor's colour $17 (instead of $0F)\ngiven to $3A96; no carry, so the move does not happen.","comment":"The reader back at the line's start, not counting"},
        "11509": {"comment":"The state, bit 7 cleared"},
        "11515": {"comment":"The column"},
        "11519": {"comment":"The row"},
        "11521": {"comment":"BC = the count from $3C63"},
        "11524": {"comment":"No carry: BC = $EC06, no move"},
        "11530": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC06 - BC; the cursor reloaded.","comment":"HL = $EC06 - BC"},
        "11536": {"comment":"The subtraction's flags kept"},
        "11538": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "11543": {"comment":"BC the larger: right"},
        "11545": {"comment":"Equal: no move"},
        "11547": {"synopsis":"One place left."},
        "11548": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "11549": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "11553": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "11555": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "11556": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "11560": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11562": {"synopsis":"BC above $EC06: HL = BC - $EC06 places right."},
        "11563": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 cleared while moving right"},
        "11569": {"comment":"DE = $EC06 - BC"},
        "11570": {"comment":"HL = BC - $EC06"},
        "11576": {"synopsis":"One place right."},
        "11577": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "11578": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "11582": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "11584": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "11585": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "11589": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored, its colour $17; no carry.","comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set"},
        "11594": {"comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "11597": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $17"},
        "11599": {"comment":"CURSOR_COLOUR"},
        "11602": {"comment":"No carry: the move not made"},
        "11604": {"synopsis":"Gives the next character of the line being entered, read from the editor's rows (from\n$3D9D). The reader's state is $EC00 (low four bits; bit 7 set while characters before the\ncursor are counted), column $EC01 and row $EC02. While bit 7 is set, $EC06 counts each call.\nThe state picks the routine through ROWS_CHAR_TABLE (TABLE_DISPATCH): 1 the rows kept above\nthe window (ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR), 2 the window's rows (ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR), 4 the rows kept below\nit (ROWS_BELOW_CHAR); each passes over 0s (no character) and returns the next character with\nL = the new state; 8, the line's end, is not in the table and gives $0D.\nExit: A = the character; the column, row and state stored back.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "11607": {"comment":"Counting to the cursor?"},
        "11611": {"comment":"One more character before the cursor"},
        "11618": {"synopsis":"State, column and row; the state's routine.","comment":"HL = the reader"},
        "11621": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "11623": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "11625": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "11626": {"comment":"The row's address kept"},
        "11627": {"comment":"The state's routine"},
        "11629": {"comment":"HL = ROWS_CHAR_TABLE"},
        "11632": {"comment":"TABLE_DISPATCH: the state's routine"},
        "11635": {"comment":"E = the new state"},
        "11637": {"comment":"No routine (state 8): $0D"},
        "11641": {"synopsis":"Row, column and the new state stored.","comment":"The row"},
        "11643": {"comment":"The column"},
        "11645": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "11646": {"comment":"The state's low four bits replaced"},
        "11651": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "11653": {"synopsis":"LINE_ROWS_CHAR's table for TABLE_DISPATCH: a count (3), then for each state its number and\nroutine: 2 ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR, 4 ROWS_BELOW_CHAR, 1 ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR."},
        "11663": {"synopsis":"State 1: the next character from row C of the rows kept above the window ($F9DE,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $32B7); after their last row on to state 2 at row 0, column 0.\nExit: A = the character, L = 1.","comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C above the window"},
        "11666": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "11669": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "11671": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "11675": {"comment":"State 1"},
        "11678": {"synopsis":"The next row; past the last, state 2.","comment":"The next row"},
        "11679": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "11681": {"comment":"Past the rows above? (HL = the word at $F9DB)"},
        "11685": {"comment":"C against the byte HL points at, not the count: a slip?"},
        "11688": {"comment":"State 2 at row 0, column 0"},
        "11692": {"synopsis":"State 2: the next character from window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Reaching the cursor's place\n($F6EE row, $F6EF column) clears $EC00 bit 7, which stops the count in $EC06. A row that is\nits line's last (flags bit 3) ends the line ($0D, state 8); past row ($F6F3) on to state 4\nat row 1.\nExit: A = the character, L = 2.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "11693": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "11700": {"comment":"The cursor's column?"},
        "11705": {"comment":"Reached: stop counting"},
        "11710": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "11711": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11714": {"comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "11717": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "11719": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "11723": {"comment":"State 2"},
        "11726": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11730": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "11734": {"comment":"State 8: the line's end"},
        "11739": {"synopsis":"The next row; past row ($F6F3), state 4.","comment":"HL = the window's last row, $F6F3"},
        "11742": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "11743": {"comment":"Past row ($F6F3)?"},
        "11745": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "11749": {"comment":"State 4 at row 1, column 0"},
        "11753": {"synopsis":"State 4: the next character from row C of the rows kept below the window ($F6F8,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $31C3, rows 1 up to the count in $F6F5). The line's last row (flags\nbit 3), or the last row kept, ends the line ($0D, state 8).\nExit: A = the character, L = 4.","comment":"BELOW_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C below the window"},
        "11756": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "11759": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "11761": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "11765": {"comment":"State 4"},
        "11768": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "11772": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
