        "11779": {"comment":"Past the last row kept?"},
        "11785": {"synopsis":"The line's end: A = $0D, L = 8."},
        "11790": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of the row at DE, B moved on; carry. No carry when B is past\ncolumn 31.","comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "11793": {"comment":"No carry when past"},
        "11795": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "11799": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "11800": {"comment":"B moved on"},
        "11801": {"comment":"Carry: one read"},
        "11803": {"synopsis":"Copy lists for $3FBA (a count, then the bytes): 1, $14 (EDIT_IN_MAIN), and at $2E1D 1, $01\n(EDIT_IN_LOWER), each put in $EC15."},
        "11805": {"synopsis":"1, $01: EDIT_IN_LOWER's $EC15."},
        "11807": {"synopsis":"Editing in the main screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared and $EC15, the window's last row, = 20\n(ROW_COUNT_MAIN through $3FBA).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "11812": {"comment":"$EC15 = 20"},
        "11821": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 set, the print position at row 0, column 0\n(PRINT_AT_BC), and $EC15, the window's last row, = 1 (ROW_COUNT_LOWER through $3FBA).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 set"},
        "11829": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0"},
        "11832": {"comment":"$EC15 = 1"},
        "11841": {"synopsis":"Is column B of the row at DE in or next to text? Carry when the character at B is not 0, or\n(B not 0) the one before it is not 0, or one further right up to column 30 is not 0 (B moved\nto it; A = it).\nExit: no carry, B = 31, when the row is empty from there on.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "11846": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "11850": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "11854": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "11855": {"comment":"The column before"},
        "11857": {"comment":"A character before B?"},
        "11862": {"synopsis":"A character here?"},
        "11867": {"synopsis":"The next column, up to 30.","comment":"The next column"},
        "11870": {"comment":"Up to column 30"},
        "11875": {"synopsis":"Carry when column B of the row at DE holds a character; otherwise B moves left over 0s to\njust after the last character before it (carry), or to 0 when there is none (no carry).\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "11880": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "11884": {"synopsis":"A 0 here: one column left."},
        "11889": {"comment":"Column 0: none, no carry"},
        "11892": {"comment":"One column left"},
        "11896": {"synopsis":"Just after the character; carry."},
        "11899": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B in the row at DE, A = the character there.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "11903": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "11905": {"synopsis":"Inserts character A at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving right\nacross its rows; nothing when $EC0D bit 0 is set (no carry).\n1. The character goes in at column B ($16AC) and the row is redrawn ($3604).\n2. The character pushed out of column 31, when not 0, goes on to the next row: when row C\n   was its line's last (flags bit 3 or 5 set) a blank row is inserted after it (INSERT_ROW,\n   flags as row C's without bit 0, the first ($FD6B) columns cleared by $35F4) and taken at\n   column 0; otherwise at the start of the next row's text (TEXT_FROM_COL). Row C's flags\n   lose bits 3 and 5 and get bit 1 (continued).\n3. Past the window's last row ($EC15) the character goes to $316E. Keeps BC.","comment":"HL = the editor's flags"},
        "11908": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "11909": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set: nothing"},
        "11912": {"comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "11913": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "11914": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11918": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B; the row redrawn.","comment":"In at column B; A = the character pushed out of column 31"},
        "11921": {"comment":"The character pushed out kept"},
        "11922": {"comment":"HL = the row, for SHOW_ROW"},
        "11923": {"comment":"The row redrawn"},
        "11927": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "11929": {"comment":"Nothing pushed out: done"},
        "11931": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11932": {"comment":"The next row, from column 0"},
        "11935": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "11941": {"comment":"Row C's flags: bits 3 and 5 cleared; Z when they were clear"},
        "11947": {"comment":"A = the flags as they were"},
        "11948": {"comment":"Row C continued"},
        "11950": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "11951": {"comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "11955": {"comment":"Not the line's last row before: already continued"},
        "11957": {"comment":"New row's flags: not the first"},
        "11959": {"comment":"INSERT_ROW: a new row there"},
        "11962": {"comment":"Not inserted: done"},
        "11964": {"comment":"Its first columns cleared"},
        "11967": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "11968": {"comment":"Into the new row"},
        "11970": {"synopsis":"The row already continued: into the next row at its text's start.","comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL: B = where its text starts"},
        "11973": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "11974": {"comment":"Into that row"},
        "11976": {"synopsis":"Past the window's last row: $316E.","comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "11977": {"comment":"Into the rows below"},
        "11980": {"synopsis":"BC back."},
        "11982": {"synopsis":"Inserts a blank row at row C flagged as both the first and the last row of a line ($09,\nINSERT_ROW); DE = row C's address first.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "11985": {"comment":"Flags: first and last row"},
        "11987": {"synopsis":"Inserts BLANK_ROW at window row C ($1675, the rows from C down moving down) and gives it\nflags A.\nExit: carry when inserted. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "11989": {"comment":"B = the row"},
        "11990": {"comment":"HL = BLANK_ROW"},
        "11993": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "11995": {"comment":"The template inserted at row B"},
        "11999": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "12000": {"comment":"Not inserted?"},
        "12002": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "12003": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "12006": {"comment":"The new row's flags"},
        "12011": {"comment":"Carry: inserted"},
        "12012": {"synopsis":"DE and BC back."},
        "12015": {"synopsis":"A blank editor row for INSERT_ROW: 32 columns of 0 (no character), flags $09 (the line's\nfirst and last row) and two 0 bytes."},
        "12050": {"synopsis":"Deletes the character at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving left\nacross its rows:\n1. Down the continued rows (flags bit 1) to the line's last row; when the line runs on past\n   the window's last row ($EC15), $31C9 gives the character to bring in from below,\n   otherwise 0 is brought in.\n2. From that row back up to row C each row moves one column left ($16C1) from the start of\n   its text (from column B on row C), taking the character in at column 31; the character\n   moved out at the left is carried to the row above.\n3. A row other than row C left without text is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW); the others are\n   redrawn ($3604).\nExit: carry. Keeps BC.","comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "12051": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "12054": {"comment":"Its row and column kept"},
        "12055": {"synopsis":"Row C continued (flags bit 1)?"},
        "12059": {"comment":"Row C continued?"},
        "12061": {"comment":"A = 0: nothing to bring in"},
        "12065": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "12066": {"comment":"DE = it, 35 bytes on"},
        "12071": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "12077": {"comment":"C = the window's last row"},
        "12078": {"comment":"A = the character from below"},
        "12081": {"synopsis":"H = column B, L = row C of the cursor."},
        "12082": {"synopsis":"One row: its start column (B on the cursor's row, the text's start on the others)."},
        "12083": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
