        "12154": {"comment":"Until the cursor's row is done"},
        "12157": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12158": {"comment":"The cursor back"},
        "12160": {"synopsis":"Removes window row C (at DE), which holds no text:\n1. When it is not its line's first row (flags bit 0), the row above (for row 0 the last of\n   the rows kept above the window: $FC9A moved by $334A, row ($F9DB) - 1 through $32B7)\n   loses flags bit 1 and takes row C's flags.\n2. A row taken from below the window (ROW_FROM_BELOW) and row C removed ($1648: the rows\n   below it move up, the taken row at the bottom).\nExit: carry.","comment":"HL = row C's flags"},
        "12164": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "12165": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "12169": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "12170": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "12171": {"comment":"Row 0?"},
        "12175": {"comment":"The row kept again"},
        "12176": {"comment":"The rows kept above: their last row"},
        "12179": {"comment":"PREV_LINE_NUM"},
        "12182": {"comment":"$FC9A = it"},
        "12185": {"comment":"C = the rows kept above, less 1: their last"},
        "12190": {"comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = that row"},
        "12193": {"comment":"The row back"},
        "12196": {"synopsis":"Row C - 1.","comment":"Row C - 1"},
        "12197": {"comment":"DE = row C - 1"},
        "12200": {"synopsis":"The row above: bit 1 cleared, row C's flags added.","comment":"The row back"},
        "12201": {"comment":"A = row C's flags"},
        "12202": {"comment":"HL = the row above's flags"},
        "12206": {"comment":"Not continued; row C's flags taken"},
        "12210": {"synopsis":"Row C removed, a row from below at the bottom.","comment":"B = the row"},
        "12211": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "12214": {"comment":"A row from below at HL"},
        "12217": {"comment":"Row C removed, the rows below up"},
        "12220": {"synopsis":"Key $B4 (KEY_TABLE_A): deletes left of the cursor: the spaces before it, then the word\nbefore them, stopping at the space before the word or at the line's start (AT_LINE_START).\nEach step is CURSOR_LEFT and LINE_DELETE_CHAR; the cursor then goes right past that space.\nThen DEL_KEY_END.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off"},
        "12223": {"synopsis":"At the line's start? Otherwise left one, deleted; a space: again.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "12224": {"comment":"At the line's start?"},
